  '<p class="gd-p">Every booking starts as a request. A person checks the car and the price, then sends you an offer. Nothing is charged until you approve, sign and pay.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Request</span><em>You pick a car and dates</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Offer</span><em>We confirm the price</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Sign</span><em>The rental agreement</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Pay</span><em>Your card is authorized</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Verify</span><em>Licence, selfie, coverage</em></li><li><b>6</b><span>Pick up</span><em>We hand over the keys</em></li></ol><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-find-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Find a car</h2><p class="gd-p">Start on carmacars.ca. You do not need to sign in to look around.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Go to <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca</span> and press <b class="gd-ui">Find a car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your pickup and return dates. The list then shows the cars that are free and what the whole trip costs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Narrow the list with Filters: type, seats, transmission and daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to see its photos, rates, what is included and its own calendar. Its car code (like CC-7F3A) is under the price: quote it when you call or chat with us, and we know the car at once.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/cars</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/880"><img src="/guides/img/public-02-cars-desktop-b6cd4fb8.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="880"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11.1%;top:56.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:3%;top:82.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:34%;top:87.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-choose-your-dates-on-the-car-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Choose your dates on the car page</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Dates and price, tap your pickup date, then your return date. Hatched days are already booked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the Pickup time and the Return time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Want it brought to you? Tick <b class="gd-ui">Deliver it to me</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Pick it up from me at the end</b>. Open Add-ons to add a baby seat, flowers, a full tank and more.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Check Your estimate, then press <b class="gd-ui">Request to book</b>. The add-ons you chose come with you.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/cars/2015-cadillac-cts-luxury</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1120/760"><img src="/guides/img/public-03-car-page-desktop-73be4d63.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1120" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:24.4%;top:39.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:12.9%;top:68.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:3%;top:76.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:97%;top:50%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>A request does not hold the car. The car is booked only once you approve the offer, sign and pay.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-send-your-request" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send your request</h2><p class="gd-p">The request has five short steps. Your answers are saved as you go, so you can come back.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Step 1, Dates and delivery: check the car and tap your dates in the calendar.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Set the Pickup time and Return time. Any time, day or night, with at least 2 hours of notice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Your request, on the right, shows the estimated total as you go.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/book/2015-cadillac-cts-luxury?from=2026-12-04&amp;to=2026-12-07&amp;tf=10:00&amp;tt=10:00</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1002"><img src="/guides/img/public-04-book-1-trip-desktop-63a3738b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1002"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.2%;top:67.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.3%;top:91%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91.1%;top:54.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="4"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Choose where you get the car: <b class="gd-ui">At our location</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Deliver it to an address</b> or <b class="gd-ui">At the airport</b>. Then choose where you return it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Continue to driver details</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/book/2015-cadillac-cts-luxury?from=2026-12-04&amp;to=2026-12-07&amp;tf=10:00&amp;tt=10:00</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:760/942"><img src="/guides/img/public-04-book-1-trip-desktop-befba4f6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="760" height="942"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:5.3%;top:26.2%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:61.8%;top:93.3%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="6"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Step 2, The driver: fill in your first and last name, email, mobile number and date of birth. Signed in? They are filled in from your profile, with your licence class and how we reach you: check them and change anything. A licence that has expired, or an address on file over a year old, is flagged for you to update in your profile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Someone else will drive too? Add them under Additional drivers (drivers you named before are one tap away). Each needs a G2 or G licence and signs the agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Continue to licence</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/book/2015-cadillac-cts-luxury?from=2026-12-04&amp;to=2026-12-07&amp;tf=10:00&amp;tt=10:00</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:980/1032"><img src="/guides/img/public-05-book-2-driver-desktop-7b572499.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="980" height="1032"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:30.6%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:30.6%;top:64.8%" aria-hidden="true">7</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:55.6%;top:88%" aria-hidden="true">8</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="9"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Step 3: choose your Licence class, for example Ontario G2.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Choose how the car is covered: Option 1 (OPCF 27 on your own auto policy), Option 2 (rental coverage on your credit card) or Option 3 (the CarmaCars Protection Plan). You can change this any time before pickup. You may also see a link to RentalCoverage, a separate company&#39;s optional product. It is not issued or handled by CarmaCars and does not replace the option you choose here, and we may earn a commission if you buy it, at no extra cost to you.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the Booking type: Standard, or Non-refundable for 10% off with no refund.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Add anything we should know in the notes, for example a flight number. If a body shop, a tow company or a friend sent you, type their name or the referral code from their card in Did someone refer you?.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Continue to add-ons</b>. Step 4, Add-ons: tick what you want (see Add-ons below), then press <b class="gd-ui">Review request</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/book/2015-cadillac-cts-luxury?from=2026-12-04&amp;to=2026-12-07&amp;tf=10:00&amp;tt=10:00</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:760/1452"><img src="/guides/img/public-06-book-3-licence-desktop-22bb144e.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="760" height="1452"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:61.8%;top:11.2%" aria-hidden="true">9</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.1%;top:32.2%" aria-hidden="true">10</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.1%;top:50.4%" aria-hidden="true">11</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.1%;top:66.9%" aria-hidden="true">12</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:71.7%;top:97%" aria-hidden="true">13</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="14"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">Step 5, Check it and send: read every line. Use Edit beside a line to change it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">15</span><div class="gd-t">Tick the box to confirm you are 18 or older and agree to the Terms of use and Privacy policy.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">16</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send request</b>. Nothing is charged and no card is needed.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/book/2015-cadillac-cts-luxury?from=2026-12-04&amp;to=2026-12-07&amp;tf=10:00&amp;tt=10:00</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:760/492"><img src="/guides/img/public-07-book-4-review-desktop-005f4c0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="760" height="492"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.1%;top:24.8%" aria-hidden="true">14</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:3.9%;top:59.3%" aria-hidden="true">15</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:73.7%;top:89%" aria-hidden="true">16</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--side"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="17"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">17</span><div class="gd-t">The confirmation shows your request number, for example CC-10021. Keep it for any question.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">18</span><div class="gd-t">A person checks the calendar, your dates and your place, usually within 2 hours, day or night. Your offer arrives by email and in Trips.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/755"><img src="/guides/img/public-08-book-5-sent-phone-14a99ccf.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="755"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.8%;top:12.3%" aria-hidden="true">17</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-upload-your-licence" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Upload your licence</h2><p class="gd-p">Right after you send your request: the front and back of your licence and a selfie holding it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Request sent page, press <b class="gd-ui">Upload your licence</b> (or open your booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Your licence</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Take each photo with your phone, or choose it. Add the licence number and expiry date if we ask: it must be valid after your return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Rented with us before? A licence on file that is still valid is used again; nothing to upload.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">We read each photo at once. Blurry or cut off? A message asks you to take it again: do it straight away. The licence details we read are filled in for you: check them and press <b class="gd-ui">These are right</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Change them</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>You need your licence on file to accept the offer.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-the-main-driver-needs-an-ontario-licence" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The main driver needs an Ontario licence</h2><p class="gd-p">The main driver of a booking holds an Ontario licence. Drivers with a licence from elsewhere can drive as extra drivers.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">If your licence is not from Ontario, your booking shows: &quot;The main driver needs an Ontario licence. Add a driver with an Ontario licence as the main driver. You&#39;ll stay on the booking as an extra driver.&quot;</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add main driver</b>. Enter their name, email, mobile and date of birth, then press <b class="gd-ui">Add main driver</b> again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Upload the front and back of their licence on the same page. They get their own link to accept and sign the agreement, which names them as the main driver.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">You have an Ontario licence after all? Press <b class="gd-ui">I have an Ontario licence: upload it instead</b> and upload it.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Pickup waits until the main driver has an Ontario licence on file. Your own licence photos stay on the booking: our team still checks them for you as an extra driver.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-add-ons" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add-ons</h2><p class="gd-p">Extras for your trip, such as a baby seat, a child or booster seat, flowers waiting in the car, a chauffeur, an umbrella, a phone charger or a full tank of gas.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the car page (under Add-ons) or in step 4 of the request, tick an add-on or use + and − for seats. The estimate shows the price at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each add-on shows its price: a trip, a day (with the most for a trip) or an hour. HST is added.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Some need notice, for example flowers need 24 hours. Seats and other items show how many are left for your dates.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A chauffeur is confirmed by our team in your offer.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">With a full tank of gas (prepaid) you can return the car at any fuel level, with no fuel charge.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-a-discount-code" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A discount code</h2><p class="gd-p">A code from a game on the site, an offer we sent you, or from our team.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>On the last step of your request, type it in the promo code box. The price shows the discount at once.</li><li>Every code has a last day. You find it in the email or text that brought the code, and under Your discount codes on Your trips.</li><li>If you have not used a code, we remind you 3 days before its last day and the day before, by email and text as you chose in Profile. A code you won in a game is always reminded; a reminder of an offer comes only if you agreed to get offers, and every email has an Unsubscribe link.</li><li>A code that ended is refused with &quot;This code has expired&quot;. You can still send the request without it.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-ask-in-the-chat" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Ask in the chat</h2><p class="gd-p">The chat button sits in the corner of every page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press it and write your question: a car, your dates, the price, how booking works. The CarmaCars assistant answers right away with prices from our booking system.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Want a person? Press <b class="gd-ui">Talk to a person</b>. When our team is away, leave your name and email or phone with <b class="gd-ui">Send my details</b> and tick &quot;Email me a copy of this chat&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">End chat</b> when you are done. If you gave your email, a copy of the chat arrives by email.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">A price in the chat is for the dates you asked. Nothing is booked until you approve an offer, sign and pay.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-carry-on-later" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Carry on later</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Your name, email and mobile number are saved as you type them, so nothing is lost if you stop. We open an account for you with that email.</li><li>Every form that saves as you type says so under it: &quot;Saved as you type so you can pick up where you left off.&quot;, with a link to the privacy policy.</li><li>On the same phone or computer, open <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/account</span> (or the request page again) to carry on, no password needed.</li><li>We send you one email, &quot;Continue your request&quot;. One tap signs you in, confirms your email and opens your request on any device. You need it before you can accept an offer, sign or pay.</li><li>Already have an account? The form says &quot;You have an account: we sent you a sign-in link&quot;.</li></ul><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Search:</b> the <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> button at the top of every page finds cars, places, help and, once you are signed in, your own bookings by number or car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-book-instantly-when-you-have-rented-with-us" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book instantly when you have rented with us</h2><p class="gd-p">After a completed rental, with your licence verified and nothing owing, you can book an available car instantly: you go straight to sign and pay, without waiting for an offer.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="find-a-car-and-send-a-request-book-again-instantly-and-coverage-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book again instantly, and coverage (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Rented with us before and verified? Book an available car instantly: sign and pay at once, with no wait for an offer. Your next request goes to the person who helped you last time.</li><li>Pick your credit card from the list to see at once whether it covers the car. If it does not, use your own policy (OPCF 27: send the pink slip and the endorsement page) or the Protection Plan.</li><li>Delivery is priced by distance, with the first kilometres included, shown in your estimate.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('owner', 'bookings-and-your-own-use', 'chapter', 'home-and-your-vehicles', 'See every booking in your cars on a calendar, and book a car for yourself when it is free.

## See your bookings

1. Cars > Bookings shows two months of your cars on a calendar. Each block is a booking number.
2. All bookings lists every trip with its car, dates, amount and status.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-be31cbae.jpg "desktop; size: 980 1092; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 1 53.1 15.8, 2 12.2 94.5")

> Good to know: A booking can show as Booked, with its dates and no amount: its amounts show once we approve the statement that covers it, and your statement carries every booking you can see, and every booking paid by the renter. The only bookings left out are an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your car''s calendar: they are not part of your revenue, so they stay off your statements and payouts, and you see only that the car is unavailable for those dates. If one of them later starts counting, you get the new booking email then. Unavailable is time your car is in use by us with no revenue for you (for example an insurance hold). A booking expense or a Revenue Share set for one booking is listed on that booking with the reason, and on your statement.

## Book your own car

You pay no rental charge, fee or deposit. A renter''s confirmed booking comes first.

1. Open Cars > Bookings and use **Book my own car** on the right (or **Book it for myself** on the car''s page).
2. Choose the Vehicle, then the Pickup and Return date and time.
3. Add a Note (optional) for our team.
4. Press **Book my car**. You sign the same agreement a renter signs.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-a4500851.jpg "desktop; size: 450 570; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 2 92.2 14.6, 3 92.2 64.9, 4 42.2 89.6")

> Good to know: No price and no deposit apply to you. One booking can be 30 days at most, and you sign the rental agreement before pickup.

## Rideshare and repeat renters (release 35)

Renters may drive for rideshare and delivery platforms with the documents we issue. Verified repeat renters can book your car instantly when it is free, within your price limits.', 'Bookings and your own use', 'The bookings calendar and booking your own car.',
  'See every booking in your cars on a calendar, and book a car for yourself when it is free.

## See your bookings

1. Cars > Bookings shows two months of your cars on a calendar. Each block is a booking number.
2. All bookings lists every trip with its car, dates, amount and status.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-be31cbae.jpg "desktop; size: 980 1092; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 1 53.1 15.8, 2 12.2 94.5")

> Good to know: A booking can show as Booked, with its dates and no amount: its amounts show once we approve the statement that covers it, and your statement carries every booking you can see, and every booking paid by the renter. The only bookings left out are an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your car''s calendar: they are not part of your revenue, so they stay off your statements and payouts, and you see only that the car is unavailable for those dates. If one of them later starts counting, you get the new booking email then. Unavailable is time your car is in use by us with no revenue for you (for example an insurance hold). A booking expense or a Revenue Share set for one booking is listed on that booking with the reason, and on your statement.

## Rental history

Cars > Bookings also has the **Rental history**: every rental on your cars.

1. Each line: the booking number, the car and its plate, the pickup and the return, the days, the status and your earnings from your approved statements. Not on an approved statement yet: it says so.
2. Choose one car or all, and oldest or newest first. The totals at the top count every rental in the list.
3. Renter details, payments and deposits are never shown, and a cancelled booking is listed only when a charge was kept.

## Book your own car

You pay no rental charge, fee or deposit. A renter''s confirmed booking comes first.

1. Open Cars > Bookings and use **Book my own car** on the right (or **Book it for myself** on the car''s page).
2. Choose the Vehicle, then the Pickup and Return date and time.
3. Add a Note (optional) for our team.
4. Press **Book my car**. You sign the same agreement a renter signs.

![](/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-a4500851.jpg "desktop; size: 450 570; address: carmacars.ca/owner/bookings; pins: 2 92.2 14.6, 3 92.2 64.9, 4 42.2 89.6")

> Good to know: No price and no deposit apply to you. One booking can be 30 days at most, and you sign the rental agreement before pickup.

## Rideshare and repeat renters (release 35)

Renters may drive for rideshare and delivery platforms with the documents we issue. Verified repeat renters can book your car instantly when it is free, within your price limits.',
  '<p class="gd-p">See every booking in your cars on a calendar, and book a car for yourself when it is free.</p><section class="gd-task" id="bookings-and-your-own-use-see-your-bookings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">See your bookings</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Cars &gt; Bookings shows two months of your cars on a calendar. Each block is a booking number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">All bookings lists every trip with its car, dates, amount and status.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/bookings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:980/1092"><img src="/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-be31cbae.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="980" height="1092"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.1%;top:15.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:12.2%;top:94.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A booking can show as Booked, with its dates and no amount: its amounts show once we approve the statement that covers it, and your statement carries every booking you can see, and every booking paid by the renter. The only bookings left out are an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your car&#39;s calendar: they are not part of your revenue, so they stay off your statements and payouts, and you see only that the car is unavailable for those dates. If one of them later starts counting, you get the new booking email then. Unavailable is time your car is in use by us with no revenue for you (for example an insurance hold). A booking expense or a Revenue Share set for one booking is listed on that booking with the reason, and on your statement.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="bookings-and-your-own-use-rental-history" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental history</h2><p class="gd-p">Cars &gt; Bookings also has the <b class="gd-ui">Rental history</b>: every rental on your cars.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each line: the booking number, the car and its plate, the pickup and the return, the days, the status and your earnings from your approved statements. Not on an approved statement yet: it says so.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose one car or all, and oldest or newest first. The totals at the top count every rental in the list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Renter details, payments and deposits are never shown, and a cancelled booking is listed only when a charge was kept.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="bookings-and-your-own-use-book-your-own-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book your own car</h2><p class="gd-p">You pay no rental charge, fee or deposit. A renter&#39;s confirmed booking comes first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Cars &gt; Bookings and use <b class="gd-ui">Book my own car</b> on the right (or <b class="gd-ui">Book it for myself</b> on the car&#39;s page).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the Vehicle, then the Pickup and Return date and time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add a Note (optional) for our team.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Book my car</b>. You sign the same agreement a renter signs.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/bookings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:450/570"><img src="/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-a4500851.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="450" height="570"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.2%;top:14.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:92.2%;top:64.9%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.2%;top:89.6%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>No price and no deposit apply to you. One booking can be 30 days at most, and you sign the rental agreement before pickup.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="bookings-and-your-own-use-rideshare-and-repeat-renters-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rideshare and repeat renters (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Renters may drive for rideshare and delivery platforms with the documents we issue. Verified repeat renters can book your car instantly when it is free, within your price limits.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'people-and-access', 'chapter', 'getting-around-admin', 'Let people in, help them back in when they are locked out, and see exactly what they see. Every step is recorded in the audit log.

## Portals and sign-in

Open **People** > **Portals and view as**. Every portal has a card.

1. Each card links to **Its sign-in page**, the address to send that person.
2. Choose a person in the list on the card.
3. Press **Open as this person** to see that portal as they see it.

> Good to know: The site''s own test accounts (verify- addresses and Resend''s test inboxes) are marked "Test account" in People who can sign in. They sign in like anyone, but no real work is ever given to them (see Data health).

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-0361bf61.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 65.9 30.2, 2 58.1 39.4, 3 51.6 45.6")

## Invite a person

Invitations work for staff, field staff, owners and investors. The person gets our invitation email and chooses a password.

1. Under Invite a person, choose the Role: Staff (assistant), Field staff, Owner on file or Investor on file. Admin is not offered: only rent@carmacars.ca can be an Admin.
2. Fill in the Name and Email.
3. For staff, pick the Main function, and tick Also covers for any other function they help with. For field staff, pick the Field function.
4. Press **Invite**. The link in the email works for 24 hours.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-c10725cb.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 360; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 18.8 40.8, 2 50.0 40.8, 3 18.8 66.7, 4 9.8 87.8")

> Tip: Someone who already signs in gets the new role at once, with no email. Owners and investors must be on file first: People > Owners and People > Investors also have a one-click invite for a record without a sign-in.

## Add an investor

1. Open **People** > **Investors** and press **Add an investor**.
2. Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).
3. Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer''s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).
4. Invite now is ticked: press **Add and invite**. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.

## Send a password link

For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.

1. Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.
2. On their row, press **Send password link**. They get "Reset your CarmaCars password", valid for 24 hours.
3. **View as (...)** on the same row opens their portal, read only.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 440; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 74.8 6.6, 2 68.2 28.6, 3 84.1 28.6")

## View as: see what someone sees

1. A red banner says "Viewing as Name (email), read only." on every page.
2. Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.
3. Press **Exit** to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.

![](/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 620; address: carmacars.ca/owner; pins: 1 48.6 4.5, 3 94.4 4.5")

> Watch out: Can''t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.

## The audit log

**Settings** > **Logs**, the **Changes** tab, shows who changed what, and when.

1. Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.
2. Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.
3. Search by table, record id or value.

![](/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/audit; pins: 1 22.6 31.1, 2 39.0 46.4, 3 89.6 20.7")

## Staff and roles

**People** > **Team** opens Staff and roles.

1. Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then **Invite**.
2. Each row has **Send password link**, **View as (...)** and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).
3. Press **End access** to close their staff portal at once. **Restore** undoes it.

![](/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 780; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff; pins: 1 20.8 59.0, 2 94.4 86.7, 3 83.3 92.6")

## Admin access

**Settings**, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.

1. The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site''s nightly checks sign in with.
2. Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.
3. Change the list only if the business''s Admin address changes.

## Staff scorecards

See how each assistant is doing against the targets.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Scorecard**.
2. By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 350; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 2 21.1 42.9")

## Sales by staff member

See each person''s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Sales**. Press **By week** or **By month**.
2. The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.
3. Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.
4. A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press **Reassign** beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.
5. **Commission rate** gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). **Reverse** beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.
6. Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. **Home address** here changes it if it is wrong.
7. The whole team: **Today** > **Overview**, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press **Show**.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to | Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |

## Sales staff: in person or remote

Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.

1. Press **Work mode** on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.
2. The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month''s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.
3. On a remote person''s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. **Void** beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.
4. When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.

|  | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Rates | In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15% |
| Credit | In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing |
| Remote minimum | 400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings > Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor |

## An Admin has every staff page

An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.
## Two records of one person

When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: "Your CarmaCars accounts are now one". A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and **Merge into this record** under the renter still works as before.

1. Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.
2. Two different people after all? Press **Undo** and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.

## New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal

Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: the academy first, then their staff agreement, then everything else. Until the academy is passed they open only the academy, the guide, their profile and **Welcome**; after it, until the agreement is signed, only Welcome, their profile and their documents to sign.

1. The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire''s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.
2. **Team** > **Staff and roles**, **Staff agreements**: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire''s licence number), and **Waive** with the reason.
3. Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the academy and the agreement are done, shows the team''s WhatsApp group (Program settings, **WhatsApp team group link** and **WhatsApp Sales group link**; empty until you set them). The same link goes by email, once.

## Accounts locked for inactivity

A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, **Staff inactive lock days**) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees "Account locked for inactivity" when they sign in. You get an alert. On **Team** > **Staff and roles** the row says **Locked for inactivity**: press **Unlock**. The staff list shows each person''s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.

## Hours and the townhall

**Team** > **Timesheet**: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.

**Breaks and idle time (release 35).** Customer service, Fleet and Finance press **Start break** and **End break** next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On **Timesheet**, each person''s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. **Edit** or **Remove** a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is **Program settings** > va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period''s breaks).

While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, "Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min", and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with **Set Quo user** on Timesheet; the **Call** button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. **KPIs** shows **Idle minutes** against kpi_idle_minutes_week.

**Team** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 1:00 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week''s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; **Build again** refreshes the numbers. Set the call link in Program settings; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.

## The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)

1. The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time. To change it, press **Change the day or time** on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website''s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants'' live calls always take the hour before.
2. Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. **Join the call** on the townhall page, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.
3. When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows "Missed N townhalls" for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.
4. The deck''s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role''s numbers for the week. Press **Add a shout-out** on a tile to add yours.

## Where staff live (release 35)

Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.

## Staff onboarding, breaks and shifts (release 35)

- New staff open their portal after four steps in order: the academy, the staff agreement, confirming the team''s WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval (or a rejection with a reason the person sees). Everyone already working waits for the same approval once.
- Each person''s row on the Staff onboarding card in Settings and on the Fleet approvals list says exactly what is missing, for example "Waiting on: Academy (3 of 11 sections), Staff agreement signature". **Mark WhatsApp joined** records only the WhatsApp groups, at any step: it never passes the academy or signs the agreement, and it counts when the person reaches that step. Once the academy and the agreement are done, **Confirm WhatsApp and approve** marks the groups and approves in one press (Admins only, recorded in the audit log).
- Schedules: customer service, Fleet and Finance have a schedule per role, and an Admin can give one person their own. Today''s duty board shows who is working, late or absent.
- Breaks: office staff log a break from their home page, and the time on break is kept on their timesheet. While someone is on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused; otherwise a person with no activity for a while on a shift gets an alert, then the Admins do.
- Quiet hours: staff alerts held by a person''s quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, and no text goes to a renter at night (an answer asked for then arrives in the morning).
- Field staff set their availability (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday) on Welcome and later on My shifts or Profile; Fleet and Admin see it on the shift board.
- Standing weekly shifts are claimed by themselves up to two weeks ahead; the minimum shifts a week is a Program setting (2 in 7 days), and anyone under it gets a reminder and a To do.
- A published shift nobody has claimed 48 hours before it starts alerts Fleet and the Admins with the people to ask.
- Payroll runs every two weeks: Finance prepares it, an Admin approves it and records the payments. KPIs per role are on Team, KPIs, each against a target in Program settings.
- The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock the account until an Admin restores it.', 'People and access', 'Portals and sign-in, invitations, password links, View as, staff and scorecards.',
