See each person''s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Sales**. Press **By week** or **By month**.
2. The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.
3. Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.
4. A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press **Reassign** beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.
5. **Commission rate** gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). **Reverse** beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.
6. Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. **Home address** here changes it if it is wrong.
7. The whole team: **Today** > **Overview**, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press **Show**.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to | Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |

## Sales staff: in person or remote

Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.

1. Press **Work mode** on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.
2. The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month''s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.
3. On a remote person''s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. **Void** beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.
4. When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.

|  | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Rates | In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15% |
| Credit | In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing |
| Remote minimum | 400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings > Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor |

## An Admin has every staff page

An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.
## Two records of one person

When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: "Your CarmaCars accounts are now one". A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and **Merge into this record** under the renter still works as before.

1. Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.
2. Two different people after all? Press **Undo** and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.

## New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal

Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: the academy first, then their staff agreement, then everything else. Until the academy is passed they open only the academy, the guide, their profile and **Welcome**; after it, until the agreement is signed, only Welcome, their profile and their documents to sign.

1. The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire''s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.
2. **Team** > **Staff and roles**, **Staff agreements**: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire''s licence number), and **Waive** with the reason.
3. Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the academy and the agreement are done, shows the team''s WhatsApp group (Program settings, **WhatsApp team group link** and **WhatsApp Sales group link**; empty until you set them). The same link goes by email, once.

## Accounts locked for inactivity

A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, **Staff inactive lock days**) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees "Account locked for inactivity" when they sign in. You get an alert. On **Team** > **Staff and roles** the row says **Locked for inactivity**: press **Unlock**. The staff list shows each person''s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.

## Hours and the townhall

**Team** > **Timesheet**: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.

**Breaks and idle time (release 35).** Customer service, Fleet and Finance press **Start break** and **End break** next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On **Timesheet**, each person''s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. **Edit** or **Remove** a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is **Program settings** > va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period''s breaks).

While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, "Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min", and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with **Set Quo user** on Timesheet; the **Call** button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. **KPIs** shows **Idle minutes** against kpi_idle_minutes_week.

**Team** > **Townhall**: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 1:00 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week''s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; **Build again** refreshes the numbers. Set the call link in Program settings; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.

## The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)

1. The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time. To change it, press **Change the day or time** on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website''s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants'' live calls always take the hour before.
2. Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. **Join the call** on the townhall page, or **Check in** from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.
3. When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows "Missed N townhalls" for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.
4. The deck''s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role''s numbers for the week. Press **Add a shout-out** on a tile to add yours.

## Where staff live (release 35)

Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.

## Staff onboarding, breaks and shifts (release 35)

- New staff open their portal after four steps in order: the academy, the staff agreement, confirming the team''s WhatsApp groups, then an Admin''s or a Fleet VA''s approval (or a rejection with a reason the person sees). Everyone already working waits for the same approval once.
- Each person''s row on the Staff onboarding card in Settings and on the Fleet approvals list says exactly what is missing, for example "Waiting on: Academy (3 of 11 sections), Staff agreement signature". **Mark WhatsApp joined** records only the WhatsApp groups, at any step: it never passes the academy or signs the agreement, and it counts when the person reaches that step. Once the academy and the agreement are done, **Confirm WhatsApp and approve** marks the groups and approves in one press (Admins only, recorded in the audit log).
- Schedules: customer service, Fleet and Finance have a schedule per role, and an Admin can give one person their own. Today''s duty board shows who is working, late or absent.
- Breaks: office staff log a break from their home page, and the time on break is kept on their timesheet. While someone is on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused; otherwise a person with no activity for a while on a shift gets an alert, then the Admins do.
- Quiet hours: staff alerts held by a person''s quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, and no text goes to a renter at night (an answer asked for then arrives in the morning).
- Field staff set their availability (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday) on Welcome and later on My shifts or Profile; Fleet and Admin see it on the shift board.
- Standing weekly shifts are claimed by themselves up to two weeks ahead; the minimum shifts a week is a Program setting (2 in 7 days), and anyone under it gets a reminder and a To do.
- Shifts are published by themselves every hour from the shift template in Program settings (Field jobs and handovers: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day, up to 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift already published and never before the start date set there). A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own, 90 minutes either side.
- A published shift nobody has claimed 48 hours before it starts alerts Fleet and the Admins with the people to ask.
- Payroll runs every two weeks: Finance prepares it, an Admin approves it and records the payments. KPIs per role are on Team, KPIs, each against a target in Program settings.
- The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock the account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, cancelled ahead, or marked by an Admin) counts nobody absent.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Let people in, help them back in when they are locked out, and see exactly what they see. Every step is recorded in the audit log.</p><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-portals-and-sign-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Portals and sign-in</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Portals and view as</b>. Every portal has a card.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each card links to <b class="gd-ui">Its sign-in page</b>, the address to send that person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose a person in the list on the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Open as this person</b> to see that portal as they see it.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The site&#39;s own test accounts (verify- addresses and Resend&#39;s test inboxes) are marked &quot;Test account&quot; in People who can sign in. They sign in like anyone, but no real work is ever given to them (see Data health).</div></aside><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/820"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-0361bf61.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:65.9%;top:30.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:58.1%;top:39.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:51.6%;top:45.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-invite-a-person" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Invite a person</h2><p class="gd-p">Invitations work for staff, field staff, owners and investors. The person gets our invitation email and chooses a password.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Invite a person, choose the Role: Staff (assistant), Field staff, Owner on file or Investor on file. Admin is not offered: only rent@carmacars.ca can be an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in the Name and Email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For staff, pick the Main function, and tick Also covers for any other function they help with. For field staff, pick the Field function.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Invite</b>. The link in the email works for 24 hours.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/360"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-c10725cb.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="360"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.8%;top:40.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:40.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.8%;top:66.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.8%;top:87.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Someone who already signs in gets the new role at once, with no email. Owners and investors must be on file first: People &gt; Owners and People &gt; Investors also have a one-click invite for a record without a sign-in.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-add-an-investor" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add an investor</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Add an investor</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer&#39;s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Invite now is ticked: press <b class="gd-ui">Add and invite</b>. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-send-a-password-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send a password link</h2><p class="gd-p">For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On their row, press <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>. They get &quot;Reset your CarmaCars password&quot;, valid for 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> on the same row opens their portal, read only.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/portals</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/440"><img src="/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="440"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.8%;top:6.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:68.2%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.1%;top:28.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-view-as-see-what-someone-sees" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">View as: see what someone sees</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A red banner says &quot;Viewing as Name (email), read only.&quot; on every page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Exit</b> to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/620"><img src="/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="620"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:4.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Can&#39;t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-audit-log" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The audit log</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Logs</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Changes</b> tab, shows who changed what, and when.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Search by table, record id or value.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/audit</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.6%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:39%;top:46.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:89.6%;top:20.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-and-roles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff and roles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> opens Staff and roles.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then <b class="gd-ui">Invite</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each row has <b class="gd-ui">Send password link</b>, <b class="gd-ui">View as (...)</b> and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">End access</b> to close their staff portal at once. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> undoes it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/780"><img src="/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="780"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:59%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:94.4%;top:86.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:92.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-admin-access" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Admin access</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site&#39;s nightly checks sign in with.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Change the list only if the business&#39;s Admin address changes.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-scorecards" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff scorecards</h2><p class="gd-p">See how each assistant is doing against the targets.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Scorecard</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/va/scorecard</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/350"><img src="/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="350"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.1%;top:42.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-by-staff-member" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales by staff member</h2><p class="gd-p">See each person&#39;s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a staff member&#39;s row in Staff and roles, press <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">By week</b> or <b class="gd-ui">By month</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b> beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Commission rate</b> gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). <b class="gd-ui">Reverse</b> beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. <b class="gd-ui">Home address</b> here changes it if it is wrong.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The whole team: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b>, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Figure</th><th scope="col">How it is counted</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Credited to</td><td>Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it.</td></tr><tr><td>Conversion</td><td>Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far.</td></tr><tr><td>Booked revenue</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off.</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-sales-staff-in-person-or-remote" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sales staff: in person or remote</h2><p class="gd-p">Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Work mode</b> on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month&#39;s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a remote person&#39;s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. <b class="gd-ui">Void</b> beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Rule</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Rates</td><td>In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15%</td></tr><tr><td>Credit</td><td>In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing</td></tr><tr><td>Remote minimum</td><td>400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month&#39;s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings &gt; Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-an-admin-has-every-staff-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">An Admin has every staff page</h2><p class="gd-p">An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-two-records-of-one-person" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Two records of one person</h2><p class="gd-p">When two renter records are clearly the same person (the same phone verified with a code, or the same name, date of birth and phone), the site merges them by itself within 15 minutes, into the record with more bookings. Bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages move. The person can then sign in with either email or with their phone number and a code, and gets one short note: &quot;Your CarmaCars accounts are now one&quot;. A match on the name alone stays a task for you, and <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> under the renter still works as before.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the renter. The Merged records card lists each merge, automatic or by staff, with what moved and the emails that now sign in there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Two different people after all? Press <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> and say why. Everything moved goes back and both records are as they were.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-new-staff-the-academy-then-the-agreement-then-the-portal" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">New staff: the academy, then the agreement, then the portal</h2><p class="gd-p">Every staff member (never an Admin) opens their portal in this order: the academy first, then their staff agreement, then everything else. Until the academy is passed they open only the academy, the guide, their profile and <b class="gd-ui">Welcome</b>; after it, until the agreement is signed, only Welcome, their profile and their documents to sign.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The agreement is sent by itself to everyone without one, filled from their record and their hire&#39;s pay and start date: the Field Staff Agreement for field work, the contractor agreement for customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales (in person or remote). One reminder goes 3 days after it was sent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Staff agreements</b>: who has not signed, what the automatic send waits for (for example a field hire&#39;s licence number), and <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Welcome also asks for the name they go by (the preferred name, shown across the portals and on the staff list), and, once the academy and the agreement are done, shows the team&#39;s WhatsApp group (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">WhatsApp team group link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">WhatsApp Sales group link</b>; empty until you set them). The same link goes by email, once.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-accounts-locked-for-inactivity" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Accounts locked for inactivity</h2><p class="gd-p">A staff account with no sign-in or use for 10 days (Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Staff inactive lock days</b>) is locked; the person is warned by email on day 7 and sees &quot;Account locked for inactivity&quot; when they sign in. You get an alert. On <b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Staff and roles</b> the row says <b class="gd-ui">Locked for inactivity</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b>. The staff list shows each person&#39;s last sign-in. Admin accounts are never locked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-hours-and-the-townhall" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Hours and the townhall</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>: the hours customer service, Fleet and Finance clocked (Clock in and out on their home page). Add hours someone forgot, or void a wrong entry, with the reason. A person not clocked in 15 minutes after their start time (customer service 9:00, Fleet 11:00, Toronto) is reminded.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Breaks and idle time (release 35).</b> Customer service, Fleet and Finance press <b class="gd-ui">Start break</b> and <b class="gd-ui">End break</b> next to the clock; breaks have no fixed length. On <b class="gd-ui">Timesheet</b>, each person&#39;s days show the hours clocked and worked, their breaks (how many, the total and the longest) and their idle time, with every break and idle stretch listed. <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> a break with the reason (in the audit log). Finance sees the breaks but never the idle time. A break open past 30 minutes reminds the person and you. Whether breaks are paid is <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; va_breaks_paid (on: salaried; off: breaks come off the hours on the payroll, where each line shows the period&#39;s breaks).</p><p class="gd-p">While someone is clocked in, not on a break and within their scheduled hours, the portal notes the fact of their activity (never keys, pages or screens), at most once a minute; their actions count too. With no activity for more than va_idle_alert_minutes (10), you get one alert, &quot;Name (role) inactive since 10:42, 12 min&quot;, and one more at va_idle_followup_minutes (30). A call they are on (their Quo user, set with <b class="gd-ui">Set Quo user</b> on Timesheet; the <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> button; a note in the caller pop-up) and the townhall (joined or present, to its end plus 10 minutes) pause it. <b class="gd-ui">KPIs</b> shows <b class="gd-ui">Idle minutes</b> against kpi_idle_minutes_week.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Team</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Townhall</b>: the weekly staff call (Wednesdays at 1:00 pm Toronto). The deck builds itself every Sunday night from the week&#39;s data: the week, platform updates, fleet, staff, sales with the leaderboard, finances and claims (the last two for Admins only). Add a note to any slide; <b class="gd-ui">Build again</b> refreshes the numbers. Set the call link in Program settings; staff add the call to their calendar from the page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-the-townhall-day-attendance-and-the-team-slide-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The townhall day, attendance and the team slide (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time. To change it, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the day or time</b> on the Townhall page. Beside it, a table shows the website&#39;s visitor sessions of the last 8 weeks for each day, as information. Field applicants&#39; live calls always take the hour before.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Every staff member is invited and reminded an hour before. <b class="gd-ui">Join the call</b> on the townhall page, or <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> from 15 minutes before, counts them as there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When the call ends, the people who missed it are recorded, the staff list shows &quot;Missed N townhalls&quot; for the last 8 weeks, and you get an alert with the names.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The deck&#39;s last slide is the team: a tile per person with their role&#39;s numbers for the week. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a shout-out</b> on a tile to add yours.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-where-staff-live-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where staff live (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Welcome asks every hire for their city and country. In the Toronto area Sales keep the mode they were hired in; elsewhere Sales is remote. The staff list shows the location.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="people-and-access-staff-onboarding-breaks-and-shifts-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff onboarding, breaks and shifts (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>New staff open their portal after four steps in order: the academy, the staff agreement, confirming the team&#39;s WhatsApp groups, then an Admin&#39;s or a Fleet VA&#39;s approval (or a rejection with a reason the person sees). Everyone already working waits for the same approval once.</li><li>Each person&#39;s row on the Staff onboarding card in Settings and on the Fleet approvals list says exactly what is missing, for example &quot;Waiting on: Academy (3 of 11 sections), Staff agreement signature&quot;. <b class="gd-ui">Mark WhatsApp joined</b> records only the WhatsApp groups, at any step: it never passes the academy or signs the agreement, and it counts when the person reaches that step. Once the academy and the agreement are done, <b class="gd-ui">Confirm WhatsApp and approve</b> marks the groups and approves in one press (Admins only, recorded in the audit log).</li><li>Schedules: customer service, Fleet and Finance have a schedule per role, and an Admin can give one person their own. Today&#39;s duty board shows who is working, late or absent.</li><li>Breaks: office staff log a break from their home page, and the time on break is kept on their timesheet. While someone is on a break, on a call or in the townhall, the idle alert is paused; otherwise a person with no activity for a while on a shift gets an alert, then the Admins do.</li><li>Quiet hours: staff alerts held by a person&#39;s quiet hours arrive as one summary when they end, and no text goes to a renter at night (an answer asked for then arrives in the morning).</li><li>Field staff set their availability (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday) on Welcome and later on My shifts or Profile; Fleet and Admin see it on the shift board.</li><li>Standing weekly shifts are claimed by themselves up to two weeks ahead; the minimum shifts a week is a Program setting (2 in 7 days), and anyone under it gets a reminder and a To do.</li><li>Shifts are published by themselves every hour from the shift template in Program settings (Field jobs and handovers: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 for one person, every second day, up to 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift already published and never before the start date set there). A handover or return no shift covers gets a shift of its own, 90 minutes either side.</li><li>A published shift nobody has claimed 48 hours before it starts alerts Fleet and the Admins with the people to ask.</li><li>Payroll runs every two weeks: Finance prepares it, an Admin approves it and records the payments. KPIs per role are on Team, KPIs, each against a target in Program settings.</li><li>The townhall is every Wednesday at 1:00 pm Toronto time; two missed in a row lock the account until an Admin restores it. A townhall that did not happen (nobody attended, cancelled ahead, or marked by an Admin) counts nobody absent.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'requests-offers-and-bookings', 'chapter', 'people-and-access', 'A booking starts as a request from the website, or as an offer you send yourself to a customer on the phone. You check it, adjust it and send the offer; an offer that is out is changed in place. After that, the booking page holds the money, documents, changes and history.

## Bookings now: what is out, coming back and owed

Open **Bookings**. It opens on **Now**, one screen that refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. Every time is Toronto time.

1. The numbers at the top: cars out now, due back today, overdue, going out in the next 72 hours, payments due in the next 7 days (with the total) and free cars. Tap one to jump to its list.
2. **Out now**: every car on rent, overdue returns first in red. Each shows the car (photo, code, plate), the renter with **Call** and **Text**, when it was picked up, when it is due back with a countdown, the payment plan and the next payment, the deposit held, and the km and fuel at pickup. Filter by Overdue, Due today or Payment due.
3. A confirmed booking whose pickup time has passed with no check-in recorded is listed as out, with **Out (pickup not recorded)**. The car most likely left. Press **Mark picked up**: it records the pickup at the booked time (change it if the car left at another time), the booking goes on rent, and Fleet gets a task to add the photos, km and fuel. The usual checks stay: the deposit taken (or an Admin waives it with the reason), the renter''s signature (or an Admin''s reason), the agreement''s details, every driver verified and the coverage confirmed. If one is missing, the reason is shown.
4. **Coming back**: overdue, today and tomorrow, by the time each is due.
5. **Going out**: confirmed pickups in the next 72 hours, delivery or pickup, with ticks and crosses for the licence, the signed agreement, the payment, the deposit (a clock until the morning of the pickup day, when the hold is placed on the card on file) and the check-in photos (done at the handover).
6. **Money due**: every rental payment due in the next 7 days or overdue, the amount, the plan and which payment it is (for example 3 of 4).
7. **Free now**: cars available and not out, the longest idle first, with the next pickup; then the cars in maintenance or cleaning. Partners'' cars are counted apart.

> Good to know: Placeholder bookings never show on Now.

### Payment plans

A rental is paid in full at pickup, weekly, every 2 weeks, or monthly. A rental longer than one period (30 days) pays each period by itself. To change it, open the booking, then the **Payment plan** card on Overview or Money, and press **Change the plan**. Each payment is its share of the total by its days, due on the day it starts. An insurer-billed rental shows **Insurer billed** and is never in Money due unless the renter owes a part. Admins, customer service and finance change the plan; fleet sees it.

## All bookings

The **All bookings** tab of Bookings has the search (booking number, name, email, phone, plate or car code), the status (All, Out now, Booked, Returned, Cancelled; closed bookings are found with the search, which also finds the insurer). **Out now** shows the bookings on rent and those whose pickup passed without a check-in, together. Each booking is one row: its number and status in plain words, the car with its photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the dates, the money (paid up, to pay, overdue, insurer billed) and Bill to.

## The request queue

Open **Bookings** > **Requests and offers**. The oldest waiting request is at the top.

1. The numbers at the top: waiting for an offer, past the reply target (red), offers out, accepted but not paid, and offers expired. Each one is a filter: press it and the list shows just those, with the matching chip below marked as chosen.
2. One queue, the most urgent first: the longest wait, then offers accepted but not paid, then offers out by when they expire. Each row has the car with its photo, the dates, the price, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence (verified, to review, or not uploaded yet), who is answering it, and one button: **Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**. **Decline** sits beside **Send offer**.
3. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited ("12 min", "3 h", "2 days"); red means past the first reply target (5 minutes, set in Program settings). **Promise** counts down the 2 hours the site promises the renter.
4. Filter by Active, New, Changes asked, Offer out, Accepted, not paid or Expired. The list remembers your last choice on that device; **Active** always shows the whole queue and replaces what it remembered. When the same renter asks for the same car for overlapping dates again and the earlier request or offer expired, only the newest is listed: the older ones are linked to it and leave Requests (they keep their history). An expired offer leaves the active queue 48 hours after it expired, or once its pickup time passed; Expired lists the ones from the last 7 days. After 7 days an expired offer leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead, once, in People > Renters > Leads (Expired offers), with the car and the dates the renter wanted and a To do for Sales to win them back. An offer still out when its pickup time passes expires by itself.

![](/guides/img/admin-02-requests-desktop-6521282d.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/requests; pins: 1 38.9 29.9, 2 22.2 43.3")

> Good to know: A request whose pickup time passes without an offer expires by itself, with a note in its history. The renter is not emailed unless "Email the renter when their request expires that way" is on in Program settings.

## Answer a request with an offer

1. The Review and offer tab shows the request as the renter sent it.
2. Adjust the car, the dates, the rate type, the places, the rates (under **Show rate card**) and fees, the deposit and extras. A place changed away from a delivery or a collection takes its fee box and its fee with it.
3. Price on the right updates as you change things.
4. Add a message, choose how long the offer stays open, then press **Send the offer**.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-353f3707.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 1550; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 1 5.0 6.5, 2 7.5 45.8, 3 74.2 42.6, 4 76.7 98.1")

5. Changed fields but not ready to send? Press **Save changes**. The panel "The offer as the renter sees it" shows the result.
6. Can''t do it? Press **Decline** and fill in Reason and any alternative.
7. Need an answer first? Press **Ask the renter** to send a question.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-4dd4ed06.jpg "desktop; size: 500 80; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 6 41.2 52.5, 7 18.0 52.5")

Opening a request takes it for you: everyone else sees "Being answered by" your name and since when, with Send the offer and Decline off, until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work; Program settings). Press **Take over** to answer one someone else holds; it is noted in the history. A second answer is refused with who answered and when. A request from the website opens to Sales after 15 minutes (Program settings); until then Admins, customer service and fleet answer it.

## Send an offer without a request

Press **Send an offer** at the top of Bookings, or **Send an offer without a request** on Requests and offers. For a customer on the phone, by text or at the counter: no request needed.

The screen is seven short steps, each with one line saying what to do, and the price beside it (on a phone the total sits at the bottom of the screen: press **See every line**). What most offers never need is under each step''s **More options**, which stays open while something in it is used.

1. **Who is renting and when**: find the renter by name, phone or email, or press **Not on file? Add a new customer** (full legal name, mobile, email for the offer link, date of birth). A customer already on file with the same email or phone is shown with Use: one person, one record. Then the pickup and the return.
2. **Which car**: search by car code, plate or name; each car says Free or Not free for the dates. More options: the rate card and the type and free-only filters.
3. **Where they pick up and return**: at our location, we deliver or collect (the address and distance), an airport or the owner''s location. The fee each one makes shows under it, Automatic or Set by hand.
4. **How damage is covered**: the renter''s own insurance, a credit card or the Protection Plan. More options: another Protection Plan price.
5. **Extras**: add-ons, when the car has any.
6. **The price**: the rate sheet price is filled in. More options: another price (a total for the trip or a rate a day, with why), Amounts I type (before or after HST), the total the renter pays, kilometres, a promo code, the deposit and a discount (an Admin), and **Fees**: press **Change** to set one by hand, **Reset to automatic** to undo it. Below: how it is paid (card online and a card hold unless you change it under More options).
7. **Send it**: who found this client (sales and customer service), a message, and Text or Email. More options: how long the offer is open, the owner''s view, who found the client (an Admin) and the internal note. Above the button, **Ready to send** or **Missing:** with what is left; press Send and each missing field says what it needs. Press **Send the offer to** the renter, or **Save without sending** to keep it as a request for later. **The offer as the renter sees it** is under the price.

> Good to know: Choices drive the charges. Take off a delivery, a collection, the Protection Plan or an add-on and its fee goes with it, even a fee set by hand: there is nothing to remove in a second place. Choose it again and the fee starts from the automatic amount.

> Good to know: It makes the same request and offer the website makes: the renter approves, signs and pays (or you record the payment), and only then is the car on the calendar. No "request received" email goes to the renter for an offer you send. Staff commissions and statements count it like any other booking.

## Change an offer that is out

The renter has the offer (Offered), or approved it and has not paid (Signing and payment). Open **More actions** on the booking and press **Edit the offer**.

1. Change anything: the car, the dates, the places, the price, fees, the deposit, add-ons, how it is paid. Each changed field is highlighted and the before and after are listed. Amounts I type (Before tax or After tax) and the Total the renter pays (after tax) work as on Send an offer.
2. Write what changed in Message to the renter and choose how long the offer is open.
3. Press **Save and send the update**: the renter gets the new version by email or text (ticked), and the old version no longer counts. Or press **Save without telling the renter** and tell them yourself.
4. A confirmed booking is changed with **Change the booking** (Propose a change, below).

> Tip: No need to withdraw first. **Withdraw the offer** is only for taking it back for good; **Send again, later expiry** gives the renter more time, and **Renter approved by phone** records a yes given on a call.

## Edit a booking that has started

On a confirmed, on-trip or returned booking (an Admin: a closed one too), Overview, **Edit the booking**, **Edit**.

1. Change the pickup or the return (extend or shorten: the rental charge is worked out again at this booking''s rates), the car (on trip: the car it leaves goes to Out of service for Fleet to check), the rental charge for the trip, each fee, the kilometres a day, the deposit (an Admin) and the note.
2. Type why, if you like, and tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction. Press **Save the changes**.
3. What is open now shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, **Charge** the saved card (the renter agreed), or record cash or an e-Transfer on the Money tab.

> Good to know: Each edit is kept with who, when, why, before and after (Edits, under the form) and in the booking''s history. A closed booking''s owner split and the staff commission follow. To have the renter accept and sign first, use Propose a change instead.

## Fees, a forgotten fee and the balance

On the booking''s Money tab, Fees lists each fee. Press **Change or add a fee**.

1. Type a new amount (for the whole trip, before HST) beside any fee, or choose one not on the booking (the young driver fee shows its price for these dates), or add a charge of its own with or without HST.
2. Press **Save the fees**. The balance shows by part (rental, fees) with the pay link, the saved card and Record a payment beside it.
3. The renter sees the balance on their booking with a Pay button, and pays by card on Stripe''s form.

> Good to know: Every change is recorded (Changes to the fees): the amount before and after, who and why. Customer service and sales may change fees while Program settings, Staff may change fees, is on.

## A renter with only a debit or prepaid card

A credit card is required by default: the deposit must be on a credit card so the deductible can be charged. The pay page tells a renter with only a debit or prepaid card to contact us.

1. On the booking''s Money tab, press **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** and type the reason. Who and when are kept, and the change is in the booking''s history.
2. The booking''s pay page, staff pay links and deposit hold then take a debit or prepaid card, and the renter is told the hold lowers the money available on the card until it is released, which can take several business days.
3. **Require a credit card again** turns it off.

The Money tab shows each card used and its type (credit, debit, prepaid). A booking on credit card rental coverage is always paid on the credit card that carries the coverage, and cannot be allowed. Program settings, **Card types accepted**, can open debit and prepaid cards to every booking.

## Correct a renter''s details

On the renter''s page (People, Renters) or on any of their bookings, **Edit renter**.

1. Correct the name, email, phone, date of birth, licence, home address (start typing to find it) or the staff note.
2. A new email also becomes their sign-in at once (no confirmation needed for a typo you correct); tick **Email the renter a link to set a password** to send one there. Unsigned agreements and offers go to the new address.
3. Press **Save the renter**. An email that another renter has is refused with their name; the same phone is a warning.
4. The same person entered twice? Possible duplicates (same email, same phone, or same name and date of birth) shows under the renter. **Merge into this record** moves the other record''s bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages here and fills any detail missing here; the other record stays, blocked, with the merge in both histories.

## The Money tab: Rental charges and Security deposit

The booking''s Money tab opens on a strip with the three numbers that matter: **Rental due**, **Deposit** (one word: Not collected, Held, Charged, Released or Partly kept) and **Total paid**. Below are two panels, side by side on a computer and one above the other on a phone. Collecting one never touches the other, and every receipt says which one it is.

**Rental charges**: each line of the price and the total, Paid, then Balance due.

1. The one main button, Collect (the amount) rental: choose how. **The card on file** charges it now (Finance or an Admin); **A payment link by text** or **A payment link by email** sends the renter Stripe''s secure form; **On this device: hand it to the renter** opens it for the renter to type; **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)** records money received (an e-Transfer, cheque or transfer needs its reference). For: the rental and fees together by default, or one of them. With the card on file, the rental and fees together are one charge with one receipt that lists both (the rental is paid first, then the fees; an insurer''s part and money already received another way are left out). The renter gets a receipt; **Print** prints one to hand over.
2. **A later charge** (before the return): on the card on file, by a link, on this device, or recorded. Choose the **Reason** from the list (Mileage overage, Fuel, Cleaning, Smoking, Late return, Tolls, Tickets/fines, Damage, Missing items, Other) and add a note; Other needs its note. The renter''s receipt shows the reason.
3. **Save a card** saves the renter''s card without charging it. Card readers, the fees (**Change or add a fee**), failed card payments (**Paid another way**), payments received another way and **Refund** sit in this panel too. The history lists rental payments only.
4. An offer paid another way: once the renter approved and signed and the money is recorded, the booking is confirmed (or press **Confirm the booking**).

**Security deposit**: the amount, how it is taken (a credit card hold, a debit or prepaid card at the standard multiple, a charge, or cash), its status in one word and the next step.

1. Not collected: the one main button, Collect (the amount) deposit. **Hold on the card on file** places the hold now (Finance or an Admin); **A deposit hold link by text** or **A deposit hold link by email**, or **A hold on this device: hand it to the renter**; **Charge the card on file as the deposit** only when no hold can be placed; **Cash or e-Transfer (record it)**. The rental balance is not touched.
2. Before every pickup the deposit hold link is texted to the renter on its own: 24 hours before (at once when the pickup is sooner), for a confirmed booking whose deposit is a card hold with no hold yet. The panel says **Deposit link texted** and when it was opened. No mobile number, or the text not sent: a task **Deposit link not sent**. **Settings**, then Site settings, Deposit link by text: on or off, and the hours.
3. Held, while the car is out: **Release** (an Admin, with the reason), **Keep part (damage/fees)** with the amount and the reason from the list, or **Re-authorize the hold** on the saved card before it lapses (the panel shows when the hold expires). A job re-authorizes it by itself about 24 hours before it expires; if it cannot, Finance and the Admins get the alert **Deposit hold not re-authorized**.
4. **Hold expired**: a card hold lasts about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. Once it has expired, nothing can be kept from it: the panel says Hold expired, Keep and Release are hidden, and **Charge the card on file instead** opens the later charge with the amount and the reason filled in.
4. After the return: **Settle the deposit** (below).
5. **Waive the deposit** (an Admin, before it is taken), **Change the debit deposit**, and **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** sit in this panel. The history lists deposit payments only.
6. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way after the return: Finance gets a task; press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

> Good to know: Statements, reconciliation and the deposit settlement read each payment with its method: a cash deposit is never refunded to a card.

## Settle the deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-out statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: **Keep the whole deposit (damage)** turns what is left of the deposit into a damage charge, with what was damaged and the photos; the renter is told. **Bill damage** adds a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible (more goes through a claim): the deposit pays first, then the card on file.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## A booking

Open **Bookings** > **Bookings**, then a booking number. Or type the number in the search box.

1. Tabs: Overview, Money, Changes, History, and Drivers and documents.
2. Overview shows the trip, the renter, what is still missing for the handover, and the price.
3. Open tasks for this booking, with the queue and the due time.
4. Top right: **Email the renter** and **More actions**, the menu with **Edit the offer**, **Stop blocking the calendar**, **Cancel for the renter**, **Cancel by CarmaCars** and the rest.
5. Under the booking number: **Next step**, what happens next and who does it, with one button for that step (for example **Send the offer**, **Sign on this device** or **Check in the car**); then where the booking is on its way, from Request to Closed, with the dates, the days, the total and who pays.

![](/guides/img/admin-04-booking-desktop-b56b668a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 960; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065; pins: 2 50.0 46.6, 4 85.4 14.5, 5 22.9 26.8")

## Check a car out or in

From the booking, with your phone or a tablet: the same checklist field staff use.

1. A confirmed booking shows **Check in (pickup)** under Check-in, check-out and signing; a booking on rent shows **Check out (return)**. Today lists the check-ins and check-outs due, each with **Check in** or **Check out**.
2. The checklist opens: the ready check, the renter and their licence and card, the odometer (km) and fuel or charge, the keys, the photo set (every side, the wheels, the interior, the odometer and fuel gauge, the plate), damage marks with close-ups, then the renter and you sign.
3. Photos wait on the device without a connection and upload in the background. Each keeps its time, and the place when the device allows location.
4. A field job of the booking is taken over (the history says so); with no job, one is made for you. When done, press **See the photo report**.

> Tip: Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in the same way from their own booking page.

## The photo report, late returns and the return charges

Under Check-in, check-out and signing, press **Photo report**.

1. The report shows the due-back time, the actual check-in and check-out, Late by (or Overdue by while the car is out), the odometer and kilometres over the allowance, the fuel or charge out and in, every photo with its time and place, and the damage.
2. At check-out the mileage overage and the fuel or recharging are written to the return charges at once. A late return (after the grace period of the fee defaults) is not: it waits for a choice on the booking (see "A late return is a choice"). The fuel is a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the pump price of its grade (Program settings, updated weekly) x 1.25, plus the refuelling fee; an electric car the battery kWh x the charge missing x the price a kWh, plus the fee. A pump receipt entered later replaces it. Fleet and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; it is never charged to a card by itself.
3. Not charging one? Press **Waive** beside it and give the reason: it stays waived if the charges are worked out again.
4. The time was wrong? Press **Correct the check-out time** (or the check-in time) with the reason: lateness follows, a return that is no longer late loses its late charge, and the history keeps both times.
5. The renter gets the same report (without these buttons) by email and in their Documents. Late by shows on the booking and in the Bookings list.

### The renter says the car is back

Every overdue email, text and alert (at the return time, at 15 minutes and the final notice) has a one-tap **I''ve returned the car** link, and the renter''s booking page has the button. The renter can add photos, the odometer, the fuel level and the time they returned it. Sending it stops every overdue notice of the booking at once, the booking shows **Returned, waiting for confirmation**, and Fleet gets an urgent To do: "The renter says the car is back".

1. Open the booking. The card **The renter says the car is back** shows what the renter gave, marked renter-provided, with their photos.
2. Check the car: the return place, the tracker, the photos.
3. Press **Confirm** to complete the trip. Correct the odometer, fuel or return time first if they are wrong: the late charges follow the time you confirm. The renter''s photos join the check-out report.
4. Or press **Deny** and say why. The renter gets your reason by email and text, and the overdue notices start again.

Checking the car in the usual way also completes the trip and stops the notices. Admins, Fleet, Sales, Customer service and field staff can Confirm or Deny.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

The renter or an additional driver signs the rental agreement on your device, or on their own phone.

1. While a signature is missing, the booking shows **Sign now on this device**, **Email the signing link** and **Text the signing link**.
2. No agreement made yet (the renter has not saved their details at home)? **Sign now on this device** still shows: press **Prepare the agreement to sign now** and it is made on the spot.
3. **Sign now on this device**: confirm the name matches their licence and that you saw the original licence (photograph it if none is on file), then press **Hand the device to** and their name.
4. They read both agreements (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), tick the statements and sign. Then **Back to the staff view** for the next signer.
5. The record is the same as signing online, and says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your device. It is printed on the signed copy''s signature record page.

## Rental agreements: every version, every field

The booking''s Rental agreements card: the current version of CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s agreements, every earlier one, and what is still blank.

1. Once the agreement is signed and countersigned, any change to what it prints makes a new version of both documents by itself: the dates, the price lines, the car, a driver added or corrected, the coverage, the deposit or how it was paid, an address.
2. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage option is signed again: the renter (and each driver it affects) gets their link by email and text, and the card shows "Agreement v3 waiting for signature". A correction (a typo in an address, a plate written differently) is filed without signing; the renter gets the corrected copy by email.
3. Check-in makes the "as picked up" copy (time out, km out, fuel out, the car''s plate and VIN, the check-in report), countersigned by whoever checked the car out; check-out makes the closing copy (time in, km in, driven and charged, fuel in, late hours, damage, the return charges, the final totals). Both go to the renter by email.
4. **Every version** lists each one with what changed and both PDFs. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your phone or tablet.
5. The card lists what the agreements still print blank (a licence expiry, the insurer''s policy number, the insured vehicle, a VIN). Type the values and press **Save the missing fields**: the agreements follow.
6. Check-in stops while a field a claim needs is blank. An Admin can let it go ahead: type the reason and press **Override**; the reason is in the booking''s history.
7. **Make the agreements again** checks both against the booking at once (they also follow every change by themselves).
8. **Edit the wording** (Admin only) changes CarmaCars'' agreement text for this booking: press **Change** beside a clause, edit its text, say why and press **Save the wording**; **Add** writes Additional terms at the end of Part 2. Only clauses not required by law or the insurer can be removed; the consents are fixed, and Blind Spot''s form (the insurer''s official form) is never changed. Before the renter signs, the agreement is made again; after, the change is a new version they sign, and **Every version** shows each clause before and after.

## Signing that holds up in a dispute

Every signature on the site is made the same way: rental agreements, amendments and new versions (remotely or on your device), and the owner agreements, schedules and forms, a co-owner''s link, the partner, investment and staff agreements.

1. The licence on file is shown. A 6-digit code to their phone or email on file is optional: the signer may press **Verify by code (optional)**, and Program settings, E-signing, **ask for a one-time code** makes it a required first step again (off by default). Without the code, the certificate says the identity was not confirmed by a code.
2. They say they read the documents, initial the key terms (each initials box is saved with **Save initials**; **Clear** takes it back to initial again) (damage and the deductible, the deposit and later charges, fuel, kilometres and late returns, their coverage, cancellation), give three consents (to sign electronically, to receive records electronically, to card charges under the agreement) and draw their signature.
3. Owners, partners, investors and staff do the same for their documents: the code, the reading, the key terms of their documents initialled (for example the Enrollment Agreement''s three confirmations, Form C''s acknowledgments, Schedule C, the staff agreement''s confidentiality), two consents and the drawn signature. Form C''s witness still types their name beside the owner.
4. Each step is recorded with its time, IP address and device, and the place when the device shares it. The signed PDFs end with a certificate of completion; anyone can check a signed file at `carmacars.ca/verify`.
5. Typed names are off. For a signer who cannot draw, an Admin can turn on the accessibility fallback: **Settings** > **Program**, Esign typed fallback.

## Card disputes: the evidence pack

Everything that proves the rental, in one PDF for Stripe.

1. When a card payment is disputed, the evidence pack is built by itself: the signed agreements with their certificates, the check-in and check-out reports with photos, kilometres and fuel, the licence, the payments and charges, every message to the renter, and the card checks from Stripe. It is staged in Stripe as the dispute''s evidence, and To do gets an urgent task.
2. Open the booking: the Rental agreements card shows the pack. Press **Download** to check it, then **Submit to Stripe** before the evidence date.
3. **Build the dispute evidence pack** makes one at any time (an Admin or Finance).

## The licence before an offer is accepted

Front, back and a selfie, from the request on.

1. After sending a request the renter is asked for their licence. A licence already on file from an earlier booking is used again while it is valid after the return.
2. The offer cannot be accepted (by the renter, or by you on their word) and nothing is paid until the licence and its expiry date are on file.
3. Review the images as usual with **Review documents**: the card Renter documents is on Review and offer too.
4. The switch is in **Settings** > **Program**, Booking requests and offers: Booking licence required (on), with the selfie (on).

## The licence reader

Every licence photo is read on upload: the back''s barcode first, else the vision model (within the day''s AI allowance).

1. The renter''s empty licence fields are filled from the read; the renter confirms them. A blurry or cut-off photo is taken again at once.
2. **Review documents** shows what was read and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos, valid to the return, class accepted, age at pickup, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back, and the main driver''s Ontario licence. Staff still approve.
3. **Settings** > **Program**, Driver''s licence reader: **Approve automatically when every check passes** (off). On: a driver whose front and back both read sharp and every check passes is approved in your name; anything flagged waits for a person.
4. **Primary driver must hold an Ontario licence** (on): a main driver with a licence from elsewhere becomes an additional driver, the booking needs "Primary driver: Ontario licence needed" and pickup is blocked. The renter adds a main driver, who signs on their own link. On the document review, **Admin: undo or let it go**: undo puts the first main driver back; let it go needs a reason.

> Tip: What was read is staff only and is deleted with the licence image. The licence number is never written to the logs.

## Renter documents: licence and proof of coverage

A renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage (OPCF 27 or a credit card''s rental coverage) are checked before the handover. You check them yourself; no task is needed.

1. A booking with documents waiting is a line on To do: "Check ''s documents for booking ", marked Now when the pickup is within two days. Press **Review documents**.
2. The pop-up shows each driver''s images and the coverage: the insurer, policy number and expiry, or the card, its type and whether the name matches.
3. What to check is written once at the top. One wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**: they are asked for a new one.
4. Then press **Approve all**: every image, the proof of coverage and the Protection Plan still waiting are approved in one step. The number in the button is exactly what it approves (an image whose file was removed is not counted), and an image not tied to a driver of the booking is listed under **Other documents**. Anything the system refuses is named with the reason.
5. The same pop-up is on the booking: the card Renter documents (**Review documents**) on Overview and on Drivers and documents.

> Tip: Each opening of a renter''s documents is logged. The links to the images last one minute. Field staff can also check a licence in person at the check-in (photos and four checks): the history says "checked in person". Field staff also review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from My jobs, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the reviewer''s role, field. Sales review the licence images (not the coverage) of any booking being arranged or under way from their To do or the booking, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the role, sales.

## Payments by day

**Money** > **Payments**, the **By day** tab: every payment and refund of a day or a range, by method, the cash drawer and the refunds waiting. Finance has the same screen.

1. Choose From and To and the methods (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer, bank transfer, pre-authorized debit, other), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method and for each day; cards read as the card and its last four digits, never a code.
3. The cash drawer: expected (cash in less cash given back) against the count Finance records with **Record the count**; a difference shows over or short.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere with the policy maths. **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the row, then **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** for the bookkeeper.

## Propose a change to a confirmed booking

The renter gets an email and answers on their booking. The calendar moves only when they accept.

1. Open the booking''s Changes tab. Under Propose a change, set the new pickup, return or car.
2. To price it by hand, type a New rental charge before tax. Leave it empty to use the car''s rates.
3. Write the Reason, for the renter. They read it.
4. Press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**.

![](/guides/img/admin-05-booking-changes-desktop-97008b21.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065?tab=changes; pins: 1 17.5 33.7, 2 9.2 50.0, 3 38.3 71.2, 4 12.9 91.9")

## Who a booking is credited to

Overview (and Review and offer) shows the Sales credit: the staff member the booking counts for in their sales.

1. A quote or a rental is credited to whoever created or added it. A request from the website is credited to whoever sent its first offer.
2. To give it to someone else, press **Reassign**, choose who (or Nobody), say whether they sourced the client and write the reason. The booking''s history and the audit log keep it, and the deal stays in the same week and month.
3. Sourced means the staff member chose I sourced this client when they entered it, it came with a field staff referral link, or you credited it. Only a sourced booking earns a staff commission. A website request earns none unless you credit someone.
4. Someone said they sourced a website request? The credit line shows the claim: press **Credit them** or **Not theirs**, with a reason.
5. A price typed by hand shows beside the rate-sheet price, with the reason. A price under the floor or past the discount limit is flagged: press **Mark reviewed** once you have looked at it.

> Good to know: A request keeps the lead-time adjustment of the moment it came in ("Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%"), through the offer and the payment. To change it, open the booking''s review screen, **More options**, **Lead-time pricing (%)**: a number (0 for none), or empty for the tier of the request. A price typed by hand replaces it.

> Good to know: The rental never goes below the car''s minimum daily rate or above its maximum (its price limits, set by the owner or on the car''s Rates tab), whatever the discount, promo code or lead-time pricing: a line "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car" brings it back. Only an Admin allows a price outside them: **More options**, **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)**, with the reason.

> Tip: The renter has 48 hours to accept (and sign the amendment) or decline, with one reminder. Any extra is charged to their Card on File; a lower price raises a refund for your approval.

## Review requests

Every renter is asked for a review by email and text, as they chose, only from 9 am to 9 pm Toronto time. Nothing needs setting up.

| Message | When |
| --- | --- |
| Mid-trip check | Rentals of 2 days or more, 24 hours after the pickup: "How is the car? Reply or call if anything is off." No review ask. |
| Review request | 1 hour after the check-out. It links the review page: the renter taps what they liked, adds a sentence, and gets a short draft to copy and post on Google. |
| Reminder | 24 hours after the request. |
| Final follow-up | 7 days after the request. Nothing more after it. |

1. The booking page has the card Review requests: each message with when it went or when it will go, and why it stopped.
2. **Ask for a review** sends the request now (or at 9 am if it is later than 9 pm), on any booking on a trip, returned or closed. Not twice in 24 hours.
3. On hold: a return or later charge (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls and tickets) is not settled or waived, or an incident or dispute is open. The request goes by itself once they are. Press **Send anyway** to send it now.
4. **Mark reviewed** stops the messages when the renter tells you they already reviewed.

The messages also stop by themselves when the renter presses "I already left a review", leaves a review on the site, unsubscribes, or a Google review is matched to them. **Bookings** > **Reviews** has the numbers (requests sent, on hold, reviews detected, the average rating), the hold list and the Google reviews to match.

> Tip: The draft is made only from what the renter picked and wrote, and from the booking (the car, how long, delivery or pickup). Everyone gets the Google link, whatever their stars; a renter who gives 3 stars or fewer also sees "Something wasn''t right? Tell us directly".

## What the owner sees, and owner deductions

Each booking on an owner''s or partner''s car shows the card What the owner sees at the top of its page.

1. **Hide from the owner** keeps the booking''s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.
2. **Show to the owner** shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.
3. Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder''s or the owner''s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.
4. Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings > Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking''s revenue (right away by default).
5. On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: **Add a booking expense** (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.
6. **Set the Revenue Share for this booking** applies within the car''s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. **Back to the car''s terms** undoes it.
7. Add a rental has the same under The car''s owner.

> Good to know: The owner''s statement carries each booking that counts toward the owner''s revenue, at its true amounts, and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. A booking billed to the renter always counts. Left out: a booking billed to an insurer and hidden from the owner (while Program settings keep only insurance replacements hidden), an insurer-billed rental that does not block the calendar, and a rental with "Counts toward the owner''s revenue" off. The booking page says when a booking is not part of the owner''s revenue and why. When a booking that was left out starts counting (Blocks the calendar turned on, shown to the owner, or billed to the renter), the owner gets the new booking email once, at that moment. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.

## Email the renter or the adjuster

Press **Email the renter** at the top of a booking, or open its **Messages & history** section.

1. Write a **Subject** and a **Message**, or pick a **Quick reply** to start from (Settings > Quick replies keeps them).
2. Press **Email the renter**. It goes from CarmaCars (bookings@carmacars.ca) and replies come back to the bookings inbox. The renter also sees it in their account and can answer there.
3. On a booking an insurer pays, choose **From**: CarmaCars, or Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance). **Email the adjuster** writes to the adjuster''s email on the booking (Insurance claim), always from Blind Spot Car Rental.

The **Messages & history** section is the booking''s Activity log (release 35): what you and the renter wrote, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes, events, payments, documents and visits, newest first, with a chip for each type and a search. The email form is under the log; each email you send shows in the log with your name.

> Good to know: Emails go out through the same daily limit as every email (the line under the form shows today''s use). A message to a renter goes before digests and marketing; past the limit it waits until midnight. To write to a renter from **People** > **Renters**, open the renter: Email the renter is at the bottom, about their latest booking or the one you pick.

### Record the pickup or the return now (details later)
When the car went out or came back but the checklist could not be done (no photos, no time, the renter dropped the keys), the booking''s **Check-in, check-out and signing** card has **Record the pickup now (details later)** on a confirmed booking and **Record the return now (details later)** while the car is on rent. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the odometer and fuel if you know them, and why. The booking moves on (on rent, or returned), late return charges follow the actual time, and Fleet gets the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. A car overdue or due back today also has **Returned**: on the To do list (Check-ins and check-outs today), on Bookings > Now and at the top of the booking page, which the late return alert opens. It asks only the return time (now, or earlier) and the km and fuel if you know them, and records the return the same way. Once returned, the statement can be issued and the deposit settled; releasing the deposit before the photos are in needs an Admin and a reason. A pickup without the deposit taken needs an Admin to waive it with a reason, and without the renter''s signature on the check-in report an Admin''s reason too. Later, **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings** opens the usual checklist (photos, readings, your signature): the task closes when it is saved.

The Agreement card says **Waiting for the renter''s details** when the renter still has blanks to fill (date of birth, address, mobile, licence, coverage): their account asks for them before signing and paying. No email or text is sent.

### Find a booking
**Bookings** has one search box: type the booking number (CC-1042, cc1042 or just 1042), the renter''s or a driver''s name, an email, a phone number in any format, a plate (spaces do not matter) or a car code, then press Enter. The status filters still apply to what is found.

### Record a card payment taken outside the site
A card taken in the Stripe Dashboard, or on a card reader, is recorded on the booking''s **Money** tab with **Record card payment**.

1. Choose what it paid: **Rental and fees**, **Rental**, **Fees**, **Later charges** or **Deposit hold**, and where it was taken.
2. Type the **Last 4 digits** and the amount. A Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard) is optional for a payment: press **Look up** and the amount and last 4 digits are checked against Stripe.
3. Press **Record it**. A payment confirms a booking waiting for payment, as any payment does.

> Good to know: A deposit hold needs its Stripe payment id, so it can be captured or released from **Settle the deposit**. It is recorded as held, with the usual release reminders. A hold on a reader lapses after 2 days, one made online after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise.

### Link a payment taken outside the platform
A charge or a card deposit taken in the Stripe Dashboard or through a Stripe payment link is linked to its booking by an Admin, on the booking''s **Money** tab: **Link a payment taken outside the platform**, in the rental panel or the deposit panel.

1. Paste the Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard). **Look up** shows what Stripe says: the amount, paid or a hold, and the card.
2. Press **Link as a rental payment** or **Link as the deposit**.

> Good to know: It must be in Canadian dollars and not already linked. A rental payment may not be more than is open for the rental and fees. A deposit must be the whole deposit: a hold waiting to be captured is kept as held (settle it as any hold), a charged deposit is kept as captured. **Money** > **Unlinked Stripe** lists, every night, the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, with a best guess of the booking.

### Charge or hold the deposit on the card reader
With the S700 paired (Settings > Card reader), the **Money** tab has **Charge on reader** (everything open, the rental, the fees or a later charge) and **Hold deposit on reader**. Press **Send to the reader**: the amount shows on the reader and the renter taps, inserts or swipes the card. The screen updates by itself; **Cancel** stops the reader and nothing is charged. A deposit hold is captured or released from Settle the deposit like any hold.

### Credit card coverage: the same card
When the renter''s coverage is their credit card, the whole rental (rental and fees) is paid on that same card. The Money tab says which card. Another card on the pay page is refused and refunded at once; on the reader it is refused before the money is taken; a payment by e-Transfer, cash or the like is refused; a card typed by hand needs its last 4 digits and the box **This is the same card**. Deposits and later charges can go on any card. If the renter truly has to use another card or method, press **Allow another card** and give the reason (an Admin).

## Booked as soon as the renter accepts (release 28)

A booking is booked the moment the renter approves the offer. It takes the car on every calendar, the fleet board, the car''s availability and the counts, even before the payment or the pickup is recorded. Payment and the handover show as their own badges: **Booked, payment due** and **Pickup not recorded**. The first renter to approve gets the car: any other open offer on the same car and dates goes back to Requests with a Re-offer To do.

- **Booked, payment due** To do: a booked rental still unpaid within 48 hours of its pickup. Send the pay link, charge the saved card or record the payment.
- Record the pickup To do: a pickup time that passed with nothing recorded, as before.

When you send an offer, **The offer as the renter sees it** sits right under **Send the offer**: check it before you press it.

## Changes after signing: an amended agreement, no new signature

The rental terms (section 15.4) let CarmaCars update a booking after signing: an extension, new dates or times, a price adjustment, a fee, a car swap. The signed agreement keeps applying. Each change makes a new version of the agreement marked **Amended** with the date, carrying the renter''s original signature, and the renter is sent it. Nobody is asked to sign again, except an additional driver who never signed (they sign before driving).

## Check-in and check-out on one screen

On the booking page, **Check in (pickup)** and **Check out (return)** are one screen: the time (now unless you change it), the odometer, the fuel, the photos and a note. Pick many photos at once from the camera roll or take them; tag an angle on any photo if you like. The suggested angles (front, each corner and side, rear, odometer, fuel gauge, interior front and rear, trunk, wheels, any damage) tick themselves as photos are tagged. Nothing is required but the time; the renter''s own photos are added to the same report, each marked with who took it (the renter or staff) and its angle. The one-screen checklist is the button above it.

## Type into the Blind Spot agreement

On the **Rental agreements** card, **Type into the Blind Spot agreement** shows each box as the form prints it. Change a value and **Save the corrections**: it is drawn in that box, and the insured vehicle, the claim number, the adjuster and missing km or fuel go back onto the booking. **Preview the filled form** opens it with your corrections.

## Reopen an expired offer (release 28)

An expired offer reopens in one click: **Reopen offer** on the booking or on the **Expired** filter of Requests. The renter gets the usual offer email and text; the offer stays open 24 hours unless you type other hours. When the pickup time has passed, the dialog asks for the new pickup and return first. A renter can also press **Ask to reopen this offer**: you get the To do "Renter wants expired offer reopened" and an alert, as for a new request.

An offer sent after its pickup time no longer expires by itself: it expires at its own expiry time (the pickup only counts when the offer was sent before it and the pickup is 2 hours past). The offer screens say **Pickup time has passed: update it** and do not send until you move the pickup.

## One booking page, six sections (release 31)

A booking has six sections: **Overview** (the next step; the review and offer while it is being arranged), **Money**, **Drivers & documents** (with the agreement), **Car & handovers** (the check-in and check-out, the photo report, signing on this device, what the owner sees), **Messages & history** (with the review request) and **Claims & extras** (changes, extensions, add-ons). Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance see the sections their work needs. An old link to a tab opens the section that holds it now.

Admin and staff open the same booking page, the same car page and the same listing review: you see every section and button, each staff function sees the parts it works with (Fleet has no Money section; only customer service and you have **Claims & extras**; refunds are asked for by you or Finance). A staff link to a booking opens the same page in the staff portal.

Every list has one search box (it finds names, numbers, plates, phones, emails and VINs) and one row of at most five chips. **Clear** removes every filter; the last one you used comes back next time on this device.

## Charge the renter after the return

Once the car is back, the Money tab has one action for everything owed after the trip: **Charge the renter**.

1. Press **Charge the renter**.
2. Choose the **Reason** from the list and add a note if it helps (Other needs its note). Enter the **Amount**.
3. Read the line under it: it says where the money comes from before anything moves. The deposit hold while it is still valid and covers the amount (the rest of the hold is released at the same time); otherwise the card on file; otherwise a pay link to the renter by text or email.
4. Press **Charge $...**. If the hold expired meanwhile, the card on file is charged instead, with the same amount and reason.

**Release** stays its own button. The renter''s receipt shows the reason.

## A deposit charged to a debit or prepaid card

When the deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card (Charge the card on file as the deposit), the renter also pays the **Card processing fee for a debit deposit** (Program settings, 2.9% and $0.30 by default): a separate, non-refundable amount on the same charge. The Money tab''s history and the receipt show it; the deposit refund returns the deposit only.

## What the renter sees still to do

While a booking waits to be signed and paid, the Next step quotes the renter''s own Sign and pay card, for example: The renter sees: "Two steps left: sign the rental agreement, then pay $...". Signed for an older version of the offer counts as not signed: the renter signs the updated agreement on their Sign and pay page.

## Override a pickup or a return that must go ahead (release 33)
Sometimes the trip has to start (or end) even though a check still stops it. On the booking page, a confirmed booking (or one waiting for payment) and a car on rent show **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) with each check in plain words: the deposit not taken, the rental agreement not signed, no renter signature on the check-in report, a licence or identity not verified, the coverage not confirmed, an additional driver who has not accepted, the payment still due, the calendar switch off, the car not marked available, maintenance overdue, the Ontario licence, the fleet insurance policy (when that rule is on in Program settings), the agreement''s claim details, the tracker; at a return, an odometer lower than at pickup.

1. Press **Override and record the pickup** (or the return).
2. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the km and fuel if you know them, and why the trip must go ahead. The reason is required.
3. Press the button. The pickup (or the return) is recorded at that time, only the checks listed are passed, for this booking and this once. The booking''s history and the audit log say who, when, why and which checks; every Admin gets the alert Override used. A payment still due is not waived: the booking is confirmed with the balance open, and the deposit is still to collect (it is not waived). The photos and readings come later, as with Record now.

When staff (Fleet, customer service, Sales, field staff) need it, they press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return) on the same card with the time they recorded. You get the alert Override asked for and a line on the To do: press **Approve** (one tap) and it is recorded with the time they entered, or **Decline** with a note. The request also shows on the booking page, with Approve and Decline.

## Record a past trip (release 33)
A trip that happened but was never recorded (the pickup and the return both passed): on the booking page press **Record a past trip**. Give the actual pickup and return times, the km and fuel at each if you know them, and the reason. Every check that would stop it is overridden as above, in one step: the booking lands in **Returned**, the late return charges follow the actual return time, and the deposit can be settled. The car''s status today is left as it is, and the renter is not sent a "your rental started" email for a trip long over. Fleet gets the task to add the photos and readings. Staff ask for it the same way; you approve in one tap.

## Book it now: an offer that is a booking at once (release 33)
When you send an offer (answering a request, or **Send an offer** without one), tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** above Send. The offer becomes the approved version at once: the booking waits for payment, the car is held for its dates as for any approved offer, and the renter gets one link to the **Sign and pay** page to sign and pay (the "approve your offer" email is not sent). To have them sign and pay with you, open the booking: **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device. When customer service or Sales tick it, the offer goes out and you get the alert Override asked for and a To do line: **Approve** in one tap books it the same way. The booking''s history says who booked it and that the renter did not approve it.

Already sent the offer? Tell Claude or the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the renter agreed by phone". Claude''s connector has the tool **Book an offer now**, and **Send an offer** and **Make an offer** take Book it now too; the assistant (Assistant at the top of the menu) takes it in the same sentence as the offer. Each is two steps: you see what will change (nothing is changed yet), then you confirm, and the booking waits for the renter to sign and pay as above. As an Admin it is done at once; when customer service or Sales ask the assistant, it waits for your one-tap Approve.

## A request replaced by a newer one
When a request or offer expired and the renter made a newer one for the same car and dates, the old one is hidden from Requests and keeps its number and history. Both booking pages say so under the title: **Replaced by #CC-10483** on the old one and **Replaces #CC-10482** on the new one, each a link to the other. Customer service, Sales and the other staff pages show the same note.

## Change protection (release 41)

How damage to the car is covered is one control on the booking page: the **Protection** card at the top (Overview and the Money tab). An Admin, customer service and fleet use it on any booking; sales on a request or an offer.

1. Press **Change protection**. A small window lists the three options: **Own insurance (OPCF 27)**, **Credit card coverage** and **Protection Plan**, each with the price difference (the plan shows its price a day times the days, plus HST), the deposit (no coverage rule changes it) and what the renter provides.
2. The rule is the same as on the renter''s page: credit card coverage needs the renter''s card picked from the coverage list, a card that covers this car, and the renter''s confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs the renter''s confirmation that they upload their policy; otherwise the Protection Plan. An Admin can tick Admin override: the reason is recorded on the change and in the booking history.
3. Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press **Change protection**.

What happens: the booking is repriced at once. More to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab; less, when the plan was paid, is a refund for an Admin to approve. No money moves by itself. An offer is sent again as a new version; a confirmed booking or a rental in progress gets the amended agreement (the renter signs the new version when the rules ask) and one email. Proof tasks follow the new option. Changes are refused after damage is reported on the booking.

A renter''s request to leave the Protection Plan shows on the same card with their proof (**Open the proof**). Customer service or an Admin presses **Approve** (the change is made and the coverage confirmed) or **Decline** with a note the renter reads. The task "The renter asks to leave the Protection Plan" opens the booking.

## Change the car before pickup

On a request, an offer or a confirmed booking that is not picked up yet, press **Change the car** at the top of the booking.

1. Choose the new car. Only cars free for the whole booking are listed, each with its new total and the difference.
2. Say why the car changes, then press **Change the car**.
3. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet (its rates, the km included and the rate per km). The coverage, the drivers and the add-ons stay as they are.
4. An offer is sent again with the new car: that offer is the renter''s one email.
5. On a confirmed booking, more to pay is left open: the renter sees **Pay the balance** on their booking, or you send a pay link or charge the saved card from Money. Less to pay becomes a refund that waits for approval, with a To do for Finance. The renter gets one email, **Booking updated**, with the new car and the money.
6. The open handover and return jobs move to the new car. The agreement gets a new version for the renter to sign; its link goes by text.
7. The booking''s history and the audit log keep who changed it, from which car, to which car and why.

Customer service and Admins change any of them; Sales changes a request or an offer; Fleet changes a confirmed booking. Once the car is out, use **Swap vehicle** instead.

## The accident card of a booking

Every booking from confirmation to the return shows its **Accident card**: the steps after an accident and the coverage this booking uses.

- OPCF 27: the renter''s own insurer and policy number, from the proof they uploaded.
- Credit card coverage: the card and its coverage provider, from their proof.
- Protection Plan: the provider, the policy number and the claims phone from Settings > Program (Tolls and damage), with the renter''s plan reference.

Press **Print the card** for the printable card. The renter has the same card on their booking. It never shows the fleet policy.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Bookings** shows a banner when trips have ended and are not closed; **Close ended trips** lists each one: never picked up in the system, on rent after the return, or returned and never closed. Fleet and Finance have the same page.

1. Tick one or several, then **Mark them**: returned on time, returned late (give the time it came back), or a no-show (an Admin or customer service).
2. Choose the deposit: **Deduct the balance owed**, **Deduct the late fee**, or **Release in full**. A card hold that has expired is marked settled at once (released by expiry: no money moves).
3. If no deposit was taken, an Admin fills **Admin: deposit not taken, waive it because** (the same field is in Record a past trip).
4. Nothing is released by itself: the decision waits under **Deposit decisions waiting for an Admin**, and an Admin presses **Release** (or **Release now (tolls window)**).

## Return charges

A late return is charged per started extra day at the booking''s full daily cost (the rental per day after discounts, plus per-day and per-trip fees such as the Protection Plan, never delivery), and only the started hours after the whole days get the hourly late fee. On the booking''s **Money** tab, each renter line not on a statement yet has **Change amount** (lower) and **Waive**, with the reason; it is in the booking history and the next assessment keeps it. An expired card hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## Switching a booking to the Protection Plan (release 43)

**Change protection** > **Protection Plan** uses the car''s own plan price, the same amount the window quotes. It is no longer refused when Fees has no flat Protection Plan amount.

## The Protection Plan priced from RentalCover (release 35)

The Protection Plan stays our product: renters never see the RentalCover name. Without the RentalCover partner key it is priced from the Protection Plan table, as before. Once the key is set, its price comes from a real RentalCover quote for the renter (their dates, their age at pickup, their name and email) plus our markup (20% unless **Settings** > **Program** changes it). The request form asks for the quote once the renter''s details are in, and an offer as you choose option 3; a quote is reused for 15 minutes. A price you type for the plan wins. If RentalCover does not answer, the table price applies.

RentalCover covers up to $50,000 an incident, so the plan is offered only for a car worth less. The value used: your override under **Value for the Protection Plan** on the car''s page when set, else the car''s Canadian Black Book value, else an AI estimate from typical listing prices that the site makes by itself (**Refresh the AI estimate** asks again). A car with no value counts as over the limit: the request form, the offer screen and the database then offer only OPCF 27 or credit card coverage.

## Extensions at the all-in price a day (release 35)

An extension costs what the renter already pays, averaged per day: the booking''s total for the booked period (the rental after discounts, every fee, one-time fees like delivery included, and HST) divided by its days, for each added day. A booking of $729.36 for 7 days costs $104.19 for each added day. Added hours under a day cost the hourly late fee with HST, never more than a day. There is no extension discount.

| Where | What happens |
| --- | --- |
| The renter''s **Extend** page | Each option shows the total and the price a day before paying |
| **Edit** on a confirmed or on-trip booking, made longer | The booking''s new total is the all-in price of the longer stay; the per-trip fees stay as booked and the rental charge takes the difference |
| The next period of a long rental | Keeps the rate of the booked period (the rental a day, per-trip fees scaled) |
| An insurer-billed booking | Priced as before |

The extension is one line on the booking, "Extension: 3 days at $104.19/day (all-in)", HST included. Its HST is the booking''s own share of HST, so invoices and the books never add HST on top. Type a rental charge in **Edit** to set another price. Late returns are unchanged: the daily cost of each extra day and the hourly late fee.

## A fixed amount per payment (release 35)

On a weekly, every 2 weeks or monthly plan, an Admin can set **Fixed amount per payment** in **Change the plan**. Each payment is that amount and the last one takes the remainder. The total and the payments already made never change. Leave it empty to split the payments by the days again.

## The request as sent and every offer (release 35)

On a request or a booking, **Original request, as the renter sent it** shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. **Offer history** lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.

1. To go back to an old version, press **Revert to this offer** on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.
2. Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.

The **Coverage** line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.

## Send an offer in three steps (release 35)

1. **Car and dates**: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.
2. **Price**: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout''s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.
3. **Review and send**: what changed, the message and how the link goes.

Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under **More options**. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.

## The owner''s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)

- **Owner''s own trip ($0)**: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.
- **Instant (repeat renter)**: a Gold renter or above (Rewards, release 40) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter''s instant booking away from the booking page.
- **Any car, any time** (release 40): a Platinum renter asked for dates the car shows as taken. Fleet gets an urgent task due within 4 hours: confirm it, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter''s confirmed booking for it. The task closes when the request is answered.
- **Book it now** pressed by staff waits for an Admin''s one-tap approval.

## Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)

The booking shows the renter''s **Secondary contact** when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes **rideshare documents** (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.

## Offers, coverage, delivery and fuel (releases 35 and 36)

- Sending an offer is three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every request shows the renter''s original request as sent and every offer version, with who sent it and when; reverting loads an old version as a new offer to send.
- Instant booking: a verified Gold renter or above books an available car at once, signs and pays; the booking is marked Instant (repeat renter), and an Admin can take instant booking away from a renter.
- Card coverage is checked against the car: the card, the car''s value, its type and the rental length. A card that does not cover it cannot be approved. OPCF 27 needs both the pink slip and the endorsement page.
- Delivery is priced by distance from the company''s address (1570 Midland Ave, Scarborough): a base, the kilometres included and a rate per km, all in Program settings; a car''s own fee stays as an override.
- The fuel line at the return is suggested from the car''s tank, the weekly pump price and a multiplier, plus the refuelling fee, and checked on the deposit review before any charge.
- Owner price limits: the daily minimum and maximum of a car or an owner hold every price, discount and offer; only an Admin can allow one request outside them, with a reason.
- Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking page (rental agreement copy, coverage letter, vehicle letter); staff get an alert when they are made. The secondary contact shows on the booking.
- Mid-trip review ask: halfway through a trip of several days, the renter gets one short message asking how it is going; a problem they report becomes a To do for customer service.
- A car that has only test bookings can be deleted by an Admin; the test bookings go with it. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

On **Close ended trips**, marking a trip returned late and choosing **Deduct the late fee** is the same choice of the late return fee, made there. The other deposit choices leave the late return to be chosen on the booking.', 'Requests, offers and bookings', 'See what is out, coming back and owed now; send an offer with or without a request, change it in place, take payments by part, run a booking.',
  'A booking starts as a request from the website, or as an offer you send yourself to a customer on the phone. You check it, adjust it and send the offer; an offer that is out is changed in place. After that, the booking page holds the money, documents, changes and history.

## Bookings now: what is out, coming back and owed

Open **Bookings**. It opens on **Now**, one screen that refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. Every time is Toronto time.

1. The numbers at the top: cars out now, due back today, overdue, going out in the next 72 hours, payments due in the next 7 days (with the total) and free cars. Tap one to jump to its list.
2. **Out now**: every car on rent, overdue returns first in red. Each shows the car (photo, code, plate), the renter with **Call** and **Text**, when it was picked up, when it is due back with a countdown, the payment plan and the next payment, the deposit held, and the km and fuel at pickup. Filter by Overdue, Due today or Payment due.
3. A confirmed booking whose pickup time has passed with no check-in recorded is listed as out, with **Out (pickup not recorded)**. The car most likely left. Press **Mark picked up**: it records the pickup at the booked time (change it if the car left at another time), the booking goes on rent, and Fleet gets a task to add the photos, km and fuel. The usual checks stay: the deposit taken (or an Admin waives it with the reason), the renter''s signature (or an Admin''s reason), the agreement''s details, every driver verified and the coverage confirmed. If one is missing, the reason is shown.
4. **Coming back**: overdue, today and tomorrow, by the time each is due.
5. **Going out**: confirmed pickups in the next 72 hours, delivery or pickup, with ticks and crosses for the licence, the signed agreement, the payment, the deposit (a clock until the morning of the pickup day, when the hold is placed on the card on file) and the check-in photos (done at the handover).
6. **Money due**: every rental payment due in the next 7 days or overdue, the amount, the plan and which payment it is (for example 3 of 4).
7. **Free now**: cars available and not out, the longest idle first, with the next pickup; then the cars in maintenance or cleaning. Partners'' cars are counted apart.

> Good to know: Placeholder bookings never show on Now.

### Payment plans

A rental is paid in full at pickup, weekly, every 2 weeks, or monthly. A rental longer than one period (30 days) pays each period by itself. To change it, open the booking, then the **Payment plan** card on Overview or Money, and press **Change the plan**. Each payment is its share of the total by its days, due on the day it starts. An insurer-billed rental shows **Insurer billed** and is never in Money due unless the renter owes a part. Admins, customer service and finance change the plan; fleet sees it.

## All bookings

The **All bookings** tab of Bookings has the search (booking number, name, email, phone, plate or car code), the status (All, Out now, Booked, Returned, Cancelled; closed bookings are found with the search, which also finds the insurer). **Out now** shows the bookings on rent and those whose pickup passed without a check-in, together. Each booking is one row: its number and status in plain words, the car with its photo, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the dates, the money (paid up, to pay, overdue, insurer billed) and Bill to.

## The request queue

Open **Bookings** > **Requests and offers**. The oldest waiting request is at the top.

1. The numbers at the top: waiting for an offer, past the reply target (red), offers out, accepted but not paid, and offers expired. Each one is a filter: press it and the list shows just those, with the matching chip below marked as chosen.
2. One queue, the most urgent first: the longest wait, then offers accepted but not paid, then offers out by when they expire. Each row has the car with its photo, the dates, the price, the renter with **Call** and **Text**, the licence (verified, to review, or not uploaded yet), who is answering it, and one button: **Send offer**, **Follow up** or **Open**. **Decline** sits beside **Send offer**.
3. Waiting shows how long the renter has waited ("12 min", "3 h", "2 days"); red means past the first reply target (5 minutes, set in Program settings). **Promise** counts down the 2 hours the site promises the renter.
4. Filter by Active, New, Changes asked, Offer out, Accepted, not paid or Expired. The list remembers your last choice on that device; **Active** always shows the whole queue and replaces what it remembered. When the same renter asks for the same car for overlapping dates again and the earlier request or offer expired, only the newest is listed: the older ones are linked to it and leave Requests (they keep their history). An expired offer leaves the active queue 48 hours after it expired, or once its pickup time passed; Expired lists the ones from the last 7 days. After 7 days an expired offer leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead, once, in People > Renters > Leads (Expired offers), with the car and the dates the renter wanted and a To do for Sales to win them back. An offer still out when its pickup time passes expires by itself.

![](/guides/img/admin-02-requests-desktop-6521282d.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/requests; pins: 1 38.9 29.9, 2 22.2 43.3")

> Good to know: A request whose pickup time passes without an offer expires by itself, with a note in its history. The renter is not emailed unless "Email the renter when their request expires that way" is on in Program settings.

## Answer a request with an offer

1. The Review and offer tab shows the request as the renter sent it.
2. Adjust the car, the dates, the rate type, the places, the rates (under **Show rate card**) and fees, the deposit and extras. A place changed away from a delivery or a collection takes its fee box and its fee with it.
3. Price on the right updates as you change things.
4. Add a message, choose how long the offer stays open, then press **Send the offer**.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-353f3707.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 1550; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 1 5.0 6.5, 2 7.5 45.8, 3 74.2 42.6, 4 76.7 98.1")

5. Changed fields but not ready to send? Press **Save changes**. The panel "The offer as the renter sees it" shows the result.
6. Can''t do it? Press **Decline** and fill in Reason and any alternative.
7. Need an answer first? Press **Ask the renter** to send a question.

![](/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-4dd4ed06.jpg "desktop; size: 500 80; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review; pins: 6 41.2 52.5, 7 18.0 52.5")

Opening a request takes it for you: everyone else sees "Being answered by" your name and since when, with Send the offer and Decline off, until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work; Program settings). Press **Take over** to answer one someone else holds; it is noted in the history. A second answer is refused with who answered and when. A request from the website opens to Sales after 15 minutes (Program settings); until then Admins, customer service and fleet answer it.

## Send an offer without a request

Press **Send an offer** at the top of Bookings, or **Send an offer without a request** on Requests and offers. For a customer on the phone, by text or at the counter: no request needed.

The screen is seven short steps, each with one line saying what to do, and the price beside it (on a phone the total sits at the bottom of the screen: press **See every line**). What most offers never need is under each step''s **More options**, which stays open while something in it is used.

1. **Who is renting and when**: find the renter by name, phone or email, or press **Not on file? Add a new customer** (full legal name, mobile, email for the offer link, date of birth). A customer already on file with the same email or phone is shown with Use: one person, one record. A renter picked from the file shows what is on their record under their name: the licence (class, number, expiry), the home address and the drivers named before, with a licence that has expired or an address over a year old flagged to ask them about. Then the pickup and the return.
2. **Which car**: search by car code, plate or name; each car says Free or Not free for the dates. More options: the rate card and the type and free-only filters.
3. **Where they pick up and return**: at our location, we deliver or collect (the address and distance), an airport or the owner''s location. The fee each one makes shows under it, Automatic or Set by hand.
4. **How damage is covered**: the renter''s own insurance, a credit card or the Protection Plan. More options: another Protection Plan price.
5. **Extras**: add-ons, when the car has any.
6. **The price**: the rate sheet price is filled in. More options: another price (a total for the trip or a rate a day, with why), Amounts I type (before or after HST), the total the renter pays, kilometres, a promo code, the deposit and a discount (an Admin), and **Fees**: press **Change** to set one by hand, **Reset to automatic** to undo it. Below: how it is paid (card online and a card hold unless you change it under More options).
7. **Send it**: who found this client (sales and customer service), a message, and Text or Email. More options: how long the offer is open, the owner''s view, who found the client (an Admin) and the internal note. Above the button, **Ready to send** or **Missing:** with what is left; press Send and each missing field says what it needs. Press **Send the offer to** the renter, or **Save without sending** to keep it as a request for later. **The offer as the renter sees it** is under the price.

> Good to know: Choices drive the charges. Take off a delivery, a collection, the Protection Plan or an add-on and its fee goes with it, even a fee set by hand: there is nothing to remove in a second place. Choose it again and the fee starts from the automatic amount.

> Good to know: It makes the same request and offer the website makes: the renter approves, signs and pays (or you record the payment), and only then is the car on the calendar. No "request received" email goes to the renter for an offer you send. Staff commissions and statements count it like any other booking.

## Change an offer that is out

The renter has the offer (Offered), or approved it and has not paid (Signing and payment). Open **More actions** on the booking and press **Edit the offer**.

1. Change anything: the car, the dates, the places, the price, fees, the deposit, add-ons, how it is paid. Each changed field is highlighted and the before and after are listed. Amounts I type (Before tax or After tax) and the Total the renter pays (after tax) work as on Send an offer.
2. Write what changed in Message to the renter and choose how long the offer is open.
3. Press **Save and send the update**: the renter gets the new version by email or text (ticked), and the old version no longer counts. Or press **Save without telling the renter** and tell them yourself.
4. A confirmed booking is changed with **Change the booking** (Propose a change, below).

> Tip: No need to withdraw first. **Withdraw the offer** is only for taking it back for good; **Send again, later expiry** gives the renter more time, and **Renter approved by phone** records a yes given on a call.

## Edit a booking that has started

On a confirmed, on-trip or returned booking (an Admin: a closed one too), Overview, **Edit the booking**, **Edit**.

1. Change the pickup or the return (extend or shorten: the rental charge is worked out again at this booking''s rates), the car (on trip: the car it leaves goes to Out of service for Fleet to check), the rental charge for the trip, each fee, the kilometres a day, the deposit (an Admin) and the note.
2. Type why, if you like, and tick **Email the renter what changed**, or leave it off for a silent correction. Press **Save the changes**.
3. What is open now shows at once: **Email a pay link** or **Text a pay link** for exactly that amount, **Charge** the saved card (the renter agreed), or record cash or an e-Transfer on the Money tab.

> Good to know: Each edit is kept with who, when, why, before and after (Edits, under the form) and in the booking''s history. A closed booking''s owner split and the staff commission follow. To have the renter accept and sign first, use Propose a change instead.

## Restore a version of a confirmed booking

Once a confirmed booking has been changed, Overview shows **Versions of this booking**: the booking before its first change, then one version after each change (a fee changed on its own too), the newest marked current.

1. Find the version to go back to (its dates, days, car, rental charge and total are listed) and press **Restore this version**.
2. The preview shows what changes: the dates, the car, the rental charge, the total, and what the renter would owe or be owed. Nothing is changed yet.
3. Type why, tick **Tell the renter what changed** if they should know, and press **Restore version** with its number. The dates, the car, the rental charge and every fee go back exactly as they were in that version.
4. It is one more change in the history, with your name and the reason. Payments are never touched: a difference is a balance to collect or a credit to settle, as with any edit.

> Good to know: The same checks as Edit: the car must be free for those dates, and customer service and Sales restore only while Program settings let staff change bookings (and fees). A version kept before Release 45 has no fees with it: its dates, car and rental charge go back and the fees stay as they are; the preview says so.

## Fees, a forgotten fee and the balance

On the booking''s Money tab, Fees lists each fee. Press **Change or add a fee**.

1. Type a new amount (for the whole trip, before HST) beside any fee, or choose one not on the booking (the young driver fee shows its price for these dates), or add a charge of its own with or without HST.
2. Press **Save the fees**. The balance shows by part (rental, fees) with the pay link, the saved card and Record a payment beside it.
3. The renter sees the balance on their booking with a Pay button, and pays by card on Stripe''s form.

> Good to know: Every change is recorded (Changes to the fees): the amount before and after, who and why. Customer service and sales may change fees while Program settings, Staff may change fees, is on.

> Good to know: Changing the amount of a line on the Money tab changes the booking''s total and balance with it, so no balance appears that nobody owes. An Admin can set the total directly with **Change the total**: the difference goes on the rental charge.

## A renter with only a debit or prepaid card

A credit card is required by default: the deposit must be on a credit card so the deductible can be charged. The pay page tells a renter with only a debit or prepaid card to contact us.

1. On the booking''s Money tab, press **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** and type the reason. Who and when are kept, and the change is in the booking''s history.
2. The booking''s pay page, staff pay links and deposit hold then take a debit or prepaid card, and the renter is told the hold lowers the money available on the card until it is released, which can take several business days.
3. **Require a credit card again** turns it off.

The Money tab shows each card used and its type (credit, debit, prepaid). A booking on credit card rental coverage is always paid on the credit card that carries the coverage, and cannot be allowed. Program settings, **Card types accepted**, can open debit and prepaid cards to every booking.

## Correct a renter''s details

On the renter''s page (People, Renters) or on any of their bookings, **Edit renter**.

1. Correct the name, email, phone, date of birth, licence, home address (start typing to find it) or the staff note.
2. A new email also becomes their sign-in at once (no confirmation needed for a typo you correct); tick **Email the renter a link to set a password** to send one there. Unsigned agreements and offers go to the new address.
3. Press **Save the renter**. An email that another renter has is refused with their name; the same phone is a warning.
4. The same person entered twice? Possible duplicates (same email, same phone, or same name and date of birth) shows under the renter. **Merge into this record** moves the other record''s bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages here and fills any detail missing here; the other record stays, blocked, with the merge in both histories.

## The Money tab: Rental charges and Security deposit

The booking''s Money tab opens on a strip with the three numbers that matter: **Rental due**, **Deposit** (one word: Not collected, Held, Charged, Released or Partly kept) and **Total paid**. Below are two panels, side by side on a computer and one above the other on a phone. Collecting one never touches the other, and every receipt says which one it is.

**Rental charges**: each line of the price and the total, Paid, then Balance due.

1. The one main button, Collect (the amount) rental: choose how. **The card on file** charges it now (Finance or an Admin); **A payment link by text** or **A payment link by email** sends the renter Stripe''s secure form; **On this device: hand it to the renter** opens it for the renter to type; **Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)** records money received (an e-Transfer, cheque or transfer needs its reference). For: the rental and fees together by default, or one of them. With the card on file, the rental and fees together are one charge with one receipt that lists both (the rental is paid first, then the fees; an insurer''s part and money already received another way are left out). The renter gets a receipt; **Print** prints one to hand over.
2. **A later charge** (before the return): on the card on file, by a link, on this device, or recorded. Choose the **Reason** from the list (Mileage overage, Fuel, Cleaning, Smoking, Late return, Tolls, Tickets/fines, Damage, Missing items, Other) and add a note; Other needs its note. The renter''s receipt shows the reason.
3. **Save a card** saves the renter''s card without charging it. Card readers, the fees (**Change or add a fee**), failed card payments (**Paid another way**), payments received another way and **Refund** sit in this panel too. The history lists rental payments only.
4. An offer paid another way: once the renter approved and signed and the money is recorded, the booking is confirmed (or press **Confirm the booking**).

**Security deposit**: the amount, how it is taken (a credit card hold, a debit or prepaid card at the standard multiple, a charge, or cash), its status in one word and the next step.

1. Not collected: the one main button, Collect (the amount) deposit. **Hold on the card on file** places the hold now (Finance or an Admin); **A deposit hold link by text** or **A deposit hold link by email**, or **A hold on this device: hand it to the renter**; **Charge the card on file as the deposit** only when no hold can be placed; **Cash or e-Transfer (record it)**. The rental balance is not touched.
2. Before every pickup the deposit hold link is texted to the renter on its own: 24 hours before (at once when the pickup is sooner), for a confirmed booking whose deposit is a card hold with no hold yet. The panel says **Deposit link texted** and when it was opened. No mobile number, or the text not sent: a task **Deposit link not sent**. **Settings**, then Site settings, Deposit link by text: on or off, and the hours.
3. Held, while the car is out: **Release** (an Admin, with the reason), **Keep part (damage/fees)** with the amount and the reason from the list, or **Re-authorize the hold** on the saved card before it lapses (the panel shows when the hold expires). A job re-authorizes it by itself about 24 hours before it expires; if it cannot, Finance and the Admins get the alert **Deposit hold not re-authorized**.
4. **Hold expired**: a card hold lasts about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. Once it has expired, nothing can be kept from it: the panel says Hold expired, Keep and Release are hidden, and **Charge the card on file instead** opens the later charge with the amount and the reason filled in.
4. After the return: **Settle the deposit** (below).
5. **Waive the deposit** (an Admin, before it is taken), **Change the debit deposit**, and **Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking** sit in this panel. The history lists deposit payments only.
6. A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way after the return: Finance gets a task; press **Returned** with the reference or receipt number.

> Good to know: Statements, reconciliation and the deposit settlement read each payment with its method: a cash deposit is never refunded to a card.

## Settle the deposit

The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking''s Money tab, under Deposit, press **Settle the deposit**. Issue the Check-out statement first.

1. The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.
2. Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.
3. Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.
4. Damage: **Keep the whole deposit (damage)** turns what is left of the deposit into a damage charge, with what was damaged and the photos; the renter is told. **Bill damage** adds a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible (more goes through a claim): the deposit pays first, then the card on file.
5. Press **Settle**. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.

> Good to know: A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.

## A booking

Open **Bookings** > **Bookings**, then a booking number. Or type the number in the search box.

1. Tabs: Overview, Money, Changes, History, and Drivers and documents.
2. Overview shows the trip, the renter, what is still missing for the handover, and the price.
3. Open tasks for this booking, with the queue and the due time.
4. Top right: **Email the renter** and **More actions**, the menu with **Edit the offer**, **Stop blocking the calendar**, **Cancel for the renter**, **Cancel by CarmaCars** and the rest.
5. Under the booking number: **Next step**, what happens next and who does it, with one button for that step (for example **Send the offer**, **Sign on this device** or **Check in the car**); then where the booking is on its way, from Request to Closed, with the dates, the days, the total and who pays.

![](/guides/img/admin-04-booking-desktop-b56b668a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 960; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065; pins: 2 50.0 46.6, 4 85.4 14.5, 5 22.9 26.8")

## Check a car out or in

From the booking, with your phone or a tablet: the same checklist field staff use.

1. A confirmed booking shows **Check in (pickup)** under Check-in, check-out and signing; a booking on rent shows **Check out (return)**. Today lists the check-ins and check-outs due, each with **Check in** or **Check out**.
2. The checklist opens: the ready check, the renter and their licence and card, the odometer (km) and fuel or charge, the keys, the photo set (every side, the wheels, the interior, the odometer and fuel gauge, the plate), damage marks with close-ups, then the renter and you sign.
3. Photos wait on the device without a connection and upload in the background. Each keeps its time, and the place when the device allows location.
4. A field job of the booking is taken over (the history says so); with no job, one is made for you. When done, press **See the photo report**.

> Tip: Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in the same way from their own booking page.

## The photo report, late returns and the return charges

Under Check-in, check-out and signing, press **Photo report**.

1. The report shows the due-back time, the actual check-in and check-out, Late by (or Overdue by while the car is out), the odometer and kilometres over the allowance, the fuel or charge out and in, every photo with its time and place, and the damage.
2. At check-out the mileage overage and the fuel or recharging are written to the return charges at once. A late return (after the grace period of the fee defaults) is not: it waits for a choice on the booking (see "A late return is a choice"). The fuel is a suggested line: the car''s tank x the fuel missing x the pump price of its grade (Program settings, updated weekly) x 1.25, plus the refuelling fee; an electric car the battery kWh x the charge missing x the price a kWh, plus the fee. A pump receipt entered later replaces it. Fleet and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; it is never charged to a card by itself.
3. Not charging one? Press **Waive** beside it and give the reason: it stays waived if the charges are worked out again.
4. The time was wrong? Press **Correct the check-out time** (or the check-in time) with the reason: lateness follows, a return that is no longer late loses its late charge, and the history keeps both times.
5. The renter gets the same report (without these buttons) by email and in their Documents. Late by shows on the booking and in the Bookings list.

### The renter says the car is back

Every overdue email, text and alert (at the return time, at 15 minutes and the final notice) has a one-tap **I''ve returned the car** link, and the renter''s booking page has the button. The renter can add photos, the odometer, the fuel level and the time they returned it. Sending it stops every overdue notice of the booking at once, the booking shows **Returned, waiting for confirmation**, and Fleet gets an urgent To do: "The renter says the car is back".

1. Open the booking. The card **The renter says the car is back** shows what the renter gave, marked renter-provided, with their photos.
2. Check the car: the return place, the tracker, the photos.
3. Press **Confirm** to complete the trip. Correct the odometer, fuel or return time first if they are wrong: the late charges follow the time you confirm. The renter''s photos join the check-out report.
4. Or press **Deny** and say why. The renter gets your reason by email and text, and the overdue notices start again.

Checking the car in the usual way also completes the trip and stops the notices. Admins, Fleet, Sales, Customer service and field staff can Confirm or Deny.

## Signatures on the spot, or by link

The renter or an additional driver signs the rental agreement on your device, or on their own phone.

1. While a signature is missing, the booking shows **Sign now on this device**, **Email the signing link** and **Text the signing link**.
2. No agreement made yet (the renter has not saved their details at home)? **Sign now on this device** still shows: press **Prepare the agreement to sign now** and it is made on the spot.
3. **Sign now on this device**: confirm the name matches their licence and that you saw the original licence (photograph it if none is on file), then press **Hand the device to** and their name.
4. They read both agreements (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), tick the statements and sign. Then **Back to the staff view** for the next signer.
5. The record is the same as signing online, and says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your device. It is printed on the signed copy''s signature record page.

## Rental agreements: every version, every field

The booking''s Rental agreements card: the current version of CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s agreements, every earlier one, and what is still blank.

1. Once the agreement is signed and countersigned, any change to what it prints makes a new version of both documents by itself: the dates, the price lines, the car, a driver added or corrected, the coverage, the deposit or how it was paid, an address.
2. A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage option is signed again: the renter (and each driver it affects) gets their link by email and text, and the card shows "Agreement v3 waiting for signature". A correction (a typo in an address, a plate written differently) is filed without signing; the renter gets the corrected copy by email.
3. Check-in makes the "as picked up" copy (time out, km out, fuel out, the car''s plate and VIN, the check-in report), countersigned by whoever checked the car out; check-out makes the closing copy (time in, km in, driven and charged, fuel in, late hours, damage, the return charges, the final totals). Both go to the renter by email.
4. **Every version** lists each one with what changed and both PDFs. **Resend the signing links**, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your phone or tablet.
5. The card lists what the agreements still print blank (a licence expiry, the insurer''s policy number, the insured vehicle, a VIN). Type the values and press **Save the missing fields**: the agreements follow.
6. Check-in stops while a field a claim needs is blank. An Admin can let it go ahead: type the reason and press **Override**; the reason is in the booking''s history.
7. **Make the agreements again** checks both against the booking at once (they also follow every change by themselves).
8. **Edit the wording** (Admin only) changes CarmaCars'' agreement text for this booking: press **Change** beside a clause, edit its text, say why and press **Save the wording**; **Add** writes Additional terms at the end of Part 2. Only clauses not required by law or the insurer can be removed; the consents are fixed, and Blind Spot''s form (the insurer''s official form) is never changed. Before the renter signs, the agreement is made again; after, the change is a new version they sign, and **Every version** shows each clause before and after.

## Signing that holds up in a dispute

Every signature on the site is made the same way: rental agreements, amendments and new versions (remotely or on your device), and the owner agreements, schedules and forms, a co-owner''s link, the partner, investment and staff agreements.

1. The licence on file is shown. A 6-digit code to their phone or email on file is optional: the signer may press **Verify by code (optional)**, and Program settings, E-signing, **ask for a one-time code** makes it a required first step again (off by default). Without the code, the certificate says the identity was not confirmed by a code.
2. They say they read the documents, initial the key terms (each initials box is saved with **Save initials**; **Clear** takes it back to initial again) (damage and the deductible, the deposit and later charges, fuel, kilometres and late returns, their coverage, cancellation), give three consents (to sign electronically, to receive records electronically, to card charges under the agreement) and draw their signature.
3. Owners, partners, investors and staff do the same for their documents: the code, the reading, the key terms of their documents initialled (for example the Enrollment Agreement''s three confirmations, Form C''s acknowledgments, Schedule C, the staff agreement''s confidentiality), two consents and the drawn signature. Form C''s witness still types their name beside the owner.
4. Each step is recorded with its time, IP address and device, and the place when the device shares it. The signed PDFs end with a certificate of completion; anyone can check a signed file at `carmacars.ca/verify`.
5. Typed names are off. For a signer who cannot draw, an Admin can turn on the accessibility fallback: **Settings** > **Program**, Esign typed fallback.

## Card disputes: the evidence pack

Everything that proves the rental, in one PDF for Stripe.

1. When a card payment is disputed, the evidence pack is built by itself: the signed agreements with their certificates, the check-in and check-out reports with photos, kilometres and fuel, the licence, the payments and charges, every message to the renter, and the card checks from Stripe. It is staged in Stripe as the dispute''s evidence, and To do gets an urgent task.
2. Open the booking: the Rental agreements card shows the pack. Press **Download** to check it, then **Submit to Stripe** before the evidence date.
3. **Build the dispute evidence pack** makes one at any time (an Admin or Finance).

## The licence before an offer is accepted

Front, back and a selfie, from the request on.

1. After sending a request the renter is asked for their licence. A licence already on file from an earlier booking is used again while it is valid after the return.
2. The offer cannot be accepted (by the renter, or by you on their word) and nothing is paid until the licence and its expiry date are on file.
3. Review the images as usual with **Review documents**: the card Renter documents is on Review and offer too.
4. The switch is in **Settings** > **Program**, Booking requests and offers: Booking licence required (on), with the selfie (on).

## The licence reader

Every licence photo is read on upload: the back''s barcode first, else the vision model (within the day''s AI allowance).

1. The renter''s empty licence fields are filled from the read; the renter confirms them. A blurry or cut-off photo is taken again at once.
2. **Review documents** shows what was read and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos, valid to the return, class accepted, age at pickup, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back, and the main driver''s Ontario licence. Staff still approve.
3. **Settings** > **Program**, Driver''s licence reader: **Approve automatically when every check passes** (off). On: a driver whose front and back both read sharp and every check passes is approved in your name; anything flagged waits for a person.
4. **Primary driver must hold an Ontario licence** (on): a main driver with a licence from elsewhere becomes an additional driver, the booking needs "Primary driver: Ontario licence needed" and pickup is blocked. The renter adds a main driver, who signs on their own link. On the document review, **Admin: undo or let it go**: undo puts the first main driver back; let it go needs a reason.

> Tip: What was read is staff only and is deleted with the licence image. The licence number is never written to the logs.

## Renter documents: licence and proof of coverage

A renter''s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage (OPCF 27 or a credit card''s rental coverage) are checked before the handover. You check them yourself; no task is needed.

1. A booking with documents waiting is a line on To do: "Check ''s documents for booking ", marked Now when the pickup is within two days. Press **Review documents**.
2. The pop-up shows each driver''s images and the coverage: the insurer, policy number and expiry, or the card, its type and whether the name matches.
3. What to check is written once at the top. One wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**: they are asked for a new one.
4. Then press **Approve all**: every image, the proof of coverage and the Protection Plan still waiting are approved in one step. The number in the button is exactly what it approves (an image whose file was removed is not counted), and an image not tied to a driver of the booking is listed under **Other documents**. Anything the system refuses is named with the reason.
5. The same pop-up is on the booking: the card Renter documents (**Review documents**) on Overview and on Drivers and documents.

> Tip: Each opening of a renter''s documents is logged. The links to the images last one minute. Field staff can also check a licence in person at the check-in (photos and four checks): the history says "checked in person". Field staff also review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from My jobs, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the reviewer''s role, field. Sales review the licence images (not the coverage) of any booking being arranged or under way from their To do or the booking, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the role, sales.

## Payments by day

**Money** > **Payments**, the **By day** tab: every payment and refund of a day or a range, by method, the cash drawer and the refunds waiting. Finance has the same screen.

1. Choose From and To and the methods (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer, bank transfer, pre-authorized debit, other), then press **Show**.
2. Totals by method and for each day; cards read as the card and its last four digits, never a code.
3. The cash drawer: expected (cash in less cash given back) against the count Finance records with **Record the count**; a difference shows over or short.
4. Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere with the policy maths. **Approve** or **Decline** with the reason in the row, then **Issue the refund**.
5. **Export CSV** for the bookkeeper.

## Propose a change to a confirmed booking

The renter gets an email and answers on their booking. The calendar moves only when they accept.

1. Open the booking''s Changes tab. Under Propose a change, set the new pickup, return or car.
2. To price it by hand, type a New rental charge before tax. Leave it empty to use the car''s rates.
3. Write the Reason, for the renter. They read it.
4. Press **Preview the price**, then **Send to the renter**.

![](/guides/img/admin-05-booking-changes-desktop-97008b21.jpg "desktop; size: 1200 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065?tab=changes; pins: 1 17.5 33.7, 2 9.2 50.0, 3 38.3 71.2, 4 12.9 91.9")

## Who a booking is credited to

Overview (and Review and offer) shows the Sales credit: the staff member the booking counts for in their sales.

1. A quote or a rental is credited to whoever created or added it. A request from the website is credited to whoever sent its first offer.
2. To give it to someone else, press **Reassign**, choose who (or Nobody), say whether they sourced the client and write the reason. The booking''s history and the audit log keep it, and the deal stays in the same week and month.
3. Sourced means the staff member chose I sourced this client when they entered it, it came with a field staff referral link, or you credited it. Only a sourced booking earns a staff commission. A website request earns none unless you credit someone.
4. Someone said they sourced a website request? The credit line shows the claim: press **Credit them** or **Not theirs**, with a reason.
5. A price typed by hand shows beside the rate-sheet price, with the reason. A price under the floor or past the discount limit is flagged: press **Mark reviewed** once you have looked at it.

> Good to know: A request keeps the lead-time adjustment of the moment it came in ("Short-notice pricing +10%" or "Booked ahead −5%"), through the offer and the payment. To change it, open the booking''s review screen, **More options**, **Lead-time pricing (%)**: a number (0 for none), or empty for the tier of the request. A price typed by hand replaces it.

> Good to know: The rental never goes below the car''s minimum daily rate or above its maximum (its price limits, set by the owner or on the car''s Rates tab), whatever the discount, promo code or lead-time pricing: a line "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car" brings it back. Only an Admin allows a price outside them: **More options**, **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)**, with the reason.

> Tip: The renter has 48 hours to accept (and sign the amendment) or decline, with one reminder. Any extra is charged to their Card on File; a lower price raises a refund for your approval.

## Review requests

Every renter is asked for a review by email and text, as they chose, only from 9 am to 9 pm Toronto time. Nothing needs setting up.

| Message | When |
| --- | --- |
| Mid-trip check | Rentals of 2 days or more, 24 hours after the pickup: "How is the car? Reply or call if anything is off." No review ask. |
| Review request | 1 hour after the check-out. It links the review page: the renter taps what they liked, adds a sentence, and gets a short draft to copy and post on Google. |
| Reminder | 24 hours after the request. |
| Final follow-up | 7 days after the request. Nothing more after it. |

1. The booking page has the card Review requests: each message with when it went or when it will go, and why it stopped.
2. **Ask for a review** sends the request now (or at 9 am if it is later than 9 pm), on any booking on a trip, returned or closed. Not twice in 24 hours.
3. On hold: a return or later charge (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls and tickets) is not settled or waived, or an incident or dispute is open. The request goes by itself once they are. Press **Send anyway** to send it now.
4. **Mark reviewed** stops the messages when the renter tells you they already reviewed.

The messages also stop by themselves when the renter presses "I already left a review", leaves a review on the site, unsubscribes, or a Google review is matched to them. **Bookings** > **Reviews** has the numbers (requests sent, on hold, reviews detected, the average rating), the hold list and the Google reviews to match.

> Tip: The draft is made only from what the renter picked and wrote, and from the booking (the car, how long, delivery or pickup). Everyone gets the Google link, whatever their stars; a renter who gives 3 stars or fewer also sees "Something wasn''t right? Tell us directly".

## What the owner sees, and owner deductions

Each booking on an owner''s or partner''s car shows the card What the owner sees at the top of its page.

1. **Hide from the owner** keeps the booking''s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.
2. **Show to the owner** shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.
3. Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder''s or the owner''s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.
4. Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings > Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking''s revenue (right away by default).
5. On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: **Add a booking expense** (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.
6. **Set the Revenue Share for this booking** applies within the car''s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. **Back to the car''s terms** undoes it.
7. Add a rental has the same under The car''s owner.

> Good to know: The owner''s statement carries each booking that counts toward the owner''s revenue, at its true amounts, and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. A booking billed to the renter always counts. Left out: a booking billed to an insurer and hidden from the owner (while Program settings keep only insurance replacements hidden), an insurer-billed rental that does not block the calendar, and a rental with "Counts toward the owner''s revenue" off. The booking page says when a booking is not part of the owner''s revenue and why. When a booking that was left out starts counting (Blocks the calendar turned on, shown to the owner, or billed to the renter), the owner gets the new booking email once, at that moment. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.

## Email the renter or the adjuster

Press **Email the renter** at the top of a booking, or open its **Messages & history** section.

1. Write a **Subject** and a **Message**, or pick a **Quick reply** to start from (Settings > Quick replies keeps them).
2. Press **Email the renter**. It goes from CarmaCars (bookings@carmacars.ca) and replies come back to the bookings inbox. The renter also sees it in their account and can answer there.
3. On a booking an insurer pays, choose **From**: CarmaCars, or Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance). **Email the adjuster** writes to the adjuster''s email on the booking (Insurance claim), always from Blind Spot Car Rental.

The **Messages & history** section is the booking''s Activity log (release 35): what you and the renter wrote, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes, events, payments, documents and visits, newest first, with a chip for each type and a search. The email form is under the log; each email you send shows in the log with your name.

> Good to know: Emails go out through the same daily limit as every email (the line under the form shows today''s use). A message to a renter goes before digests and marketing; past the limit it waits until midnight. To write to a renter from **People** > **Renters**, open the renter: Email the renter is at the bottom, about their latest booking or the one you pick.

### Record the pickup or the return now (details later)
When the car went out or came back but the checklist could not be done (no photos, no time, the renter dropped the keys), the booking''s **Check-in, check-out and signing** card has **Record the pickup now (details later)** on a confirmed booking and **Record the return now (details later)** while the car is on rent. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the odometer and fuel if you know them, and why. The booking moves on (on rent, or returned), late return charges follow the actual time, and Fleet gets the task **Add the photos and readings for CC-...**. A car overdue or due back today also has **Returned**: on the To do list (Check-ins and check-outs today), on Bookings > Now and at the top of the booking page, which the late return alert opens. It asks only the return time (now, or earlier) and the km and fuel if you know them, and records the return the same way. Once returned, the statement can be issued and the deposit settled; releasing the deposit before the photos are in needs an Admin and a reason. A pickup without the deposit taken needs an Admin to waive it with a reason, and without the renter''s signature on the check-in report an Admin''s reason too. Later, **Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings** opens the usual checklist (photos, readings, your signature): the task closes when it is saved.

The Agreement card says **Waiting for the renter''s details** when the renter still has blanks to fill (date of birth, address, mobile, licence, coverage): their account asks for them before signing and paying. No email or text is sent.

### Find a booking
**Bookings** has one search box: type the booking number (CC-1042, cc1042 or just 1042), the renter''s or a driver''s name, an email, a phone number in any format, a plate (spaces do not matter) or a car code, then press Enter. The status filters still apply to what is found.

### Record a card payment taken outside the site
A card taken in the Stripe Dashboard, or on a card reader, is recorded on the booking''s **Money** tab with **Record card payment**.

1. Choose what it paid: **Rental and fees**, **Rental**, **Fees**, **Later charges** or **Deposit hold**, and where it was taken.
2. Type the **Last 4 digits** and the amount. A Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard) is optional for a payment: press **Look up** and the amount and last 4 digits are checked against Stripe.
3. Press **Record it**. A payment confirms a booking waiting for payment, as any payment does.

> Good to know: A deposit hold needs its Stripe payment id, so it can be captured or released from **Settle the deposit**. It is recorded as held, with the usual release reminders. A hold on a reader lapses after 2 days, one made online after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise.

### Link a payment taken outside the platform
A charge or a card deposit taken in the Stripe Dashboard or through a Stripe payment link is linked to its booking by an Admin, on the booking''s **Money** tab: **Link a payment taken outside the platform**, in the rental panel or the deposit panel.

1. Paste the Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard). **Look up** shows what Stripe says: the amount, paid or a hold, and the card.
2. Press **Link as a rental payment** or **Link as the deposit**.

> Good to know: It must be in Canadian dollars and not already linked. A rental payment may not be more than is open for the rental and fees. A deposit must be the whole deposit: a hold waiting to be captured is kept as held (settle it as any hold), a charged deposit is kept as captured. **Money** > **Unlinked Stripe** lists, every night, the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, with a best guess of the booking.

### Charge or hold the deposit on the card reader
With the S700 paired (Settings > Card reader), the **Money** tab has **Charge on reader** (everything open, the rental, the fees or a later charge) and **Hold deposit on reader**. Press **Send to the reader**: the amount shows on the reader and the renter taps, inserts or swipes the card. The screen updates by itself; **Cancel** stops the reader and nothing is charged. A deposit hold is captured or released from Settle the deposit like any hold.

### Credit card coverage: the same card
When the renter''s coverage is their credit card, the whole rental (rental and fees) is paid on that same card. The Money tab says which card. Another card on the pay page is refused and refunded at once; on the reader it is refused before the money is taken; a payment by e-Transfer, cash or the like is refused; a card typed by hand needs its last 4 digits and the box **This is the same card**. Deposits and later charges can go on any card. If the renter truly has to use another card or method, press **Allow another card** and give the reason (an Admin).

## Booked as soon as the renter accepts (release 28)

A booking is booked the moment the renter approves the offer. It takes the car on every calendar, the fleet board, the car''s availability and the counts, even before the payment or the pickup is recorded. Payment and the handover show as their own badges: **Booked, payment due** and **Pickup not recorded**. The first renter to approve gets the car: any other open offer on the same car and dates goes back to Requests with a Re-offer To do.

- **Booked, payment due** To do: a booked rental still unpaid within 48 hours of its pickup. Send the pay link, charge the saved card or record the payment.
- Record the pickup To do: a pickup time that passed with nothing recorded, as before.

When you send an offer, **The offer as the renter sees it** sits right under **Send the offer**: check it before you press it.

## Changes after signing: an amended agreement, no new signature

The rental terms (section 15.4) let CarmaCars update a booking after signing: an extension, new dates or times, a price adjustment, a fee, a car swap. The signed agreement keeps applying. Each change makes a new version of the agreement marked **Amended** with the date, carrying the renter''s original signature, and the renter is sent it. Nobody is asked to sign again, except an additional driver who never signed (they sign before driving).

## Check-in and check-out on one screen

On the booking page, **Check in (pickup)** and **Check out (return)** are one screen: the time (now unless you change it), the odometer, the fuel, the photos and a note. Pick many photos at once from the camera roll or take them; tag an angle on any photo if you like. The suggested angles (front, each corner and side, rear, odometer, fuel gauge, interior front and rear, trunk, wheels, any damage) tick themselves as photos are tagged. Nothing is required but the time; the renter''s own photos are added to the same report, each marked with who took it (the renter or staff) and its angle. The one-screen checklist is the button above it.

## Type into the Blind Spot agreement

On the **Rental agreements** card, **Type into the Blind Spot agreement** shows each box as the form prints it. Change a value and **Save the corrections**: it is drawn in that box, and the insured vehicle, the claim number, the adjuster and missing km or fuel go back onto the booking. **Preview the filled form** opens it with your corrections.

## Reopen an expired offer (release 28)

An expired offer reopens in one click: **Reopen offer** on the booking or on the **Expired** filter of Requests. The renter gets the usual offer email and text; the offer stays open 24 hours unless you type other hours. When the pickup time has passed, the dialog asks for the new pickup and return first. A renter can also press **Ask to reopen this offer**: you get the To do "Renter wants expired offer reopened" and an alert, as for a new request.

An offer sent after its pickup time no longer expires by itself: it expires at its own expiry time (the pickup only counts when the offer was sent before it and the pickup is 2 hours past). The offer screens say **Pickup time has passed: update it** and do not send until you move the pickup.

## One booking page, six sections (release 31)

A booking has six sections: **Overview** (the next step; the review and offer while it is being arranged), **Money**, **Drivers & documents** (with the agreement), **Car & handovers** (the check-in and check-out, the photo report, signing on this device, what the owner sees), **Messages & history** (with the review request) and **Claims & extras** (changes, extensions, add-ons). Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance see the sections their work needs. An old link to a tab opens the section that holds it now.

Admin and staff open the same booking page, the same car page and the same listing review: you see every section and button, each staff function sees the parts it works with (Fleet has no Money section; only customer service and you have **Claims & extras**; refunds are asked for by you or Finance). A staff link to a booking opens the same page in the staff portal.

Every list has one search box (it finds names, numbers, plates, phones, emails and VINs) and one row of at most five chips. **Clear** removes every filter; the last one you used comes back next time on this device.

## Charge the renter after the return

Once the car is back, the Money tab has one action for everything owed after the trip: **Charge the renter**.

1. Press **Charge the renter**.
2. Choose the **Reason** from the list and add a note if it helps (Other needs its note). Enter the **Amount**.
3. Read the line under it: it says where the money comes from before anything moves. The deposit hold while it is still valid and covers the amount (the rest of the hold is released at the same time); otherwise the card on file; otherwise a pay link to the renter by text or email.
4. Press **Charge $...**. If the hold expired meanwhile, the card on file is charged instead, with the same amount and reason.

**Release** stays its own button. The renter''s receipt shows the reason.

## A deposit charged to a debit or prepaid card

When the deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card (Charge the card on file as the deposit), the renter also pays the **Card processing fee for a debit deposit** (Program settings, 2.9% and $0.30 by default): a separate, non-refundable amount on the same charge. The Money tab''s history and the receipt show it; the deposit refund returns the deposit only.

## What the renter sees still to do

While a booking waits to be signed and paid, the Next step quotes the renter''s own Sign and pay card, for example: The renter sees: "Two steps left: sign the rental agreement, then pay $...". Signed for an older version of the offer counts as not signed: the renter signs the updated agreement on their Sign and pay page.

## Override a pickup or a return that must go ahead (release 33)
Sometimes the trip has to start (or end) even though a check still stops it. On the booking page, a confirmed booking (or one waiting for payment) and a car on rent show **What stops the pickup now** (or the return) with each check in plain words: the deposit not taken, the rental agreement not signed, no renter signature on the check-in report, a licence or identity not verified, the coverage not confirmed, an additional driver who has not accepted, the payment still due, the calendar switch off, the car not marked available, maintenance overdue, the Ontario licence, the fleet insurance policy (when that rule is on in Program settings), the agreement''s claim details, the tracker; at a return, an odometer lower than at pickup.

1. Press **Override and record the pickup** (or the return).
2. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the km and fuel if you know them, and why the trip must go ahead. The reason is required.
3. Press the button. The pickup (or the return) is recorded at that time, only the checks listed are passed, for this booking and this once. The booking''s history and the audit log say who, when, why and which checks; every Admin gets the alert Override used. A payment still due is not waived: the booking is confirmed with the balance open, and the deposit is still to collect (it is not waived). The photos and readings come later, as with Record now.

When staff (Fleet, customer service, Sales, field staff) need it, they press **Ask an Admin to override the pickup** (or the return) on the same card with the time they recorded. You get the alert Override asked for and a line on the To do: press **Approve** (one tap) and it is recorded with the time they entered, or **Decline** with a note. The request also shows on the booking page, with Approve and Decline.

## Record a past trip (release 33)
A trip that happened but was never recorded (the pickup and the return both passed): on the booking page press **Record a past trip**. Give the actual pickup and return times, the km and fuel at each if you know them, and the reason. Every check that would stop it is overridden as above, in one step: the booking lands in **Returned**, the late return charges follow the actual return time, and the deposit can be settled. The car''s status today is left as it is, and the renter is not sent a "your rental started" email for a trip long over. Fleet gets the task to add the photos and readings. Staff ask for it the same way; you approve in one tap.

## Book it now: an offer that is a booking at once (release 33)
When you send an offer (answering a request, or **Send an offer** without one), tick **Book it now (no renter approval)** above Send. The offer becomes the approved version at once: the booking waits for payment, the car is held for its dates as for any approved offer, and the renter gets one link to the **Sign and pay** page to sign and pay (the "approve your offer" email is not sent). To have them sign and pay with you, open the booking: **Sign now on this device**, then take the card on this device. When customer service or Sales tick it, the offer goes out and you get the alert Override asked for and a To do line: **Approve** in one tap books it the same way. The booking''s history says who booked it and that the renter did not approve it.

Already sent the offer? Tell Claude or the assistant: "Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the renter agreed by phone". Claude''s connector has the tool **Book an offer now**, and **Send an offer** and **Make an offer** take Book it now too; the assistant (Assistant at the top of the menu) takes it in the same sentence as the offer. Each is two steps: you see what will change (nothing is changed yet), then you confirm, and the booking waits for the renter to sign and pay as above. As an Admin it is done at once; when customer service or Sales ask the assistant, it waits for your one-tap Approve.

## A request replaced by a newer one
When a request or offer expired and the renter made a newer one for the same car and dates, the old one is hidden from Requests and keeps its number and history. Both booking pages say so under the title: **Replaced by #CC-10483** on the old one and **Replaces #CC-10482** on the new one, each a link to the other. Customer service, Sales and the other staff pages show the same note.

## Change protection (release 41)

How damage to the car is covered is one control on the booking page: the **Protection** card at the top (Overview and the Money tab). An Admin, customer service and fleet use it on any booking; sales on a request or an offer.

1. Press **Change protection**. A small window lists the three options: **Own insurance (OPCF 27)**, **Credit card coverage** and **Protection Plan**, each with the price difference (the plan shows its price a day times the days, plus HST), the deposit (no coverage rule changes it) and what the renter provides.
2. The rule is the same as on the renter''s page: credit card coverage needs the renter''s card picked from the coverage list, a card that covers this car, and the renter''s confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs the renter''s confirmation that they upload their policy; otherwise the Protection Plan. An Admin can tick Admin override: the reason is recorded on the change and in the booking history.
3. Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press **Change protection**.

What happens: the booking is repriced at once. More to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab; less, when the plan was paid, is a refund for an Admin to approve. No money moves by itself. An offer is sent again as a new version; a confirmed booking or a rental in progress gets the amended agreement (the renter signs the new version when the rules ask) and one email. Proof tasks follow the new option. Changes are refused after damage is reported on the booking.

A renter''s request to leave the Protection Plan shows on the same card with their proof (**Open the proof**). Customer service or an Admin presses **Approve** (the change is made and the coverage confirmed) or **Decline** with a note the renter reads. The task "The renter asks to leave the Protection Plan" opens the booking.

## Change the car before pickup

On a request, an offer or a confirmed booking that is not picked up yet, press **Change the car** at the top of the booking.

1. Choose the new car. Only cars free for the whole booking are listed, each with its new total and the difference.
2. Say why the car changes, then press **Change the car**.
3. The price comes from the new car''s rate sheet (its rates, the km included and the rate per km). The coverage, the drivers and the add-ons stay as they are.
4. An offer is sent again with the new car: that offer is the renter''s one email.
5. On a confirmed booking, more to pay is left open: the renter sees **Pay the balance** on their booking, or you send a pay link or charge the saved card from Money. Less to pay becomes a refund that waits for approval, with a To do for Finance. The renter gets one email, **Booking updated**, with the new car and the money.
6. The open handover and return jobs move to the new car. The agreement gets a new version for the renter to sign; its link goes by text.
7. The booking''s history and the audit log keep who changed it, from which car, to which car and why.

Customer service and Admins change any of them; Sales changes a request or an offer; Fleet changes a confirmed booking. Once the car is out, use **Swap vehicle** instead.

## The accident card of a booking

Every booking from confirmation to the return shows its **Accident card**: the steps after an accident and the coverage this booking uses.

- OPCF 27: the renter''s own insurer and policy number, from the proof they uploaded.
- Credit card coverage: the card and its coverage provider, from their proof.
- Protection Plan: the provider, the policy number and the claims phone from Settings > Program (Tolls and damage), with the renter''s plan reference.

Press **Print the card** for the printable card. The renter has the same card on their booking. It never shows the fleet policy.

## Close ended trips

A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.

**Bookings** shows a banner when trips have ended and are not closed; **Close ended trips** lists each one: never picked up in the system, on rent after the return, or returned and never closed. Fleet and Finance have the same page.

1. Tick one or several, then **Mark them**: returned on time, returned late (give the time it came back), or a no-show (an Admin or customer service).
2. Choose the deposit: **Deduct the balance owed**, **Deduct the late fee**, or **Release in full**. A card hold that has expired is marked settled at once (released by expiry: no money moves).
3. If no deposit was taken, an Admin fills **Admin: deposit not taken, waive it because** (the same field is in Record a past trip).
4. Nothing is released by itself: the decision waits under **Deposit decisions waiting for an Admin**, and an Admin presses **Release** (or **Release now (tolls window)**).

## Return charges

A late return is charged per started extra day at the booking''s full daily cost (the rental per day after discounts, plus per-day and per-trip fees such as the Protection Plan, never delivery), and only the started hours after the whole days get the hourly late fee. On the booking''s **Money** tab, each renter line not on a statement yet has **Change amount** (lower) and **Waive**, with the reason; it is in the booking history and the next assessment keeps it. An expired card hold after the return has **Mark settled (released by expiry)**.

## Switching a booking to the Protection Plan (release 43)

**Change protection** > **Protection Plan** uses the car''s own plan price, the same amount the window quotes. It is no longer refused when Fees has no flat Protection Plan amount.

## The Protection Plan priced from RentalCover (release 35)

The Protection Plan stays our product: renters never see the RentalCover name. Without the RentalCover partner key it is priced from the Protection Plan table, as before. Once the key is set, its price comes from a real RentalCover quote for the renter (their dates, their age at pickup, their name and email) plus our markup (20% unless **Settings** > **Program** changes it). The request form asks for the quote once the renter''s details are in, and an offer as you choose option 3; a quote is reused for 15 minutes. A price you type for the plan wins. If RentalCover does not answer, the table price applies.

RentalCover covers up to $50,000 an incident, so the plan is offered only for a car worth less. The value used: your override under **Value for the Protection Plan** on the car''s page when set, else the car''s Canadian Black Book value, else an AI estimate from typical listing prices that the site makes by itself (**Refresh the AI estimate** asks again). A car with no value counts as over the limit: the request form, the offer screen and the database then offer only OPCF 27 or credit card coverage.

## Extensions at the all-in price a day (release 35)

An extension costs what the renter already pays, averaged per day: the booking''s total for the booked period (the rental after discounts, every fee, one-time fees like delivery included, and HST) divided by its days, for each added day. A booking of $729.36 for 7 days costs $104.19 for each added day. Added hours under a day cost the hourly late fee with HST, never more than a day. There is no extension discount.

| Where | What happens |
| --- | --- |
| The renter''s **Extend** page | Each option shows the total and the price a day before paying |
| **Edit** on a confirmed or on-trip booking, made longer | The booking''s new total is the all-in price of the longer stay; the per-trip fees stay as booked and the rental charge takes the difference |
| The next period of a long rental | Keeps the rate of the booked period (the rental a day, per-trip fees scaled) |
| An insurer-billed booking | Priced as before |

The extension is one line on the booking, "Extension: 3 days at $104.19/day (all-in)", HST included. Its HST is the booking''s own share of HST, so invoices and the books never add HST on top. Type a rental charge in **Edit** to set another price. Late returns are unchanged: the daily cost of each extra day and the hourly late fee.

## A fixed amount per payment (release 35)

On a weekly, every 2 weeks or monthly plan, an Admin can set **Fixed amount per payment** in **Change the plan**. Each payment is that amount and the last one takes the remainder. The total and the payments already made never change. Leave it empty to split the payments by the days again.

## The request as sent and every offer (release 35)

On a request or a booking, **Original request, as the renter sent it** shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. **Offer history** lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.

1. To go back to an old version, press **Revert to this offer** on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.
2. Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.

The **Coverage** line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.

## Send an offer in three steps (release 35)

1. **Car and dates**: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.
2. **Price**: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout''s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.
3. **Review and send**: what changed, the message and how the link goes.

Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under **More options**. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.

## The owner''s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)

- **Owner''s own trip ($0)**: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.
- **Instant (repeat renter)**: a Gold renter or above (Rewards, release 40) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter''s instant booking away with **Take instant booking away**, on the booking page or on the renter''s page.
- **Any car, any time** (release 40): a Platinum renter asked for dates the car shows as taken. Fleet gets an urgent task due within 4 hours: confirm it, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter''s confirmed booking for it. The task closes when the request is answered.
- **Book it now** pressed by staff waits for an Admin''s one-tap approval.

## Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)

The booking shows the renter''s **Secondary contact** when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes **rideshare documents** (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.

## Offers, coverage, delivery and fuel (releases 35 and 36)

- Sending an offer is three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every request shows the renter''s original request as sent and every offer version, with who sent it and when; reverting loads an old version as a new offer to send.
- Instant booking: a verified Gold renter or above books an available car at once, signs and pays; the booking is marked Instant (repeat renter), and an Admin can take instant booking away from a renter.
- Card coverage is checked against the car: the card, the car''s value, its type and the rental length. A card that does not cover it cannot be approved. OPCF 27 needs both the pink slip and the endorsement page.
- Delivery is priced by distance from the company''s address (1570 Midland Ave, Scarborough): a base, the kilometres included and a rate per km, all in Program settings; a car''s own fee stays as an override.
- The fuel line at the return is suggested from the car''s tank, the weekly pump price and a multiplier, plus the refuelling fee, and checked on the deposit review before any charge.
- Owner price limits: the daily minimum and maximum of a car or an owner hold every price, discount and offer; only an Admin can allow one request outside them, with a reason.
- Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking page (rental agreement copy, coverage letter, vehicle letter); staff get an alert when they are made. The secondary contact shows on the booking.
- Mid-trip review ask: halfway through a trip of several days, the renter gets one short message asking how it is going; a problem they report becomes a To do for customer service.
- A car that has only test bookings can be deleted by an Admin; the test bookings go with it. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)

**Start the check-in (pickup)** and **Start the check-out (return)** on the booking, and **Check in** or **Check out** on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:

1. Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.
2. What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car''s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.
3. Photos are one tap each: **Take this photo** always shows the next angle.
4. What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.
5. The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example "Next: Odometer") and takes you to it. When everything is in, press **Hand over the keys** or **Complete the return**.

Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.

**Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)** is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.

## A late return is a choice (release 42)

A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows **Late return** with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:

1. **Charge as an extension**: every started day late at the booking''s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.
2. **Charge extra days**: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.
3. **Charge the late return fee**: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).
4. **Charge a custom amount**: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.
5. **Waive it**: no charge, with the reason.

Press **Save the late return charge**. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.

Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do "Late return: choose the charge". Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.

> Good to know: A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do "Late return: approve the charge" and press **Approve as asked**, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.

On **Close ended trips**, marking a trip returned late and choosing **Deduct the late fee** is the same choice of the late return fee, made there. The other deposit choices leave the late return to be chosen on the booking.',
  '<p class="gd-p">A booking starts as a request from the website, or as an offer you send yourself to a customer on the phone. You check it, adjust it and send the offer; an offer that is out is changed in place. After that, the booking page holds the money, documents, changes and history.</p><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-bookings-now-what-is-out-coming-back-and-owed" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Bookings now: what is out, coming back and owed</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>. It opens on <b class="gd-ui">Now</b>, one screen that refreshes by itself every 30 seconds. Every time is Toronto time.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The numbers at the top: cars out now, due back today, overdue, going out in the next 72 hours, payments due in the next 7 days (with the total) and free cars. Tap one to jump to its list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Out now</b>: every car on rent, overdue returns first in red. Each shows the car (photo, code, plate), the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, when it was picked up, when it is due back with a countdown, the payment plan and the next payment, the deposit held, and the km and fuel at pickup. Filter by Overdue, Due today or Payment due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking whose pickup time has passed with no check-in recorded is listed as out, with <b class="gd-ui">Out (pickup not recorded)</b>. The car most likely left. Press <b class="gd-ui">Mark picked up</b>: it records the pickup at the booked time (change it if the car left at another time), the booking goes on rent, and Fleet gets a task to add the photos, km and fuel. The usual checks stay: the deposit taken (or an Admin waives it with the reason), the renter&#39;s signature (or an Admin&#39;s reason), the agreement&#39;s details, every driver verified and the coverage confirmed. If one is missing, the reason is shown.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Coming back</b>: overdue, today and tomorrow, by the time each is due.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Going out</b>: confirmed pickups in the next 72 hours, delivery or pickup, with ticks and crosses for the licence, the signed agreement, the payment, the deposit (a clock until the morning of the pickup day, when the hold is placed on the card on file) and the check-in photos (done at the handover).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money due</b>: every rental payment due in the next 7 days or overdue, the amount, the plan and which payment it is (for example 3 of 4).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Free now</b>: cars available and not out, the longest idle first, with the next pickup; then the cars in maintenance or cleaning. Partners&#39; cars are counted apart.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Placeholder bookings never show on Now.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Payment plans</h3><p class="gd-p">A rental is paid in full at pickup, weekly, every 2 weeks, or monthly. A rental longer than one period (30 days) pays each period by itself. To change it, open the booking, then the <b class="gd-ui">Payment plan</b> card on Overview or Money, and press <b class="gd-ui">Change the plan</b>. Each payment is its share of the total by its days, due on the day it starts. An insurer-billed rental shows <b class="gd-ui">Insurer billed</b> and is never in Money due unless the renter owes a part. Admins, customer service and finance change the plan; fleet sees it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-all-bookings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">All bookings</h2><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">All bookings</b> tab of Bookings has the search (booking number, name, email, phone, plate or car code), the status (All, Out now, Booked, Returned, Cancelled; closed bookings are found with the search, which also finds the insurer). <b class="gd-ui">Out now</b> shows the bookings on rent and those whose pickup passed without a check-in, together. Each booking is one row: its number and status in plain words, the car with its photo, the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, the dates, the money (paid up, to pay, overdue, insurer billed) and Bill to.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-request-queue" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The request queue</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Requests and offers</b>. The oldest waiting request is at the top.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The numbers at the top: waiting for an offer, past the reply target (red), offers out, accepted but not paid, and offers expired. Each one is a filter: press it and the list shows just those, with the matching chip below marked as chosen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">One queue, the most urgent first: the longest wait, then offers accepted but not paid, then offers out by when they expire. Each row has the car with its photo, the dates, the price, the renter with <b class="gd-ui">Call</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text</b>, the licence (verified, to review, or not uploaded yet), who is answering it, and one button: <b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Follow up</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Open</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> sits beside <b class="gd-ui">Send offer</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Waiting shows how long the renter has waited (&quot;12 min&quot;, &quot;3 h&quot;, &quot;2 days&quot;); red means past the first reply target (5 minutes, set in Program settings). <b class="gd-ui">Promise</b> counts down the 2 hours the site promises the renter.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by Active, New, Changes asked, Offer out, Accepted, not paid or Expired. The list remembers your last choice on that device; <b class="gd-ui">Active</b> always shows the whole queue and replaces what it remembered. When the same renter asks for the same car for overlapping dates again and the earlier request or offer expired, only the newest is listed: the older ones are linked to it and leave Requests (they keep their history). An expired offer leaves the active queue 48 hours after it expired, or once its pickup time passed; Expired lists the ones from the last 7 days. After 7 days an expired offer leaves Requests and offers and becomes a renter lead, once, in People &gt; Renters &gt; Leads (Expired offers), with the car and the dates the renter wanted and a To do for Sales to win them back. An offer still out when its pickup time passes expires by itself.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/requests</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/820"><img src="/guides/img/admin-02-requests-desktop-6521282d.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="820"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.9%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.2%;top:43.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A request whose pickup time passes without an offer expires by itself, with a note in its history. The renter is not emailed unless &quot;Email the renter when their request expires that way&quot; is on in Program settings.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-answer-a-request-with-an-offer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Answer a request with an offer</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The Review and offer tab shows the request as the renter sent it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Adjust the car, the dates, the rate type, the places, the rates (under <b class="gd-ui">Show rate card</b>) and fees, the deposit and extras. A place changed away from a delivery or a collection takes its fee box and its fee with it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Price on the right updates as you change things.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a message, choose how long the offer stays open, then press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1200/1550"><img src="/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-353f3707.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="1550"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:5%;top:6.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:7.5%;top:45.8%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.2%;top:42.6%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.7%;top:98.1%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Changed fields but not ready to send? Press <b class="gd-ui">Save changes</b>. The panel &quot;The offer as the renter sees it&quot; shows the result.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Can&#39;t do it? Press <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> and fill in Reason and any alternative.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Need an answer first? Press <b class="gd-ui">Ask the renter</b> to send a question.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10069?tab=review</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:500/80"><img src="/guides/img/admin-03-booking-review-desktop-4dd4ed06.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="500" height="80"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.2%;top:52.5%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18%;top:52.5%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Opening a request takes it for you: everyone else sees &quot;Being answered by&quot; your name and since when, with Send the offer and Decline off, until you send, decline or leave (20 minutes, renewed while you work; Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Take over</b> to answer one someone else holds; it is noted in the history. A second answer is refused with who answered and when. A request from the website opens to Sales after 15 minutes (Program settings); until then Admins, customer service and fleet answer it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-send-an-offer-without-a-request" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer without a request</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> at the top of Bookings, or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer without a request</b> on Requests and offers. For a customer on the phone, by text or at the counter: no request needed.</p><p class="gd-p">The screen is seven short steps, each with one line saying what to do, and the price beside it (on a phone the total sits at the bottom of the screen: press <b class="gd-ui">See every line</b>). What most offers never need is under each step&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, which stays open while something in it is used.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Who is renting and when</b>: find the renter by name, phone or email, or press <b class="gd-ui">Not on file? Add a new customer</b> (full legal name, mobile, email for the offer link, date of birth). A customer already on file with the same email or phone is shown with Use: one person, one record. A renter picked from the file shows what is on their record under their name: the licence (class, number, expiry), the home address and the drivers named before, with a licence that has expired or an address over a year old flagged to ask them about. Then the pickup and the return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Which car</b>: search by car code, plate or name; each car says Free or Not free for the dates. More options: the rate card and the type and free-only filters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Where they pick up and return</b>: at our location, we deliver or collect (the address and distance), an airport or the owner&#39;s location. The fee each one makes shows under it, Automatic or Set by hand.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">How damage is covered</b>: the renter&#39;s own insurance, a credit card or the Protection Plan. More options: another Protection Plan price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Extras</b>: add-ons, when the car has any.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">The price</b>: the rate sheet price is filled in. More options: another price (a total for the trip or a rate a day, with why), Amounts I type (before or after HST), the total the renter pays, kilometres, a promo code, the deposit and a discount (an Admin), and <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b>: press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> to set one by hand, <b class="gd-ui">Reset to automatic</b> to undo it. Below: how it is paid (card online and a card hold unless you change it under More options).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send it</b>: who found this client (sales and customer service), a message, and Text or Email. More options: how long the offer is open, the owner&#39;s view, who found the client (an Admin) and the internal note. Above the button, <b class="gd-ui">Ready to send</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Missing:</b> with what is left; press Send and each missing field says what it needs. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer to</b> the renter, or <b class="gd-ui">Save without sending</b> to keep it as a request for later. <b class="gd-ui">The offer as the renter sees it</b> is under the price.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Choices drive the charges. Take off a delivery, a collection, the Protection Plan or an add-on and its fee goes with it, even a fee set by hand: there is nothing to remove in a second place. Choose it again and the fee starts from the automatic amount.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>It makes the same request and offer the website makes: the renter approves, signs and pays (or you record the payment), and only then is the car on the calendar. No &quot;request received&quot; email goes to the renter for an offer you send. Staff commissions and statements count it like any other booking.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-change-an-offer-that-is-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change an offer that is out</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter has the offer (Offered), or approved it and has not paid (Signing and payment). Open <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> on the booking and press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Change anything: the car, the dates, the places, the price, fees, the deposit, add-ons, how it is paid. Each changed field is highlighted and the before and after are listed. Amounts I type (Before tax or After tax) and the Total the renter pays (after tax) work as on Send an offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Write what changed in Message to the renter and choose how long the offer is open.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save and send the update</b>: the renter gets the new version by email or text (ticked), and the old version no longer counts. Or press <b class="gd-ui">Save without telling the renter</b> and tell them yourself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking is changed with <b class="gd-ui">Change the booking</b> (Propose a change, below).</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>No need to withdraw first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw the offer</b> is only for taking it back for good; <b class="gd-ui">Send again, later expiry</b> gives the renter more time, and <b class="gd-ui">Renter approved by phone</b> records a yes given on a call.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-edit-a-booking-that-has-started" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit a booking that has started</h2><p class="gd-p">On a confirmed, on-trip or returned booking (an Admin: a closed one too), Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Edit the booking</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Change the pickup or the return (extend or shorten: the rental charge is worked out again at this booking&#39;s rates), the car (on trip: the car it leaves goes to Out of service for Fleet to check), the rental charge for the trip, each fee, the kilometres a day, the deposit (an Admin) and the note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type why, if you like, and tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter what changed</b>, or leave it off for a silent correction. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the changes</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What is open now shows at once: <b class="gd-ui">Email a pay link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Text a pay link</b> for exactly that amount, <b class="gd-ui">Charge</b> the saved card (the renter agreed), or record cash or an e-Transfer on the Money tab.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each edit is kept with who, when, why, before and after (Edits, under the form) and in the booking&#39;s history. A closed booking&#39;s owner split and the staff commission follow. To have the renter accept and sign first, use Propose a change instead.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-restore-a-version-of-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Restore a version of a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">Once a confirmed booking has been changed, Overview shows <b class="gd-ui">Versions of this booking</b>: the booking before its first change, then one version after each change (a fee changed on its own too), the newest marked current.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Find the version to go back to (its dates, days, car, rental charge and total are listed) and press <b class="gd-ui">Restore this version</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The preview shows what changes: the dates, the car, the rental charge, the total, and what the renter would owe or be owed. Nothing is changed yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Type why, tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell the renter what changed</b> if they should know, and press <b class="gd-ui">Restore version</b> with its number. The dates, the car, the rental charge and every fee go back exactly as they were in that version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">It is one more change in the history, with your name and the reason. Payments are never touched: a difference is a balance to collect or a credit to settle, as with any edit.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The same checks as Edit: the car must be free for those dates, and customer service and Sales restore only while Program settings let staff change bookings (and fees). A version kept before Release 45 has no fees with it: its dates, car and rental charge go back and the fees stay as they are; the preview says so.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-fees-a-forgotten-fee-and-the-balance" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fees, a forgotten fee and the balance</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking&#39;s Money tab, Fees lists each fee. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type a new amount (for the whole trip, before HST) beside any fee, or choose one not on the booking (the young driver fee shows its price for these dates), or add a charge of its own with or without HST.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the fees</b>. The balance shows by part (rental, fees) with the pay link, the saved card and Record a payment beside it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The renter sees the balance on their booking with a Pay button, and pays by card on Stripe&#39;s form.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every change is recorded (Changes to the fees): the amount before and after, who and why. Customer service and sales may change fees while Program settings, Staff may change fees, is on.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Changing the amount of a line on the Money tab changes the booking&#39;s total and balance with it, so no balance appears that nobody owes. An Admin can set the total directly with <b class="gd-ui">Change the total</b>: the difference goes on the rental charge.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-renter-with-only-a-debit-or-prepaid-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A renter with only a debit or prepaid card</h2><p class="gd-p">A credit card is required by default: the deposit must be on a credit card so the deductible can be charged. The pay page tells a renter with only a debit or prepaid card to contact us.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking&#39;s Money tab, press <b class="gd-ui">Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking</b> and type the reason. Who and when are kept, and the change is in the booking&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The booking&#39;s pay page, staff pay links and deposit hold then take a debit or prepaid card, and the renter is told the hold lowers the money available on the card until it is released, which can take several business days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Require a credit card again</b> turns it off.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The Money tab shows each card used and its type (credit, debit, prepaid). A booking on credit card rental coverage is always paid on the credit card that carries the coverage, and cannot be allowed. Program settings, <b class="gd-ui">Card types accepted</b>, can open debit and prepaid cards to every booking.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-correct-a-renter-s-details" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Correct a renter&#39;s details</h2><p class="gd-p">On the renter&#39;s page (People, Renters) or on any of their bookings, <b class="gd-ui">Edit renter</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the name, email, phone, date of birth, licence, home address (start typing to find it) or the staff note.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A new email also becomes their sign-in at once (no confirmation needed for a typo you correct); tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter a link to set a password</b> to send one there. Unsigned agreements and offers go to the new address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the renter</b>. An email that another renter has is refused with their name; the same phone is a warning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The same person entered twice? Possible duplicates (same email, same phone, or same name and date of birth) shows under the renter. <b class="gd-ui">Merge into this record</b> moves the other record&#39;s bookings, licences, cards, payments, documents and messages here and fills any detail missing here; the other record stays, blocked, with the merge in both histories.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-money-tab-rental-charges-and-security-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Money tab: Rental charges and Security deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking&#39;s Money tab opens on a strip with the three numbers that matter: <b class="gd-ui">Rental due</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Deposit</b> (one word: Not collected, Held, Charged, Released or Partly kept) and <b class="gd-ui">Total paid</b>. Below are two panels, side by side on a computer and one above the other on a phone. Collecting one never touches the other, and every receipt says which one it is.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Rental charges</b>: each line of the price and the total, Paid, then Balance due.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The one main button, Collect (the amount) rental: choose how. <b class="gd-ui">The card on file</b> charges it now (Finance or an Admin); <b class="gd-ui">A payment link by text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">A payment link by email</b> sends the renter Stripe&#39;s secure form; <b class="gd-ui">On this device: hand it to the renter</b> opens it for the renter to type; <b class="gd-ui">Cash, e-Transfer or another way (record it)</b> records money received (an e-Transfer, cheque or transfer needs its reference). For: the rental and fees together by default, or one of them. With the card on file, the rental and fees together are one charge with one receipt that lists both (the rental is paid first, then the fees; an insurer&#39;s part and money already received another way are left out). The renter gets a receipt; <b class="gd-ui">Print</b> prints one to hand over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">A later charge</b> (before the return): on the card on file, by a link, on this device, or recorded. Choose the <b class="gd-ui">Reason</b> from the list (Mileage overage, Fuel, Cleaning, Smoking, Late return, Tolls, Tickets/fines, Damage, Missing items, Other) and add a note; Other needs its note. The renter&#39;s receipt shows the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Save a card</b> saves the renter&#39;s card without charging it. Card readers, the fees (<b class="gd-ui">Change or add a fee</b>), failed card payments (<b class="gd-ui">Paid another way</b>), payments received another way and <b class="gd-ui">Refund</b> sit in this panel too. The history lists rental payments only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An offer paid another way: once the renter approved and signed and the money is recorded, the booking is confirmed (or press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm the booking</b>).</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Security deposit</b>: the amount, how it is taken (a credit card hold, a debit or prepaid card at the standard multiple, a charge, or cash), its status in one word and the next step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Not collected: the one main button, Collect (the amount) deposit. <b class="gd-ui">Hold on the card on file</b> places the hold now (Finance or an Admin); <b class="gd-ui">A deposit hold link by text</b> or <b class="gd-ui">A deposit hold link by email</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">A hold on this device: hand it to the renter</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file as the deposit</b> only when no hold can be placed; <b class="gd-ui">Cash or e-Transfer (record it)</b>. The rental balance is not touched.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Before every pickup the deposit hold link is texted to the renter on its own: 24 hours before (at once when the pickup is sooner), for a confirmed booking whose deposit is a card hold with no hold yet. The panel says <b class="gd-ui">Deposit link texted</b> and when it was opened. No mobile number, or the text not sent: a task <b class="gd-ui">Deposit link not sent</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, then Site settings, Deposit link by text: on or off, and the hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Held, while the car is out: <b class="gd-ui">Release</b> (an Admin, with the reason), <b class="gd-ui">Keep part (damage/fees)</b> with the amount and the reason from the list, or <b class="gd-ui">Re-authorize the hold</b> on the saved card before it lapses (the panel shows when the hold expires). A job re-authorizes it by itself about 24 hours before it expires; if it cannot, Finance and the Admins get the alert <b class="gd-ui">Deposit hold not re-authorized</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hold expired</b>: a card hold lasts about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. Once it has expired, nothing can be kept from it: the panel says Hold expired, Keep and Release are hidden, and <b class="gd-ui">Charge the card on file instead</b> opens the later charge with the amount and the reason filled in.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">After the return: <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b> (below).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive the deposit</b> (an Admin, before it is taken), <b class="gd-ui">Change the debit deposit</b>, and <b class="gd-ui">Allow debit and prepaid cards for this booking</b> sit in this panel. The history lists deposit payments only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">A deposit taken in cash or by e-Transfer is given back the same way after the return: Finance gets a task; press <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b> with the reference or receipt number.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Statements, reconciliation and the deposit settlement read each payment with its method: a cash deposit is never refunded to a card.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-settle-the-deposit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Settle the deposit</h2><p class="gd-p">The deposit is never given back by itself. Finance or an Admin settles it after the return: on the booking&#39;s Money tab, under Deposit, press <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. Issue the Check-out statement first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The form shows the deposit, what is still available, the charges owed from the statement and what is taken from the deposit for them. What the deposit does not cover is charged to the card on file; with no card (or a card declined), the renter gets a pay link by email and text, and Finance has a task until it is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tolls and tickets can take up to 7 days to come in. Inside that window the whole rest of the deposit is filled in as the hold-back, until the window ends. To give it back sooner, tick Release now anyway: a toll that comes in later is charged to the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something still open keeps the whole deposit: an incident, a claim, new damage at the return not priced, damage found later not billed, a toll or ticket on the car during the rental not matched or not charged, a card dispute, or charges not on a statement yet. The form lists them. Only an Admin can release part of it, with the reason; it is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Damage: <b class="gd-ui">Keep the whole deposit (damage)</b> turns what is left of the deposit into a damage charge, with what was damaged and the photos; the renter is told. <b class="gd-ui">Bill damage</b> adds a damage charge up to the $2,500 deductible (more goes through a claim): the deposit pays first, then the card on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Settle</b>. The money moves at Stripe at once: the charges are collected and what is not owed is refunded or the hold released. A step Stripe refuses is tried again by itself, and Finance gets a task if it keeps failing.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A card hold lapses after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise. While the car is out, or returned and not settled, the hold is collected in full a day and a half before it lapses: that keeps the money, and the settlement refunds what is not owed. A hold that lapses anyway is charged to the saved card, and Finance is told at once.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A booking</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>, then a booking number. Or type the number in the search box.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Tabs: Overview, Money, Changes, History, and Drivers and documents.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Overview shows the trip, the renter, what is still missing for the handover, and the price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open tasks for this booking, with the queue and the due time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Top right: <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b> and <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b>, the menu with <b class="gd-ui">Edit the offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Stop blocking the calendar</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Cancel for the renter</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Cancel by CarmaCars</b> and the rest.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Under the booking number: <b class="gd-ui">Next step</b>, what happens next and who does it, with one button for that step (for example <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Sign on this device</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check in the car</b>); then where the booking is on its way, from Request to Closed, with the dates, the days, the total and who pays.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/960"><img src="/guides/img/admin-04-booking-desktop-b56b668a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="960"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50%;top:46.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:85.4%;top:14.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.9%;top:26.8%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-check-a-car-out-or-in" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check a car out or in</h2><p class="gd-p">From the booking, with your phone or a tablet: the same checklist field staff use.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A confirmed booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Check in (pickup)</b> under Check-in, check-out and signing; a booking on rent shows <b class="gd-ui">Check out (return)</b>. Today lists the check-ins and check-outs due, each with <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The checklist opens: the ready check, the renter and their licence and card, the odometer (km) and fuel or charge, the keys, the photo set (every side, the wheels, the interior, the odometer and fuel gauge, the plate), damage marks with close-ups, then the renter and you sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos wait on the device without a connection and upload in the background. Each keeps its time, and the place when the device allows location.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A field job of the booking is taken over (the history says so); with no job, one is made for you. When done, press <b class="gd-ui">See the photo report</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Fleet, Sales and Customer service check cars out and in the same way from their own booking page.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-photo-report-late-returns-and-the-return-charges" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The photo report, late returns and the return charges</h2><p class="gd-p">Under Check-in, check-out and signing, press <b class="gd-ui">Photo report</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The report shows the due-back time, the actual check-in and check-out, Late by (or Overdue by while the car is out), the odometer and kilometres over the allowance, the fuel or charge out and in, every photo with its time and place, and the damage.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">At check-out the mileage overage and the fuel or recharging are written to the return charges at once. A late return (after the grace period of the fee defaults) is not: it waits for a choice on the booking (see &quot;A late return is a choice&quot;). The fuel is a suggested line: the car&#39;s tank x the fuel missing x the pump price of its grade (Program settings, updated weekly) x 1.25, plus the refuelling fee; an electric car the battery kWh x the charge missing x the price a kWh, plus the fee. A pump receipt entered later replaces it. Fleet and Finance confirm it on the deposit review; it is never charged to a card by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not charging one? Press <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b> beside it and give the reason: it stays waived if the charges are worked out again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The time was wrong? Press <b class="gd-ui">Correct the check-out time</b> (or the check-in time) with the reason: lateness follows, a return that is no longer late loses its late charge, and the history keeps both times.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The renter gets the same report (without these buttons) by email and in their Documents. Late by shows on the booking and in the Bookings list.</div></li></ol></div><h3 class="gd-h3">The renter says the car is back</h3><p class="gd-p">Every overdue email, text and alert (at the return time, at 15 minutes and the final notice) has a one-tap <b class="gd-ui">I&#39;ve returned the car</b> link, and the renter&#39;s booking page has the button. The renter can add photos, the odometer, the fuel level and the time they returned it. Sending it stops every overdue notice of the booking at once, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Returned, waiting for confirmation</b>, and Fleet gets an urgent To do: &quot;The renter says the car is back&quot;.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking. The card <b class="gd-ui">The renter says the car is back</b> shows what the renter gave, marked renter-provided, with their photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the car: the return place, the tracker, the photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm</b> to complete the trip. Correct the odometer, fuel or return time first if they are wrong: the late charges follow the time you confirm. The renter&#39;s photos join the check-out report.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Deny</b> and say why. The renter gets your reason by email and text, and the overdue notices start again.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Checking the car in the usual way also completes the trip and stops the notices. Admins, Fleet, Sales, Customer service and field staff can Confirm or Deny.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-signatures-on-the-spot-or-by-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signatures on the spot, or by link</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter or an additional driver signs the rental agreement on your device, or on their own phone.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">While a signature is missing, the booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email the signing link</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Text the signing link</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">No agreement made yet (the renter has not saved their details at home)? <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b> still shows: press <b class="gd-ui">Prepare the agreement to sign now</b> and it is made on the spot.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>: confirm the name matches their licence and that you saw the original licence (photograph it if none is on file), then press <b class="gd-ui">Hand the device to</b> and their name.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">They read both agreements (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), tick the statements and sign. Then <b class="gd-ui">Back to the staff view</b> for the next signer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The record is the same as signing online, and says it was signed in person, collected by you, on your device. It is printed on the signed copy&#39;s signature record page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-rental-agreements-every-version-every-field" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental agreements: every version, every field</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking&#39;s Rental agreements card: the current version of CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s agreements, every earlier one, and what is still blank.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Once the agreement is signed and countersigned, any change to what it prints makes a new version of both documents by itself: the dates, the price lines, the car, a driver added or corrected, the coverage, the deposit or how it was paid, an address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A change to the dates, the price, the car, the drivers or the coverage option is signed again: the renter (and each driver it affects) gets their link by email and text, and the card shows &quot;Agreement v3 waiting for signature&quot;. A correction (a typo in an address, a plate written differently) is filed without signing; the renter gets the corrected copy by email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check-in makes the &quot;as picked up&quot; copy (time out, km out, fuel out, the car&#39;s plate and VIN, the check-in report), countersigned by whoever checked the car out; check-out makes the closing copy (time in, km in, driven and charged, fuel in, late hours, damage, the return charges, the final totals). Both go to the renter by email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Every version</b> lists each one with what changed and both PDFs. <b class="gd-ui">Resend the signing links</b>, or press the button with their first name beside it to have them sign on your phone or tablet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The card lists what the agreements still print blank (a licence expiry, the insurer&#39;s policy number, the insured vehicle, a VIN). Type the values and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the missing fields</b>: the agreements follow.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Check-in stops while a field a claim needs is blank. An Admin can let it go ahead: type the reason and press <b class="gd-ui">Override</b>; the reason is in the booking&#39;s history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the agreements again</b> checks both against the booking at once (they also follow every change by themselves).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit the wording</b> (Admin only) changes CarmaCars&#39; agreement text for this booking: press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> beside a clause, edit its text, say why and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the wording</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Add</b> writes Additional terms at the end of Part 2. Only clauses not required by law or the insurer can be removed; the consents are fixed, and Blind Spot&#39;s form (the insurer&#39;s official form) is never changed. Before the renter signs, the agreement is made again; after, the change is a new version they sign, and <b class="gd-ui">Every version</b> shows each clause before and after.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-signing-that-holds-up-in-a-dispute" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Signing that holds up in a dispute</h2><p class="gd-p">Every signature on the site is made the same way: rental agreements, amendments and new versions (remotely or on your device), and the owner agreements, schedules and forms, a co-owner&#39;s link, the partner, investment and staff agreements.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The licence on file is shown. A 6-digit code to their phone or email on file is optional: the signer may press <b class="gd-ui">Verify by code (optional)</b>, and Program settings, E-signing, <b class="gd-ui">ask for a one-time code</b> makes it a required first step again (off by default). Without the code, the certificate says the identity was not confirmed by a code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">They say they read the documents, initial the key terms (each initials box is saved with <b class="gd-ui">Save initials</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> takes it back to initial again) (damage and the deductible, the deposit and later charges, fuel, kilometres and late returns, their coverage, cancellation), give three consents (to sign electronically, to receive records electronically, to card charges under the agreement) and draw their signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Owners, partners, investors and staff do the same for their documents: the code, the reading, the key terms of their documents initialled (for example the Enrollment Agreement&#39;s three confirmations, Form C&#39;s acknowledgments, Schedule C, the staff agreement&#39;s confidentiality), two consents and the drawn signature. Form C&#39;s witness still types their name beside the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Each step is recorded with its time, IP address and device, and the place when the device shares it. The signed PDFs end with a certificate of completion; anyone can check a signed file at <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/verify</span>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Typed names are off. For a signer who cannot draw, an Admin can turn on the accessibility fallback: <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Esign typed fallback.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-card-disputes-the-evidence-pack" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Card disputes: the evidence pack</h2><p class="gd-p">Everything that proves the rental, in one PDF for Stripe.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">When a card payment is disputed, the evidence pack is built by itself: the signed agreements with their certificates, the check-in and check-out reports with photos, kilometres and fuel, the licence, the payments and charges, every message to the renter, and the card checks from Stripe. It is staged in Stripe as the dispute&#39;s evidence, and To do gets an urgent task.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking: the Rental agreements card shows the pack. Press <b class="gd-ui">Download</b> to check it, then <b class="gd-ui">Submit to Stripe</b> before the evidence date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Build the dispute evidence pack</b> makes one at any time (an Admin or Finance).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-licence-before-an-offer-is-accepted" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The licence before an offer is accepted</h2><p class="gd-p">Front, back and a selfie, from the request on.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">After sending a request the renter is asked for their licence. A licence already on file from an earlier booking is used again while it is valid after the return.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The offer cannot be accepted (by the renter, or by you on their word) and nothing is paid until the licence and its expiry date are on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Review the images as usual with <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>: the card Renter documents is on Review and offer too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The switch is in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Booking requests and offers: Booking licence required (on), with the selfie (on).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-licence-reader" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The licence reader</h2><p class="gd-p">Every licence photo is read on upload: the back&#39;s barcode first, else the vision model (within the day&#39;s AI allowance).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The renter&#39;s empty licence fields are filled from the read; the renter confirms them. A blurry or cut-off photo is taken again at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b> shows what was read and one line per check, Pass or Flag: photos, valid to the return, class accepted, age at pickup, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back, and the main driver&#39;s Ontario licence. Staff still approve.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, Driver&#39;s licence reader: <b class="gd-ui">Approve automatically when every check passes</b> (off). On: a driver whose front and back both read sharp and every check passes is approved in your name; anything flagged waits for a person.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Primary driver must hold an Ontario licence</b> (on): a main driver with a licence from elsewhere becomes an additional driver, the booking needs &quot;Primary driver: Ontario licence needed&quot; and pickup is blocked. The renter adds a main driver, who signs on their own link. On the document review, <b class="gd-ui">Admin: undo or let it go</b>: undo puts the first main driver back; let it go needs a reason.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>What was read is staff only and is deleted with the licence image. The licence number is never written to the logs.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-renter-documents-licence-and-proof-of-coverage" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Renter documents: licence and proof of coverage</h2><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s licence photos, selfie and proof of coverage (OPCF 27 or a credit card&#39;s rental coverage) are checked before the handover. You check them yourself; no task is needed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A booking with documents waiting is a line on To do: &quot;Check &#39;s documents for booking &quot;, marked Now when the pickup is within two days. Press <b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The pop-up shows each driver&#39;s images and the coverage: the insurer, policy number and expiry, or the card, its type and whether the name matches.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">What to check is written once at the top. One wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>: they are asked for a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: every image, the proof of coverage and the Protection Plan still waiting are approved in one step. The number in the button is exactly what it approves (an image whose file was removed is not counted), and an image not tied to a driver of the booking is listed under <b class="gd-ui">Other documents</b>. Anything the system refuses is named with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The same pop-up is on the booking: the card Renter documents (<b class="gd-ui">Review documents</b>) on Overview and on Drivers and documents.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Each opening of a renter&#39;s documents is logged. The links to the images last one minute. Field staff can also check a licence in person at the check-in (photos and four checks): the history says &quot;checked in person&quot;. Field staff also review the licence images (not the coverage) of bookings on their own jobs in the next 7 days from My jobs, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the reviewer&#39;s role, field. Sales review the licence images (not the coverage) of any booking being arranged or under way from their To do or the booking, with the same Approve all or a reason to reject: the history says the role, sales.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-payments-by-day" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payments by day</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payments</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">By day</b> tab: every payment and refund of a day or a range, by method, the cash drawer and the refunds waiting. Finance has the same screen.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose From and To and the methods (card, e-Transfer, cash, cheque, platform payout, insurer, bank transfer, pre-authorized debit, other), then press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Totals by method and for each day; cards read as the card and its last four digits, never a code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The cash drawer: expected (cash in less cash given back) against the count Finance records with <b class="gd-ui">Record the count</b>; a difference shows over or short.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Refunds waiting: every refund asked for anywhere with the policy maths. <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with the reason in the row, then <b class="gd-ui">Issue the refund</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Export CSV</b> for the bookkeeper.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-propose-a-change-to-a-confirmed-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Propose a change to a confirmed booking</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter gets an email and answers on their booking. The calendar moves only when they accept.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open the booking&#39;s Changes tab. Under Propose a change, set the new pickup, return or car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To price it by hand, type a New rental charge before tax. Leave it empty to use the car&#39;s rates.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write the Reason, for the renter. They read it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Preview the price</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to the renter</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/bookings/CC-10065?tab=changes</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1200/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-05-booking-changes-desktop-97008b21.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1200" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:17.5%;top:33.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:9.2%;top:50%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.3%;top:71.2%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:12.9%;top:91.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-who-a-booking-is-credited-to" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Who a booking is credited to</h2><p class="gd-p">Overview (and Review and offer) shows the Sales credit: the staff member the booking counts for in their sales.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A quote or a rental is credited to whoever created or added it. A request from the website is credited to whoever sent its first offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To give it to someone else, press <b class="gd-ui">Reassign</b>, choose who (or Nobody), say whether they sourced the client and write the reason. The booking&#39;s history and the audit log keep it, and the deal stays in the same week and month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sourced means the staff member chose I sourced this client when they entered it, it came with a field staff referral link, or you credited it. Only a sourced booking earns a staff commission. A website request earns none unless you credit someone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Someone said they sourced a website request? The credit line shows the claim: press <b class="gd-ui">Credit them</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Not theirs</b>, with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A price typed by hand shows beside the rate-sheet price, with the reason. A price under the floor or past the discount limit is flagged: press <b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> once you have looked at it.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A request keeps the lead-time adjustment of the moment it came in (&quot;Short-notice pricing +10%&quot; or &quot;Booked ahead −5%&quot;), through the offer and the payment. To change it, open the booking&#39;s review screen, <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Lead-time pricing (%)</b>: a number (0 for none), or empty for the tier of the request. A price typed by hand replaces it.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The rental never goes below the car&#39;s minimum daily rate or above its maximum (its price limits, set by the owner or on the car&#39;s Rates tab), whatever the discount, promo code or lead-time pricing: a line &quot;Minimum daily rate for this car&quot; or &quot;Maximum daily rate for this car&quot; brings it back. Only an Admin allows a price outside them: <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Allow a price outside the car&#39;s price limits (Admin only)</b>, with the reason.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The renter has 48 hours to accept (and sign the amendment) or decline, with one reminder. Any extra is charged to their Card on File; a lower price raises a refund for your approval.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-review-requests" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review requests</h2><p class="gd-p">Every renter is asked for a review by email and text, as they chose, only from 9 am to 9 pm Toronto time. Nothing needs setting up.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Message</th><th scope="col">When</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mid-trip check</td><td>Rentals of 2 days or more, 24 hours after the pickup: &quot;How is the car? Reply or call if anything is off.&quot; No review ask.</td></tr><tr><td>Review request</td><td>1 hour after the check-out. It links the review page: the renter taps what they liked, adds a sentence, and gets a short draft to copy and post on Google.</td></tr><tr><td>Reminder</td><td>24 hours after the request.</td></tr><tr><td>Final follow-up</td><td>7 days after the request. Nothing more after it.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The booking page has the card Review requests: each message with when it went or when it will go, and why it stopped.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Ask for a review</b> sends the request now (or at 9 am if it is later than 9 pm), on any booking on a trip, returned or closed. Not twice in 24 hours.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On hold: a return or later charge (late return, kilometres, fuel, cleaning, smoking, damage, tolls and tickets) is not settled or waived, or an incident or dispute is open. The request goes by itself once they are. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send anyway</b> to send it now.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Mark reviewed</b> stops the messages when the renter tells you they already reviewed.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The messages also stop by themselves when the renter presses &quot;I already left a review&quot;, leaves a review on the site, unsubscribes, or a Google review is matched to them. <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Reviews</b> has the numbers (requests sent, on hold, reviews detected, the average rating), the hold list and the Google reviews to match.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The draft is made only from what the renter picked and wrote, and from the booking (the car, how long, delivery or pickup). Everyone gets the Google link, whatever their stars; a renter who gives 3 stars or fewer also sees &quot;Something wasn&#39;t right? Tell us directly&quot;.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-what-the-owner-sees-and-owner-deductions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What the owner sees, and owner deductions</h2><p class="gd-p">Each booking on an owner&#39;s or partner&#39;s car shows the card What the owner sees at the top of its page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hide from the owner</b> keeps the booking&#39;s revenue from the owner until the car is returned, or until the owner statement covering it is approved. The owner sees the booking as Booked with its dates, and the calendar still shows the car busy. Add a reason if you like: it is kept in the history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show to the owner</b> shows it now. Approving the statement shows every hidden booking on it by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Not shown to the owner is for a booking with no owner revenue (an insurance placeholder, a shareholder&#39;s or the owner&#39;s own use at no charge): the owner sees only that the car is unavailable for those dates. A booking with revenue cannot be set this way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add a rental and Send an offer have What the owner sees. It starts from Settings &gt; Program, Owners and fleet: Owners see a booking&#39;s revenue (right away by default).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">On the Money tab, Owner deductions on this booking: <b class="gd-ui">Add a booking expense</b> (cleaning, repair, fuel, platform fee or other, the amount, the reason the owner reads, a receipt number) comes off before Owner Revenue.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Set the Revenue Share for this booking</b> applies within the car&#39;s signed terms. Above the terms only an Admin can, with Above the signed terms ticked and the reason. <b class="gd-ui">Back to the car&#39;s terms</b> undoes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Add a rental has the same under The car&#39;s owner.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The owner&#39;s statement carries each booking that counts toward the owner&#39;s revenue, at its true amounts, and lists each deduction with its reason, so the payout is always right. A booking billed to the renter always counts. Left out: a booking billed to an insurer and hidden from the owner (while Program settings keep only insurance replacements hidden), an insurer-billed rental that does not block the calendar, and a rental with &quot;Counts toward the owner&#39;s revenue&quot; off. The booking page says when a booking is not part of the owner&#39;s revenue and why. When a booking that was left out starts counting (Blocks the calendar turned on, shown to the owner, or billed to the renter), the owner gets the new booking email once, at that moment. Customer service and sales add deductions only while Program settings let them change fees.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-email-the-renter-or-the-adjuster" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Email the renter or the adjuster</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b> at the top of a booking, or open its <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Write a <b class="gd-ui">Subject</b> and a <b class="gd-ui">Message</b>, or pick a <b class="gd-ui">Quick reply</b> to start from (Settings &gt; Quick replies keeps them).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Email the renter</b>. It goes from CarmaCars (bookings@carmacars.ca) and replies come back to the bookings inbox. The renter also sees it in their account and can answer there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking an insurer pays, choose <b class="gd-ui">From</b>: CarmaCars, or Blind Spot Car Rental (insurance). <b class="gd-ui">Email the adjuster</b> writes to the adjuster&#39;s email on the booking (Insurance claim), always from Blind Spot Car Rental.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> section is the booking&#39;s Activity log (release 35): what you and the renter wrote, every email of the booking, the texts, chat, calls, notes, events, payments, documents and visits, newest first, with a chip for each type and a search. The email form is under the log; each email you send shows in the log with your name.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Emails go out through the same daily limit as every email (the line under the form shows today&#39;s use). A message to a renter goes before digests and marketing; past the limit it waits until midnight. To write to a renter from <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b>, open the renter: Email the renter is at the bottom, about their latest booking or the one you pick.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Record the pickup or the return now (details later)</h3><p class="gd-p">When the car went out or came back but the checklist could not be done (no photos, no time, the renter dropped the keys), the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Check-in, check-out and signing</b> card has <b class="gd-ui">Record the pickup now (details later)</b> on a confirmed booking and <b class="gd-ui">Record the return now (details later)</b> while the car is on rent. Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the odometer and fuel if you know them, and why. The booking moves on (on rent, or returned), late return charges follow the actual time, and Fleet gets the task <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings for CC-...</b>. A car overdue or due back today also has <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b>: on the To do list (Check-ins and check-outs today), on Bookings &gt; Now and at the top of the booking page, which the late return alert opens. It asks only the return time (now, or earlier) and the km and fuel if you know them, and records the return the same way. Once returned, the statement can be issued and the deposit settled; releasing the deposit before the photos are in needs an Admin and a reason. A pickup without the deposit taken needs an Admin to waive it with a reason, and without the renter&#39;s signature on the check-in report an Admin&#39;s reason too. Later, <b class="gd-ui">Add the check-in (or check-out) photos and readings</b> opens the usual checklist (photos, readings, your signature): the task closes when it is saved.</p><p class="gd-p">The Agreement card says <b class="gd-ui">Waiting for the renter&#39;s details</b> when the renter still has blanks to fill (date of birth, address, mobile, licence, coverage): their account asks for them before signing and paying. No email or text is sent.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Find a booking</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> has one search box: type the booking number (CC-1042, cc1042 or just 1042), the renter&#39;s or a driver&#39;s name, an email, a phone number in any format, a plate (spaces do not matter) or a car code, then press Enter. The status filters still apply to what is found.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Record a card payment taken outside the site</h3><p class="gd-p">A card taken in the Stripe Dashboard, or on a card reader, is recorded on the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab with <b class="gd-ui">Record card payment</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose what it paid: <b class="gd-ui">Rental and fees</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Rental</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Later charges</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Deposit hold</b>, and where it was taken.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Last 4 digits</b> and the amount. A Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard) is optional for a payment: press <b class="gd-ui">Look up</b> and the amount and last 4 digits are checked against Stripe.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record it</b>. A payment confirms a booking waiting for payment, as any payment does.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A deposit hold needs its Stripe payment id, so it can be captured or released from <b class="gd-ui">Settle the deposit</b>. It is recorded as held, with the usual release reminders. A hold on a reader lapses after 2 days, one made online after about 30 days on Visa, Mastercard, Amex and Discover cards, and about 7 days otherwise.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Link a payment taken outside the platform</h3><p class="gd-p">A charge or a card deposit taken in the Stripe Dashboard or through a Stripe payment link is linked to its booking by an Admin, on the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab: <b class="gd-ui">Link a payment taken outside the platform</b>, in the rental panel or the deposit panel.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Paste the Stripe payment id (pi_... or ch_..., from the payment in the Stripe Dashboard). <b class="gd-ui">Look up</b> shows what Stripe says: the amount, paid or a hold, and the card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Link as a rental payment</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Link as the deposit</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>It must be in Canadian dollars and not already linked. A rental payment may not be more than is open for the rental and fees. A deposit must be the whole deposit: a hold waiting to be captured is kept as held (settle it as any hold), a charged deposit is kept as captured. <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Unlinked Stripe</b> lists, every night, the Stripe payments of the last 60 days that no booking knows, with a best guess of the booking.</div></aside><h3 class="gd-h3">Charge or hold the deposit on the card reader</h3><p class="gd-p">With the S700 paired (Settings &gt; Card reader), the <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab has <b class="gd-ui">Charge on reader</b> (everything open, the rental, the fees or a later charge) and <b class="gd-ui">Hold deposit on reader</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send to the reader</b>: the amount shows on the reader and the renter taps, inserts or swipes the card. The screen updates by itself; <b class="gd-ui">Cancel</b> stops the reader and nothing is charged. A deposit hold is captured or released from Settle the deposit like any hold.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Credit card coverage: the same card</h3><p class="gd-p">When the renter&#39;s coverage is their credit card, the whole rental (rental and fees) is paid on that same card. The Money tab says which card. Another card on the pay page is refused and refunded at once; on the reader it is refused before the money is taken; a payment by e-Transfer, cash or the like is refused; a card typed by hand needs its last 4 digits and the box <b class="gd-ui">This is the same card</b>. Deposits and later charges can go on any card. If the renter truly has to use another card or method, press <b class="gd-ui">Allow another card</b> and give the reason (an Admin).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-booked-as-soon-as-the-renter-accepts-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Booked as soon as the renter accepts (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking is booked the moment the renter approves the offer. It takes the car on every calendar, the fleet board, the car&#39;s availability and the counts, even before the payment or the pickup is recorded. Payment and the handover show as their own badges: <b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Pickup not recorded</b>. The first renter to approve gets the car: any other open offer on the same car and dates goes back to Requests with a Re-offer To do.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Booked, payment due</b> To do: a booked rental still unpaid within 48 hours of its pickup. Send the pay link, charge the saved card or record the payment.</li><li>Record the pickup To do: a pickup time that passed with nothing recorded, as before.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer, <b class="gd-ui">The offer as the renter sees it</b> sits right under <b class="gd-ui">Send the offer</b>: check it before you press it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-changes-after-signing-an-amended-agreement-no-new-signature" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Changes after signing: an amended agreement, no new signature</h2><p class="gd-p">The rental terms (section 15.4) let CarmaCars update a booking after signing: an extension, new dates or times, a price adjustment, a fee, a car swap. The signed agreement keeps applying. Each change makes a new version of the agreement marked <b class="gd-ui">Amended</b> with the date, carrying the renter&#39;s original signature, and the renter is sent it. Nobody is asked to sign again, except an additional driver who never signed (they sign before driving).</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen</h2><p class="gd-p">On the booking page, <b class="gd-ui">Check in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Check out (return)</b> are one screen: the time (now unless you change it), the odometer, the fuel, the photos and a note. Pick many photos at once from the camera roll or take them; tag an angle on any photo if you like. The suggested angles (front, each corner and side, rear, odometer, fuel gauge, interior front and rear, trunk, wheels, any damage) tick themselves as photos are tagged. Nothing is required but the time; the renter&#39;s own photos are added to the same report, each marked with who took it (the renter or staff) and its angle. The one-screen checklist is the button above it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-type-into-the-blind-spot-agreement" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Type into the Blind Spot agreement</h2><p class="gd-p">On the <b class="gd-ui">Rental agreements</b> card, <b class="gd-ui">Type into the Blind Spot agreement</b> shows each box as the form prints it. Change a value and <b class="gd-ui">Save the corrections</b>: it is drawn in that box, and the insured vehicle, the claim number, the adjuster and missing km or fuel go back onto the booking. <b class="gd-ui">Preview the filled form</b> opens it with your corrections.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-reopen-an-expired-offer-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Reopen an expired offer (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">An expired offer reopens in one click: <b class="gd-ui">Reopen offer</b> on the booking or on the <b class="gd-ui">Expired</b> filter of Requests. The renter gets the usual offer email and text; the offer stays open 24 hours unless you type other hours. When the pickup time has passed, the dialog asks for the new pickup and return first. A renter can also press <b class="gd-ui">Ask to reopen this offer</b>: you get the To do &quot;Renter wants expired offer reopened&quot; and an alert, as for a new request.</p><p class="gd-p">An offer sent after its pickup time no longer expires by itself: it expires at its own expiry time (the pickup only counts when the offer was sent before it and the pickup is 2 hours past). The offer screens say <b class="gd-ui">Pickup time has passed: update it</b> and do not send until you move the pickup.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-one-booking-page-six-sections-release-31" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One booking page, six sections (release 31)</h2><p class="gd-p">A booking has six sections: <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b> (the next step; the review and offer while it is being arranged), <b class="gd-ui">Money</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Drivers &amp; documents</b> (with the agreement), <b class="gd-ui">Car &amp; handovers</b> (the check-in and check-out, the photo report, signing on this device, what the owner sees), <b class="gd-ui">Messages &amp; history</b> (with the review request) and <b class="gd-ui">Claims &amp; extras</b> (changes, extensions, add-ons). Customer service, Sales, Fleet and Finance see the sections their work needs. An old link to a tab opens the section that holds it now.</p><p class="gd-p">Admin and staff open the same booking page, the same car page and the same listing review: you see every section and button, each staff function sees the parts it works with (Fleet has no Money section; only customer service and you have <b class="gd-ui">Claims &amp; extras</b>; refunds are asked for by you or Finance). A staff link to a booking opens the same page in the staff portal.</p><p class="gd-p">Every list has one search box (it finds names, numbers, plates, phones, emails and VINs) and one row of at most five chips. <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> removes every filter; the last one you used comes back next time on this device.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-charge-the-renter-after-the-return" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Charge the renter after the return</h2><p class="gd-p">Once the car is back, the Money tab has one action for everything owed after the trip: <b class="gd-ui">Charge the renter</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Charge the renter</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the <b class="gd-ui">Reason</b> from the list and add a note if it helps (Other needs its note). Enter the <b class="gd-ui">Amount</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Read the line under it: it says where the money comes from before anything moves. The deposit hold while it is still valid and covers the amount (the rest of the hold is released at the same time); otherwise the card on file; otherwise a pay link to the renter by text or email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Charge $...</b>. If the hold expired meanwhile, the card on file is charged instead, with the same amount and reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Release</b> stays its own button. The renter&#39;s receipt shows the reason.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-deposit-charged-to-a-debit-or-prepaid-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A deposit charged to a debit or prepaid card</h2><p class="gd-p">When the deposit is charged instead of held on a debit or prepaid card (Charge the card on file as the deposit), the renter also pays the <b class="gd-ui">Card processing fee for a debit deposit</b> (Program settings, 2.9% and $0.30 by default): a separate, non-refundable amount on the same charge. The Money tab&#39;s history and the receipt show it; the deposit refund returns the deposit only.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-what-the-renter-sees-still-to-do" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">What the renter sees still to do</h2><p class="gd-p">While a booking waits to be signed and paid, the Next step quotes the renter&#39;s own Sign and pay card, for example: The renter sees: &quot;Two steps left: sign the rental agreement, then pay $...&quot;. Signed for an older version of the offer counts as not signed: the renter signs the updated agreement on their Sign and pay page.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-override-a-pickup-or-a-return-that-must-go-ahead-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Override a pickup or a return that must go ahead (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">Sometimes the trip has to start (or end) even though a check still stops it. On the booking page, a confirmed booking (or one waiting for payment) and a car on rent show <b class="gd-ui">What stops the pickup now</b> (or the return) with each check in plain words: the deposit not taken, the rental agreement not signed, no renter signature on the check-in report, a licence or identity not verified, the coverage not confirmed, an additional driver who has not accepted, the payment still due, the calendar switch off, the car not marked available, maintenance overdue, the Ontario licence, the fleet insurance policy (when that rule is on in Program settings), the agreement&#39;s claim details, the tracker; at a return, an odometer lower than at pickup.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Override and record the pickup</b> (or the return).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Give the actual time (now, or earlier), the km and fuel if you know them, and why the trip must go ahead. The reason is required.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press the button. The pickup (or the return) is recorded at that time, only the checks listed are passed, for this booking and this once. The booking&#39;s history and the audit log say who, when, why and which checks; every Admin gets the alert Override used. A payment still due is not waived: the booking is confirmed with the balance open, and the deposit is still to collect (it is not waived). The photos and readings come later, as with Record now.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">When staff (Fleet, customer service, Sales, field staff) need it, they press <b class="gd-ui">Ask an Admin to override the pickup</b> (or the return) on the same card with the time they recorded. You get the alert Override asked for and a line on the To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> (one tap) and it is recorded with the time they entered, or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with a note. The request also shows on the booking page, with Approve and Decline.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-record-a-past-trip-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Record a past trip (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">A trip that happened but was never recorded (the pickup and the return both passed): on the booking page press <b class="gd-ui">Record a past trip</b>. Give the actual pickup and return times, the km and fuel at each if you know them, and the reason. Every check that would stop it is overridden as above, in one step: the booking lands in <b class="gd-ui">Returned</b>, the late return charges follow the actual return time, and the deposit can be settled. The car&#39;s status today is left as it is, and the renter is not sent a &quot;your rental started&quot; email for a trip long over. Fleet gets the task to add the photos and readings. Staff ask for it the same way; you approve in one tap.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-book-it-now-an-offer-that-is-a-booking-at-once-release-33" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book it now: an offer that is a booking at once (release 33)</h2><p class="gd-p">When you send an offer (answering a request, or <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> without one), tick <b class="gd-ui">Book it now (no renter approval)</b> above Send. The offer becomes the approved version at once: the booking waits for payment, the car is held for its dates as for any approved offer, and the renter gets one link to the <b class="gd-ui">Sign and pay</b> page to sign and pay (the &quot;approve your offer&quot; email is not sent). To have them sign and pay with you, open the booking: <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>, then take the card on this device. When customer service or Sales tick it, the offer goes out and you get the alert Override asked for and a To do line: <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> in one tap books it the same way. The booking&#39;s history says who booked it and that the renter did not approve it.</p><p class="gd-p">Already sent the offer? Tell Claude or the assistant: &quot;Book the offer of CC-10482 now, the renter agreed by phone&quot;. Claude&#39;s connector has the tool <b class="gd-ui">Book an offer now</b>, and <b class="gd-ui">Send an offer</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Make an offer</b> take Book it now too; the assistant (Assistant at the top of the menu) takes it in the same sentence as the offer. Each is two steps: you see what will change (nothing is changed yet), then you confirm, and the booking waits for the renter to sign and pay as above. As an Admin it is done at once; when customer service or Sales ask the assistant, it waits for your one-tap Approve.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-request-replaced-by-a-newer-one" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A request replaced by a newer one</h2><p class="gd-p">When a request or offer expired and the renter made a newer one for the same car and dates, the old one is hidden from Requests and keeps its number and history. Both booking pages say so under the title: <b class="gd-ui">Replaced by #CC-10483</b> on the old one and <b class="gd-ui">Replaces #CC-10482</b> on the new one, each a link to the other. Customer service, Sales and the other staff pages show the same note.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-change-protection-release-41" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change protection (release 41)</h2><p class="gd-p">How damage to the car is covered is one control on the booking page: the <b class="gd-ui">Protection</b> card at the top (Overview and the Money tab). An Admin, customer service and fleet use it on any booking; sales on a request or an offer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>. A small window lists the three options: <b class="gd-ui">Own insurance (OPCF 27)</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Credit card coverage</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Protection Plan</b>, each with the price difference (the plan shows its price a day times the days, plus HST), the deposit (no coverage rule changes it) and what the renter provides.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The rule is the same as on the renter&#39;s page: credit card coverage needs the renter&#39;s card picked from the coverage list, a card that covers this car, and the renter&#39;s confirmation that they pay with it; OPCF 27 needs the renter&#39;s confirmation that they upload their policy; otherwise the Protection Plan. An Admin can tick Admin override: the reason is recorded on the change and in the booking history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Write the reason (required; the renter reads it) and press <b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">What happens: the booking is repriced at once. More to pay is a balance to collect on the Money tab; less, when the plan was paid, is a refund for an Admin to approve. No money moves by itself. An offer is sent again as a new version; a confirmed booking or a rental in progress gets the amended agreement (the renter signs the new version when the rules ask) and one email. Proof tasks follow the new option. Changes are refused after damage is reported on the booking.</p><p class="gd-p">A renter&#39;s request to leave the Protection Plan shows on the same card with their proof (<b class="gd-ui">Open the proof</b>). Customer service or an Admin presses <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> (the change is made and the coverage confirmed) or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b> with a note the renter reads. The task &quot;The renter asks to leave the Protection Plan&quot; opens the booking.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-change-the-car-before-pickup" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Change the car before pickup</h2><p class="gd-p">On a request, an offer or a confirmed booking that is not picked up yet, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the car</b> at the top of the booking.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the new car. Only cars free for the whole booking are listed, each with its new total and the difference.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Say why the car changes, then press <b class="gd-ui">Change the car</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The price comes from the new car&#39;s rate sheet (its rates, the km included and the rate per km). The coverage, the drivers and the add-ons stay as they are.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An offer is sent again with the new car: that offer is the renter&#39;s one email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">On a confirmed booking, more to pay is left open: the renter sees <b class="gd-ui">Pay the balance</b> on their booking, or you send a pay link or charge the saved card from Money. Less to pay becomes a refund that waits for approval, with a To do for Finance. The renter gets one email, <b class="gd-ui">Booking updated</b>, with the new car and the money.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The open handover and return jobs move to the new car. The agreement gets a new version for the renter to sign; its link goes by text.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The booking&#39;s history and the audit log keep who changed it, from which car, to which car and why.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Customer service and Admins change any of them; Sales changes a request or an offer; Fleet changes a confirmed booking. Once the car is out, use <b class="gd-ui">Swap vehicle</b> instead.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-accident-card-of-a-booking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The accident card of a booking</h2><p class="gd-p">Every booking from confirmation to the return shows its <b class="gd-ui">Accident card</b>: the steps after an accident and the coverage this booking uses.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>OPCF 27: the renter&#39;s own insurer and policy number, from the proof they uploaded.</li><li>Credit card coverage: the card and its coverage provider, from their proof.</li><li>Protection Plan: the provider, the policy number and the claims phone from Settings &gt; Program (Tolls and damage), with the renter&#39;s plan reference.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Print the card</b> for the printable card. The renter has the same card on their booking. It never shows the fleet policy.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-close-ended-trips" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Close ended trips</h2><p class="gd-p">A back-dated close sends the renter no email or text. Fleet gets a To do when a trip is still open 2 hours after its return time, and the morning digest lists how many are open.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b> shows a banner when trips have ended and are not closed; <b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b> lists each one: never picked up in the system, on rent after the return, or returned and never closed. Fleet and Finance have the same page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Tick one or several, then <b class="gd-ui">Mark them</b>: returned on time, returned late (give the time it came back), or a no-show (an Admin or customer service).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the deposit: <b class="gd-ui">Deduct the balance owed</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Deduct the late fee</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Release in full</b>. A card hold that has expired is marked settled at once (released by expiry: no money moves).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">If no deposit was taken, an Admin fills <b class="gd-ui">Admin: deposit not taken, waive it because</b> (the same field is in Record a past trip).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing is released by itself: the decision waits under <b class="gd-ui">Deposit decisions waiting for an Admin</b>, and an Admin presses <b class="gd-ui">Release</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Release now (tolls window)</b>).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-return-charges" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Return charges</h2><p class="gd-p">A late return is charged per started extra day at the booking&#39;s full daily cost (the rental per day after discounts, plus per-day and per-trip fees such as the Protection Plan, never delivery), and only the started hours after the whole days get the hourly late fee. On the booking&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> tab, each renter line not on a statement yet has <b class="gd-ui">Change amount</b> (lower) and <b class="gd-ui">Waive</b>, with the reason; it is in the booking history and the next assessment keeps it. An expired card hold after the return has <b class="gd-ui">Mark settled (released by expiry)</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-switching-a-booking-to-the-protection-plan-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Switching a booking to the Protection Plan (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Change protection</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Protection Plan</b> uses the car&#39;s own plan price, the same amount the window quotes. It is no longer refused when Fees has no flat Protection Plan amount.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-protection-plan-priced-from-rentalcover-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Protection Plan priced from RentalCover (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The Protection Plan stays our product: renters never see the RentalCover name. Without the RentalCover partner key it is priced from the Protection Plan table, as before. Once the key is set, its price comes from a real RentalCover quote for the renter (their dates, their age at pickup, their name and email) plus our markup (20% unless <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b> changes it). The request form asks for the quote once the renter&#39;s details are in, and an offer as you choose option 3; a quote is reused for 15 minutes. A price you type for the plan wins. If RentalCover does not answer, the table price applies.</p><p class="gd-p">RentalCover covers up to $50,000 an incident, so the plan is offered only for a car worth less. The value used: your override under <b class="gd-ui">Value for the Protection Plan</b> on the car&#39;s page when set, else the car&#39;s Canadian Black Book value, else an AI estimate from typical listing prices that the site makes by itself (<b class="gd-ui">Refresh the AI estimate</b> asks again). A car with no value counts as over the limit: the request form, the offer screen and the database then offer only OPCF 27 or credit card coverage.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-extensions-at-the-all-in-price-a-day-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extensions at the all-in price a day (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">An extension costs what the renter already pays, averaged per day: the booking&#39;s total for the booked period (the rental after discounts, every fee, one-time fees like delivery included, and HST) divided by its days, for each added day. A booking of $729.36 for 7 days costs $104.19 for each added day. Added hours under a day cost the hourly late fee with HST, never more than a day. There is no extension discount.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Where</th><th scope="col">What happens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The renter&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Extend</b> page</td><td>Each option shows the total and the price a day before paying</td></tr><tr><td><b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a confirmed or on-trip booking, made longer</td><td>The booking&#39;s new total is the all-in price of the longer stay; the per-trip fees stay as booked and the rental charge takes the difference</td></tr><tr><td>The next period of a long rental</td><td>Keeps the rate of the booked period (the rental a day, per-trip fees scaled)</td></tr><tr><td>An insurer-billed booking</td><td>Priced as before</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="gd-p">The extension is one line on the booking, &quot;Extension: 3 days at $104.19/day (all-in)&quot;, HST included. Its HST is the booking&#39;s own share of HST, so invoices and the books never add HST on top. Type a rental charge in <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> to set another price. Late returns are unchanged: the daily cost of each extra day and the hourly late fee.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-fixed-amount-per-payment-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A fixed amount per payment (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a weekly, every 2 weeks or monthly plan, an Admin can set <b class="gd-ui">Fixed amount per payment</b> in <b class="gd-ui">Change the plan</b>. Each payment is that amount and the last one takes the remainder. The total and the payments already made never change. Leave it empty to split the payments by the days again.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-request-as-sent-and-every-offer-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The request as sent and every offer (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a request or a booking, <b class="gd-ui">Original request, as the renter sent it</b> shows the car, dates, places, coverage, add-ons, note and the price the renter saw, exactly as sent; staff changes never touch it. <b class="gd-ui">Offer history</b> lists every offer version, newest first: its status, who sent it and when, the car and dates, the message, how the total moved, and the price breakdown.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">To go back to an old version, press <b class="gd-ui">Revert to this offer</b> on it. Its car, dates, price, deposit, discount and fees load into the review as a new offer, highlighted.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the price, then send it in step 3. Nothing changes until you send.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Coverage</b> line at the top says what the renter chose (own insurance OPCF 27, credit card, Protection Plan) and its proof: not sent yet, waiting for review, confirmed, or rejected with the reason.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-send-an-offer-in-three-steps-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Send an offer in three steps (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Car and dates</b>: the renter, the dates, the car and where they pick it up and return it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price</b>: filled in from the rate sheet with the checkout&#39;s fees and discounts. Change it only if you agreed another price.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Review and send</b>: what changed, the message and how the link goes.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Rarely used options (billing an insurer, how it is paid, the calendar) are under <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>. Send waits while the price is being worked out again after a date change, and one tap sends once.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-the-owner-s-own-trip-instant-bookings-and-book-it-now-releas" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The owner&#39;s own trip, instant bookings and Book it now (release 35)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Owner&#39;s own trip ($0)</b>: the owner booked their own car. There is nothing to price or send; get the car ready.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Instant (repeat renter)</b>: a Gold renter or above (Rewards, release 40) with a verified licence and nothing owing booked an available car at once and went straight to sign and pay. An Admin can take a renter&#39;s instant booking away with <b class="gd-ui">Take instant booking away</b>, on the booking page or on the renter&#39;s page.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Any car, any time</b> (release 40): a Platinum renter asked for dates the car shows as taken. Fleet gets an urgent task due within 4 hours: confirm it, offer an equivalent car or an upgrade, or decline with a reason. Never cancel or move another renter&#39;s confirmed booking for it. The task closes when the request is answered.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Book it now</b> pressed by staff waits for an Admin&#39;s one-tap approval.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-secondary-contact-and-rideshare-documents-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Secondary contact and rideshare documents (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">The booking shows the renter&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Secondary contact</b> when they gave one: call them when the renter cannot be reached. Rideshare and delivery driving are welcome (rental agreement, section 10.3): never tell a renter it is not allowed. When a renter makes <b class="gd-ui">rideshare documents</b> (Uber, Lyft, DoorDash and others), you get an alert and the booking shows the letters they made.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-offers-coverage-delivery-and-fuel-releases-35-and-36" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Offers, coverage, delivery and fuel (releases 35 and 36)</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Sending an offer is three steps: car and dates, price, review and send. Every request shows the renter&#39;s original request as sent and every offer version, with who sent it and when; reverting loads an old version as a new offer to send.</li><li>Instant booking: a verified Gold renter or above books an available car at once, signs and pays; the booking is marked Instant (repeat renter), and an Admin can take instant booking away from a renter.</li><li>Card coverage is checked against the car: the card, the car&#39;s value, its type and the rental length. A card that does not cover it cannot be approved. OPCF 27 needs both the pink slip and the endorsement page.</li><li>Delivery is priced by distance from the company&#39;s address (1570 Midland Ave, Scarborough): a base, the kilometres included and a rate per km, all in Program settings; a car&#39;s own fee stays as an override.</li><li>The fuel line at the return is suggested from the car&#39;s tank, the weekly pump price and a multiplier, plus the refuelling fee, and checked on the deposit review before any charge.</li><li>Owner price limits: the daily minimum and maximum of a car or an owner hold every price, discount and offer; only an Admin can allow one request outside them, with a reason.</li><li>Rideshare and delivery work is allowed with the documents the renter makes on their booking page (rental agreement copy, coverage letter, vehicle letter); staff get an alert when they are made. The secondary contact shows on the booking.</li><li>Mid-trip review ask: halfway through a trip of several days, the renter gets one short message asking how it is going; a problem they report becomes a To do for customer service.</li><li>A car that has only test bookings can be deleted by an Admin; the test bookings go with it. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-check-in-and-check-out-on-one-screen-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check-in and check-out on one screen (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in (pickup)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out (return)</b> on the booking, and <b class="gd-ui">Check in</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Check out</b> on the To do list, open the same screen field staff use, made for a phone held in one hand:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every part is on one page in the order you do it, with a green tick once it is complete: the ready check, the renter, licence and card (one tap each), the odometer, fuel and keys, the photos, damage, the tracker, then the signatures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">What is known is filled in: the odometer and fuel from the Tracker when it reported in the last 30 minutes (else from the car&#39;s last report), the keys, and Standard for the cleanliness of a return. Check each against the car and change what differs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Photos are one tap each: <b class="gd-ui">Take this photo</b> always shows the next angle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">What is optional is folded away: new damage, a note, belongings, a renter who is not there or will not sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The button at the bottom says what is still needed (for example &quot;Next: Odometer&quot;) and takes you to it. When everything is in, press <b class="gd-ui">Hand over the keys</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Complete the return</b>.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Nothing was dropped: the condition report still needs every photo, the readings and the signatures, and the database refuses a handover with anything missing. Leave the page and come back: your answers and photos are still there.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Check in with photos already taken (from the gallery)</b> is still under the button, for a car that was photographed earlier.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="requests-offers-and-bookings-a-late-return-is-a-choice-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A late return is a choice (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">A car that comes back after the grace period is never charged by itself. The booking shows <b class="gd-ui">Late return</b> with how late the car was and five choices, each with what it costs:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge as an extension</b>: every started day late at the booking&#39;s daily rate, as an extension would have cost.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge extra days</b>: you choose the days, from 1 up to the started days, at the daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge the late return fee</b>: the fee of the rental terms (whole days at the daily rate, the started hours after them at the hourly fee, capped a day).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Charge a custom amount</b>: type the amount before tax and what it is for. The renter sees the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Waive it</b>: no charge, with the reason.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the late return charge</b>. The charge goes on the return statement and is taken as every return charge is: from the deposit, then the card on file, then a pay link. The renter gets a message on the booking that says what was chosen, and the booking history keeps who chose and why.</p><p class="gd-p">Until someone chooses, nothing is charged for the late return and Fleet has the To do &quot;Late return: choose the charge&quot;. Field staff can choose on the return screen as they complete the return.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A custom amount above your single limit, and a waiver by anyone other than an Admin, Finance or Fleet, waits for an Admin: they get the To do &quot;Late return: approve the charge&quot; and press <b class="gd-ui">Approve as asked</b>, or choose another way. Only an Admin changes a late return that is already decided, and not once it is on a statement or paid.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Close ended trips</b>, marking a trip returned late and choosing <b class="gd-ui">Deduct the late fee</b> is the same choice of the late return fee, made there. The other deposit choices leave the late return to be chosen on the booking.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'fleet-and-listings', 'chapter', 'calendar-sync-with-turo-and-other-platforms', 'Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.

## Vehicles

**Cars** > **Vehicles**

1. Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.
2. Search by plate, model or owner. **Cars** > **Rates for many cars** changes the rates of many cars at once.
3. Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.

![](/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles; pins: 1 74.3 31.1, 2 37.5 24.3, 3 48.6 52.4")

## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

5. Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: **Program settings** (the tiers there), **Off for this car**, or **Its own tiers** (a table like the one in Program settings). Press **Save**.
6. **Price limits**, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. **This car** sets the car''s own; the owner''s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car''s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press **Save price limits**. Owners set the same limits in their portal.

> Good to know: Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car", brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, **More options**, tick **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)** and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

## Fleet tracking

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the **Fleet tracking** tab. Fleet staff have the same map as **Fleet map** in their menu, and field staff see the cars of their own jobs under **Map**. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. Positions are seen by Admins and fleet staff only.

1. The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.
2. The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.
3. Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car''s power, and the trip under way.
4. **Alerts**: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press **Show** to see where, **Seen** when it is handled, or **Mark all as seen**.
5. **Trips by booking**: each booking''s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.

## Pair a tracker with a car

1. A new tracker that reports shows under **Trackers**, "Reporting, not on a car yet". Press **Pair**, choose the car and the install date.
2. Or press **Pair a tracker** and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).
3. The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner''s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car''s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.
4. **Remove** takes a tracker off a car (tick "faulty" for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.

## Tracking settings

Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before "not reporting" (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car''s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).

1. Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA''s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.
2. **Make the ingest key**: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.

> Tip: The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), **2 Cover plates**, **3 Review** and **4 Live on the site**. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with **Retry**.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day''s free AI share: a plate it finds is covered (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press **Undo** on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or **Not a plate: no plate visible** on a cover put where there is no plate.

To cover a plate yourself, press **Cover the plate** on the photo. The editor opens right under it.

1. Check the box over the plate, or press **Suggest the plate**.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. Under Cover the plate with, keep **The CARMA Ontario plate** (on a rear plate: the company''s own Ontario plate CARMA, drawn in the photo''s perspective and light) or **Edit the front plate out** (on a front photo: the bumper is filled in, no box), or choose **A CarmaCars plate**, **Pixelation** or **Blur**. Photos covered the old way are made again the new way by themselves.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows

1. On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press **Remove** under it, then **Remove it**. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing''s photos change in the review instead (Reject).
2. Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.
3. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings > Usage counts them.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room''s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings > Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car''s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car''s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with **Apply showroom to this car** or **Apply showroom to every car**.

## Failed photos

The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has **Retry failed photos** in its note; **Retry failed photos** at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.

## The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)

The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.

- **Primary photo is not exterior** is a flag and a filter in **Cars** > **Vehicles**: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.
- **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every outside photo of the car again in the showroom with the image model. Nothing changes if it cannot finish: the photos stay as they were. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.
- The same press checks the car''s **Other detail** photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.
- Every outside photo has the same room behind it. When the car cannot be cut out cleanly, Gemini replaces the background from the original photo instead of leaving the place it was taken in.
- The plate stays on the car''s plate: the CarmaCars plate is drawn only where a plate can be, never on the wall sign or the model name. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back, never blurred.
- **Redo every car with Gemini** (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) brings every car to the current photo standard: today''s Gemini allowance now, the rest by themselves over the next days, 10 calls a day kept for new photos.

## The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer

On a listing, under **First photo**, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.

- **Plain car**: the cover photo as it is (the default).
- **With a model**: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.
- **Flyer**: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.

**Make it again** makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** (First photo "flyer" and First photo "with a model"); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.

## Marketing photos in other scenes

For Marketplace and social posts, a car''s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.

1. On a listing, under **Marketing photos**, choose a scene, or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, and press **Make the marketing set**.
2. The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.
3. **Download (ZIP)** takes the set; the Marketplace kit''s **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the same set.

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Marketing scenes** lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders'' own cars. To use another, press **Change the reference photo** and pick one (the shareholders'' cars'' photos come first), or upload one. The scenes'' names and words are in the **Marketing scenes** setting.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Test bookings and deleting a car

1. On a booking made only to try the site, press **Mark as a test booking** (Admins only; the reason is optional). **Make it a real booking again** undoes it.
2. A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.
3. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Field staff take shifts you publish with **Publish shifts**. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day''s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. **To a shift** moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.', 'Fleet and listings', 'Vehicles, the listing pipeline, similar cars and covering licence plates.',
  'Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.

## Vehicles

**Cars** > **Vehicles**

1. Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.
2. Search by plate, model or owner. **Cars** > **Rates for many cars** changes the rates of many cars at once.
3. Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.

![](/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles; pins: 1 74.3 31.1, 2 37.5 24.3, 3 48.6 52.4")

## Set a car''s rates and kilometres

Open the car, then the **Rates** tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.

1. Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.
2. Kilometres: keep **Use the defaults** (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car''s class), or choose **Custom for this car** and type them.
3. Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.
4. Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press **Save the rates**.

| Rate | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Daily rate | A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday |
| Weekend rate | A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day |
| Weekly rate | The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more |
| Monthly rate | The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more |

5. Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: **Program settings** (the tiers there), **Off for this car**, or **Its own tiers** (a table like the one in Program settings). Press **Save**.
6. **Price limits**, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. **This car** sets the car''s own; the owner''s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car''s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press **Save price limits**. Owners set the same limits in their portal.

> Good to know: Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, "Minimum daily rate for this car" or "Maximum daily rate for this car", brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, **More options**, tick **Allow a price outside the car''s price limits (Admin only)** and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.

> Tip: A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on **Add a car**, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.

## Fleet tracking

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the **Fleet tracking** tab. Fleet staff have the same map as **Fleet map** in their menu, and field staff see the cars of their own jobs under **Map**. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. Positions are seen by Admins and fleet staff only.

1. The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.
2. The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.
3. Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car''s power, and the trip under way.
4. **Alerts**: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press **Show** to see where, **Seen** when it is handled, or **Mark all as seen**.
5. **Trips by booking**: each booking''s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.

## Pair a tracker with a car

1. A new tracker that reports shows under **Trackers**, "Reporting, not on a car yet". Press **Pair**, choose the car and the install date.
2. Or press **Pair a tracker** and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).
3. The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner''s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car''s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.
4. **Remove** takes a tracker off a car (tick "faulty" for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.

## Tracking settings

Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before "not reporting" (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car''s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).

1. Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA''s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.
2. **Make the ingest key**: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.

> Tip: The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).

## The listing pipeline

Open **Cars** > **Listings**. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.

1. Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.
2. Press **Start a listing** to begin one for a car that has none.
3. Open a car to review it.

![](/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings; pins: 1 53.5 37.0, 2 87.2 21.1, 3 32.6 37.0")

## Review a listing

1. Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: **1 Photos** (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), **2 Cover plates**, **3 Review** and **4 Live on the site**. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with **Retry**.
2. Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press **Not a duplicate** or **Same car**. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.
3. The copy is written by itself from the car''s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.
4. Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.

![](/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1100; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 20.6 16.6, 2 86.1 47.5, 3 19.9 106.8, 4 74.9 106.8")

## Cover the licence plate

The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day''s free AI share: a plate it finds is covered (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press **Undo** on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or **Not a plate: no plate visible** on a cover put where there is no plate.

To cover a plate yourself, press **Cover the plate** on the photo. The editor opens right under it.

1. Check the box over the plate, or press **Suggest the plate**.
2. Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.
3. Under Cover the plate with, keep **The CARMA Ontario plate** (on a rear plate: the company''s own Ontario plate CARMA, drawn in the photo''s perspective and light) or **Edit the front plate out** (on a front photo: the bumper is filled in, no box), or choose **A CarmaCars plate**, **Pixelation** or **Blur**. Photos covered the old way are made again the new way by themselves.
4. Press **Save the covered photo**. **Clear the boxes** starts over.
5. No plate in the shot? Press **No plate visible on this photo**.

![](/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg "desktop; size: 690 703; address: carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449; pins: 1 42.5 83.8, 2 49.6 29.9, 3 4.3 77.4, 4 15.5 83.8, 5 18.1 91.2")

> Tip: The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.

## Publish

1. A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press **Set rates and publish**. The daily rate is filled in (the car''s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press **Publish now**.
2. On the car itself, the Listing tab has **Publish now**; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.
3. From a listing review: press **Approve and publish**, **Approve, publish later**, or **Send back** with what to fix.

> Watch out: The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show "Plate not checked" on such photos.

## Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows

1. On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press **Remove** under it, then **Remove it**. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing''s photos change in the review instead (Reject).
2. Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.
3. A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.

## A listing without photos yet: sample photos

A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.

1. Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car''s details.
2. The car page and the car''s card show a sample photo, captioned "Sample photo", so renters know it is not this car. Staff see "Using sample photos" on the car and in Listings.
3. Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.
4. Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.

## Sample photos

**Settings** > **Sample photos**. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.

1. Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).
2. Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press **Add the photo**.
3. The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. **Turn off** or **Delete** a photo you no longer want.
4. Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with **Add photos**.

![](/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos; pins: 4 26.8 28.9")

## Publish now, and new cars published by themselves

Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.

1. **Settings** > **Program**, **Publish new cars automatically** (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner''s application is approved.
2. Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has **Publish now**. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.
3. Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.
4. An owner''s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.
5. A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press **Publish now**.

## The checklist: what is still open on a listed car

Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car''s Listing tab and after Publish now.

| Item | What it means |
| --- | --- |
| Paperwork | Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate |
| Insurance | Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over |
| Details | Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing |
| Photos | No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is |
| No VIN yet | A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it |
| Possible duplicate | An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site |
| Owner terms | The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner''s terms or the standard grid |

## The fleet policy rule at handover

A program owner''s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.

- Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.
- The handover refuses the car until the insurer''s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.
- Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.

## Cars on sample photos

**Cars**, **Listings** ends with **Cars on sample photos**: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).

1. Where a handover photographed the car, press **Use the handover photos**. They go into the car''s listing as if taken on the capture screen.
2. When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.
3. A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press **Start a listing** and take them.

> Good to know: The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings > Usage counts them.

## A car''s registration and documents

Open the car, then **Owner & documents**. The **Registration** card:

1. Correct the **VIN** (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the **Year** and the **Body style**.
2. Type the **Ontario permit number** and the date the **Plate sticker expires**. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.
3. Under **Documents**, choose the kind (**Ownership permit**, Safety Standards Certificate, owner''s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press **Upload**. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner''s checklist.
4. For the **Safety Standards Certificate**, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.
5. **Add a car** takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under **Documents (optional)**.

## A car added under the wrong owner

Open the car, Overview, **Who supplies the car**, **Move to another owner**. Choose the owner, or **CarmaCars (owner not known yet)**: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.

- The car''s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.
- It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.

### The VIN from the car, not typed

Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car''s **Registration**, **Start a listing**) has **Scan the barcode** and **Photo of the VIN**. Scan the barcode in the driver''s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone''s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.

### Photos in any order

**Add photos** on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. **Cover the plate** opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.

Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model''s name behind it) are made again with **Frame the outside photos again** above the photos of the listing, then **Yes, frame again**. The cover and the main outside views get the model''s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.

## Showroom photos

Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room''s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings > Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car''s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car''s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model''s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.

- A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press **Apply showroom to this car** above its photos, then **Yes, apply**.
- Every car at once: **Listings** > **Showroom photos** > **Apply showroom to every car**, then **Yes, every car**.
- Under a photo in the showroom: **Redo** makes it again, **Back to the original** puts back the version before the showroom.

A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with **Apply showroom to this car** or **Apply showroom to every car**.

## Failed photos

The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings**: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has **Retry failed photos** in its note; **Retry failed photos** at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.

## The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)

The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.

- **Primary photo is not exterior** is a flag and a filter in **Cars** > **Vehicles**: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.
- **Redo photos with Gemini** on the car page makes every outside photo of the car again in the showroom with the image model. Nothing changes if it cannot finish: the photos stay as they were. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.
- The same press checks the car''s **Other detail** photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.
- Every outside photo has the same room behind it. When the car cannot be cut out cleanly, Gemini replaces the background from the original photo instead of leaving the place it was taken in.
- The plate stays on the car''s plate: the CarmaCars plate is drawn only where a plate can be, never on the wall sign or the model name. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back, never blurred.
- **Redo every car with Gemini** (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) brings every car to the current photo standard: today''s Gemini allowance now, the rest by themselves over the next days, 10 calls a day kept for new photos.

## The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer

On a listing, under **First photo**, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.

- **Plain car**: the cover photo as it is (the default).
- **With a model**: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.
- **Flyer**: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.

**Make it again** makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in **Settings** > **Program settings** > **Listings** (First photo "flyer" and First photo "with a model"); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.

## Marketing photos in other scenes

For Marketplace and social posts, a car''s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.

1. On a listing, under **Marketing photos**, choose a scene, or **Mix: a different scene on each photo**, and press **Make the marketing set**.
2. The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.
3. **Download (ZIP)** takes the set; the Marketplace kit''s **With scenes (ZIP)** takes the same set.

**Settings** > **Program settings** > **Marketing scenes** lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders'' own cars. To use another, press **Change the reference photo** and pick one (the shareholders'' cars'' photos come first), or upload one. The scenes'' names and words are in the **Marketing scenes** setting.

## Extra photos

A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, **Extra outside photos** (put on the studio background) and **Extra inside and detail photos** (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car''s page.

1. In the review, **Extra photos, in their order on the car page** lists them.
2. Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press **Earlier** or **Later**.
3. Press **Save the order**.

## Fix a cut-out

When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press **Edit the cut-out** under the outside photo.

1. **Cut-out** shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose **Erase** and brush over what should go, or **Restore** and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set **Brush size** and **Zoom**; when zoomed, **Move the view** pans. **Undo** takes back the last stroke.
2. **On the studio** shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use **Size** to make it larger or smaller. **Centre and full size** puts it back.
3. Press **Save as a new version**. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. **Reset to the automatic cut-out** starts again from the automatic one.

> Good to know: If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows **Make the cut-out** first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.

Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with **Use original colours** under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin > Settings > **Program settings** (Listings) with **Auto-enhance listing photos**. The photo as uploaded is always kept.
## Import photos from a Google Drive link

The owner often hands over a car''s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.

**One car.** On the car''s listing, under the capture, **Import photos from a Google Drive link**. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press **Import the photos**. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, **Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in**, is on by default.

**Many cars.** **Cars** > **Import photos from Drive** (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder''s link and press **Read the folder**. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick **Import**, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with **Do not import this folder**. A line marked **Check this one** matched two alike cars. Then press **Import N photos from M folders**.

1. The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.
2. The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).
3. **Try the failed photos again** takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.

> Good to know: JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.

> Good to know: Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In **Settings**, the **Photo import from Google Drive** box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive''s warning pages.

## Test bookings and deleting a car

1. On a booking made only to try the site, press **Mark as a test booking** (Admins only; the reason is optional). **Make it a real booking again** undoes it.
2. A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.
3. A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.

## Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)

On a car''s page, **Pickup from owner and return to owner** records the car''s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. **Add photos** adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car''s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.

## Incident cards (release 34)
**Cars** > **Vehicles** > **Incident cards** prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press **Incident card** to print only that car; on the list, **Print all cars** prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press **Add the policy** (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.

## Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job

**Cars**, then **Field jobs**, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Shifts are published by themselves from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day by default, 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift), with a shift of its own for any handover or return no shift covers; **Publish shifts** adds more by hand, and a shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them. **Missing check-in and check-out**, on the same page, lists every past rental without its photos and readings, with **Give to field staff**. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day''s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking''s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. **To a shift** moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with **Unassign** (tick **Tell them** to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Vehicles is the fleet. Listings turns a car into a page on carmacars.ca in four steps: photos, covered plates, a review, and live on the site.</p><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-vehicles" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Vehicles</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b></p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by status; More filters has who supplies the car, retired cars and the mode. Each row shows the plate, class, owner, mode, status, listing and daily rate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Search by plate, model or owner. <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Rates for many cars</b> changes the rates of many cars at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car for its tabs: Overview, Rates, Fees and coverage, Calendar, Listing, and Owner, documents, tracker. The Tracker card links to Fleet tracking.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-08-vehicles-desktop-46461f49.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.3%;top:31.1%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:37.5%;top:24.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:48.6%;top:52.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-set-a-car-s-rates-and-kilometres" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Set a car&#39;s rates and kilometres</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then the <b class="gd-ui">Rates</b> tab. Everything on it saves together, in one step.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type the four rates. Only the daily rate is needed: an empty weekend rate is the daily rate, an empty weekly rate is 6 days at the daily rate, and an empty monthly rate is 22 days.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Kilometres: keep <b class="gd-ui">Use the defaults</b> (the kilometres a day in Settings, Kilometre choices, and the extra kilometre rate in Fee defaults for the car&#39;s class), or choose <b class="gd-ui">Custom for this car</b> and type them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Check the deposit (the class default is filled in), and the delivery and pickup fees: each is one way, an empty pickup fee is the delivery fee, and 0 means not offered.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Read What renters pay under the fields: real prices for a weekend, a few weekdays, a week and a month, worked out the way bookings are priced. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rates</b>.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Rate</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Daily rate</td><td>A price per day, for each day that starts on a Sunday, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday or Thursday</td></tr><tr><td>Weekend rate</td><td>A price per day, not for the whole weekend: each day that starts on a Friday or Saturday. Friday 10 am to Sunday 10 am is 2 days at this rate; Sunday to Monday is a daily day</td></tr><tr><td>Weekly rate</td><td>The price for 7 days. Rentals of 7 to 29 days cost this for each 7 days, counted by the day. A 1 to 6 day rental never costs more</td></tr><tr><td>Monthly rate</td><td>The price for 30 days. A 7 to 29 day rental never costs more</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Lead-time pricing for this car, below the rates: <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (the tiers there), <b class="gd-ui">Off for this car</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Its own tiers</b> (a table like the one in Program settings). Press <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Price limits</b>, beside them: the lowest and highest daily rate the owner accepts. <b class="gd-ui">This car</b> sets the car&#39;s own; the owner&#39;s line sets them for every car of that owner (a car&#39;s own come first, field by field). Empty is no limit. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save price limits</b>. Owners set the same limits in their portal.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Price limits hold the rental a day (after lead-time pricing, the non-refundable discount, a discount, a promo code or a price typed by hand; never fees, add-ons or tax) between the minimum and the maximum: one line, &quot;Minimum daily rate for this car&quot; or &quot;Maximum daily rate for this car&quot;, brings it back. Never on an Owner Booking or a booking billed to an insurer. To price one request outside them, open its review screen, <b class="gd-ui">More options</b>, tick <b class="gd-ui">Allow a price outside the car&#39;s price limits (Admin only)</b> and say why: it is kept on the booking and in the audit log. Untick it and the limits apply again.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A problem shows on its own field, in words, as you type. When similar cars have rates, a line suggests them with Use these; it is only a hint. The same fields are on <b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b>, so a car can be added with its rates in one pass.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fleet-tracking" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fleet tracking</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Fleet tracking</b> tab. Fleet staff have the same map as <b class="gd-ui">Fleet map</b> in their menu, and field staff see the cars of their own jobs under <b class="gd-ui">Map</b>. Every car on the same map as the Live map, with who has it. Positions are seen by Admins and fleet staff only.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The four numbers: cars on rent, moving, parked, and open alerts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The map shows each car as its photo in a ring: green moving (the arrow is its heading), yellow engine on, blue parked, orange not reporting. The list beside it has every car with its renter, booking, when it is due back (late in red) and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press a car on the map or in the list for its card: last report, odometer, fuel, tracker battery, whether the tracker has the car&#39;s power, and the trip under way.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Alerts</b>: speeding, left Ontario, left your zone, still driving after the return time, low tracker battery, unplugged and not reporting. Each also comes to the bell and, with phone alerts on, under Urgent alerts. Press <b class="gd-ui">Show</b> to see where, <b class="gd-ui">Seen</b> when it is handled, or <b class="gd-ui">Mark all as seen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Trips by booking</b>: each booking&#39;s trips, kilometres and top speed (red at the speeding level). Press the last trip to draw its route on the map.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pair-a-tracker-with-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pair a tracker with a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A new tracker that reports shows under <b class="gd-ui">Trackers</b>, &quot;Reporting, not on a car yet&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Pair</b>, choose the car and the install date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Or press <b class="gd-ui">Pair a tracker</b> and type its device ID (the IMEI or serial number on the tracker).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The install date starts the Tracker Fee on the owner&#39;s invoice when the car has none yet. A replacement tracker keeps the car&#39;s first date; the old tracker is taken off by itself.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes a tracker off a car (tick &quot;faulty&quot; for a broken one). The Tracker Fee is not changed.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-tracking-settings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tracking settings</h2><p class="gd-p">Below the trackers: the speeding level (140 km/h), the minutes of grace after the return time (15), the low battery level (20%), the hours before &quot;not reporting&quot; (6), the Ontario alert, and one optional zone (a name, its centre and a radius in km). History keeps a moving car&#39;s position once a minute for 90 days, trips and alerts for 365 days (at most 365: the privacy policy keeps tracker data 12 months).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Demo mode (off): simulated cars drive the GTA&#39;s highways here and on the Live map, for a demonstration. Nothing is saved. Turn it off before the trackers go live.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Make the ingest key</b>: the relay or tracker service signs every batch of positions with it. It is shown once; making a new one stops the old one at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The Live map shows the same cars with its Fleet layer (tick Fleet).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-listing-pipeline" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The listing pipeline</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>. A draft waiting for review shows Needs review.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each row shows the car, plate, state, photos and the work done on it so far.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> to begin one for a car that has none.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open a car to review it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-09-listings-desktop-970819b6.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.5%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:87.2%;top:21.1%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.6%;top:37%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-review-a-listing" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Review a listing</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Steps to go live shows four numbered steps: <b class="gd-ui">1 Photos</b> (how many of the required photos are in, 14 for most cars, 13 for a two-seater with no rear seats), <b class="gd-ui">2 Cover plates</b>, <b class="gd-ui">3 Review</b> and <b class="gd-ui">4 Live on the site</b>. Each says what it needs and has one button to where it is done; the step to do now is in red. A step that stopped (a photo edit or the copy) shows under them with <b class="gd-ui">Retry</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Similar cars on file lists possible duplicates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Not a duplicate</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Same car</b>. An open flag does not keep the car off the site; only Same car does.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The copy is written by itself from the car&#39;s facts and published when it passes the checks: nothing to type. To change a line, press Change; that field is then locked and kept by every new version.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Under Photos, each public photo shows its plate state: Plate not checked, Plate covered or No plate visible.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1100"><img src="/guides/img/admin-10-listing-review-desktop-352745fd.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1100"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.6%;top:16.6%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86.1%;top:47.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:74.9%;top:100%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cover-the-licence-plate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cover the licence plate</h2><p class="gd-p">The plates are checked by themselves. Every photo is looked at by the vision model within the day&#39;s free AI share: a plate it finds is covered (the photo shows Covered automatically, with how sure it was), a photo with no plate is marked No plate visible (No plate seen automatically), and a photo it is not sure of stays Plate not checked for you. While photos wait, the Photos card says how many. A wrong decision: press <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> on the photo (the photo as it was comes back, Plate not checked), or <b class="gd-ui">Not a plate: no plate visible</b> on a cover put where there is no plate.</p><p class="gd-p">To cover a plate yourself, press <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> on the photo. The editor opens right under it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Check the box over the plate, or press <b class="gd-ui">Suggest the plate</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag over a plate to draw a box. Drag a box to move it, or its corner to resize it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under Cover the plate with, keep <b class="gd-ui">The CARMA Ontario plate</b> (on a rear plate: the company&#39;s own Ontario plate CARMA, drawn in the photo&#39;s perspective and light) or <b class="gd-ui">Edit the front plate out</b> (on a front photo: the bumper is filled in, no box), or choose <b class="gd-ui">A CarmaCars plate</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Pixelation</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Blur</b>. Photos covered the old way are made again the new way by themselves.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the covered photo</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Clear the boxes</b> starts over.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No plate in the shot? Press <b class="gd-ui">No plate visible on this photo</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/listings/704abf3d-8905-443d-a157-d52769cf7449</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:690/703"><img src="/guides/img/admin-11-plate-editor-desktop-4219ad93.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="690" height="703"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:42.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:49.6%;top:29.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:4.3%;top:77.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.5%;top:83.8%" aria-hidden="true">4</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:18.1%;top:91.2%" aria-hidden="true">5</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The covered photo replaces the public one; the original is kept privately. Keyboard: N adds a box, the arrows move it, Shift and the arrows resize it, Delete removes it.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A real car that is not on the site is a line on To do: press <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The daily rate is filled in (the car&#39;s own, or the suggested rate from similar cars or the class); change it if you like and press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On the car itself, the Listing tab has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>; each open item of its checklist has a button to where it is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">From a listing review: press <b class="gd-ui">Approve and publish</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Approve, publish later</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Send back</b> with what to fix.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The plate check never holds a car back: a real photo whose plate is not checked stays private (the other photos, or the sample photos, show instead) and goes public by itself once its plate is covered or marked not visible. Listings already live show &quot;Plate not checked&quot; on such photos.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-photos-filed-under-the-wrong-shot-and-interior-windows" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Photos filed under the wrong shot, and interior windows</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On the Photos card, each shot lists its photos. A photo filed under the wrong shot: press <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> under it, then <b class="gd-ui">Remove it</b>. The shot is free again: take or pick the right photo. The removed photo is kept privately and the removal is in the history. A live listing&#39;s photos change in the review instead (Reject).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Dashboard and seat photos: what shows through the windows is replaced by the studio background when the cut is clean (a quality check: some but not most of the frame seen through, high in the frame, a few clean regions, sharp edges). Otherwise the windows are blurred, and the photo is marked windows blurred. Nothing to do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with 2 seats or fewer needs no Rear seats photo.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-listing-without-photos-yet-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A listing without photos yet: sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A car can be listed before its photos are taken. Until then the site shows a sample photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Submit the listing without photos. The listing copy is still written for you from the car&#39;s details.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The car page and the car&#39;s card show a sample photo, captioned &quot;Sample photo&quot;, so renters know it is not this car. Staff see &quot;Using sample photos&quot; on the car and in Listings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Publishing does not wait for a plate check: a sample photo has no plate.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Add the real photos when they are taken. Once real photos are approved they replace the sample at once; nothing else to do.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Sample photos</b>. The pictures a car shows until its real photos are in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every body type has a built-in picture (sedan, SUV, truck, van, coupe, hatchback, electric car).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add your own: choose the Body type, and a Make and Model if the photo is of that exact model, pick the Photo, and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photo</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The most specific photo wins: make and model, then make and body type, then body type. <b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a photo you no longer want.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Cars using sample photos lists the cars still waiting for real photos. Each real car showing sample photos is also a line on To do, with <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/settings/sample-photos</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/812"><img src="/guides/img/admin-36-sample-photos-desktop-55c64070.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="812"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:26.8%;top:28.9%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-publish-now-and-new-cars-published-by-themselves" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Publish now, and new cars published by themselves</h2><p class="gd-p">Nothing between a new car and the site has to be finished first: the car goes on the site, and what is still open shows on its checklist.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Publish new cars automatically</b> (on by default): a new real car goes on the site by itself as soon as it has its year, make and model and its rates, when it is added with rates, when its rates are saved, when it is added for an owner, or when an owner&#39;s application is approved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Otherwise open the car: its Listing tab says why it is not on the site and has <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>. A car with no rates yet is published with the suggested rates (similar cars, else the class defaults in Program settings); change them later on the Rates tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car has its listing from the moment it is added, as a draft. It shows in Listings and in Not on the site yet until it is published.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s own application waits for your decision before its car is published by itself; Publish now still works.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A car taken off the site by staff, or scheduled for a later date, is never published by itself: press <b class="gd-ui">Publish now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-checklist-what-is-still-open-on-a-listed-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The checklist: what is still open on a listed car</h2><p class="gd-p">Open items never stop publishing. They show as warnings on the car&#39;s Listing tab and after Publish now.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">What it means</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Paperwork</td><td>Ownership permit, registry forms, agreements signed, Forms C and D, upfront payment, registry visit, tracker, safety certificate</td></tr><tr><td>Insurance</td><td>Not on the fleet insurance policy yet: the car can be booked, but not handed over</td></tr><tr><td>Details</td><td>Colour, body, seats, gearbox: the car page leaves out what is missing</td></tr><tr><td>Photos</td><td>No real photos: sample photos stand in. A photo whose plate is not checked stays private until it is</td></tr><tr><td>No VIN yet</td><td>A car added by its plate alone: add the VIN when you have it</td></tr><tr><td>Possible duplicate</td><td>An open flag in Similar cars. Only Same car keeps the car off the site</td></tr><tr><td>Owner terms</td><td>The management fee (Revenue Share) and fees not set: a request uses the owner&#39;s terms or the standard grid</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-fleet-policy-rule-at-handover" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The fleet policy rule at handover</h2><p class="gd-p">A program owner&#39;s car is listed and can be requested, offered and paid for while its paperwork is open. It is never handed over until the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet insurance policy.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Staff see a warning on a request and an offer for a car not on the policy yet.</li><li>The handover refuses the car until the insurer&#39;s confirmation is recorded (Owners and onboarding). The field app says so on the job.</li><li>Only real states keep a car off the site: retired, left the program, out of service, Turo only, bookings turned off, a self-managed owner in arrears, or a paused listing.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-cars-on-sample-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars on sample photos</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> ends with <b class="gd-ui">Cars on sample photos</b>: each real car whose page still shows sample photos, with its newest handover photos (the check-in and check-out photos field staff take).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Where a handover photographed the car, press <b class="gd-ui">Use the handover photos</b>. They go into the car&#39;s listing as if taken on the capture screen.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">When every required shot is there, the listing is submitted: the studio editor puts the car on the CarmaCars backdrop, then the listing waits for your review like any other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with no handover photos yet gets them at its next handover, or press <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b> and take them.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The studio editor uses Cloudflare image transformations (5,000 a month included). Settings &gt; Usage counts them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-s-registration-and-documents" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s registration and documents</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, then <b class="gd-ui">Owner &amp; documents</b>. The <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b> card:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Correct the <b class="gd-ui">VIN</b> (it is checked: 17 characters, the check digit, not on another car; decoded again for the body style and trim), the <b class="gd-ui">Year</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Body style</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Type the <b class="gd-ui">Ontario permit number</b> and the date the <b class="gd-ui">Plate sticker expires</b>. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before; save the new date after the renewal and the task closes.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>, choose the kind (<b class="gd-ui">Ownership permit</b>, Safety Standards Certificate, owner&#39;s insurance, other), pick the photo or PDF and press <b class="gd-ui">Upload</b>. The ownership permit clears that item of the owner&#39;s checklist.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">For the <b class="gd-ui">Safety Standards Certificate</b>, also type its number, the date it was issued and the date it expires. Fleet gets a task 30 days and 7 days before it expires; upload the new certificate with its dates and the task closes. It is a document on the car, not a service record, and nothing is billed to the owner.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a car</b> takes the ownership permit and the Safety Standards Certificate too, under <b class="gd-ui">Documents (optional)</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-a-car-added-under-the-wrong-owner" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car added under the wrong owner</h2><p class="gd-p">Open the car, Overview, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Move to another owner</b>. Choose the owner, or <b class="gd-ui">CarmaCars (owner not known yet)</b>: the car becomes a company car, with no owner schedule or terms.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>The car&#39;s unsigned owner application and vehicle schedule are withdrawn (kept in the history), and its draft owner invoices are deleted. Nobody is notified.</li><li>It is refused once anything for the car is signed, issued, paid or on a statement.</li></ul><h3 class="gd-h3">The VIN from the car, not typed</h3><p class="gd-p">Every VIN field (Add a car, Add a car for an owner, the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Registration</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Start a listing</b>) has <b class="gd-ui">Scan the barcode</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Photo of the VIN</b>. Scan the barcode in the driver&#39;s door frame or at the bottom of the windshield: the phone&#39;s camera reads it by itself. Or take a photo of the VIN plate or sticker: the barcode in it is read first, else the photo is read for the printed VIN. The VIN is checked (17 characters, the check digit; I, O and Q become 1 and 0) and decoded as when you type it. Check it against the car before saving.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">Photos in any order</h3><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> on the listing takes any number of photos at once from the camera roll. Each is sorted to its shot by itself (front three-quarter, sides, rear, dashboard, seats and the rest); a shot that already has its photo sends the new one to the extra photos, so nothing is replaced by accident. The shots are a guide, not a rule: a listing is complete with 10 photos that can go on the site and one outside photo for the cover. Outside photos get the studio background: the car is cropped to its edges and placed big in the frame with its wheels on the floor and a soft shadow under the tyres, and any corner watermark or caption beside the car is left out. Inside and detail photos are kept as taken; when one has a watermark, a logo or caption text on it, the edge with the mark is cut off by itself, and a photo whose mark cannot be cut off (one in the middle) stays off the site until you replace it. <b class="gd-ui">Cover the plate</b> opens on every outside photo with the plate box suggested; check it and save.</p><p class="gd-p">Outside photos made before the newest framing (the car small in the frame, or without the model&#39;s name behind it) are made again with <b class="gd-ui">Frame the outside photos again</b> above the photos of the listing, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, frame again</b>. The cover and the main outside views get the model&#39;s name lettered behind the car, as on the sample photos (for example CLA, C CLASS, AMG GT). The photos leave the site until their plates are checked again: the plate box is suggested on the new photos; check each and cover it. On a published listing each goes back on the site once its plate is checked.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-showroom-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Showroom photos</h2><p class="gd-p">Outside photos go in the CarmaCars showroom by themselves. When a real photographed room is stored (dealership or studio photos licensed for commercial use, fetched once from Wikimedia Commons with their author and licence kept), the car stands in it: about 70% of the width, its wheels on the room&#39;s floor, a soft shadow and a faint reflection under it, its light matched to the room, and no sign or lettering on the real wall. Program settings &gt; Listings has the switch (Photographed showroom rooms, on), the car&#39;s width and the cut-out quality floor: a cut-out that is not clean enough (pieces, a blurry or ragged edge) is never placed in a room, the real photo is used instead (its plate covered as usual) and the photo says so. Without a stored room it is the drawn dark showroom: a simple dark dealership with linear lights in the ceiling, a slatted wood wall between two light strips with a big lit CarmaCars sign, and a polished dark floor with the car&#39;s reflection and a shadow under each tyre. Every angle of a car is in the same room, and the cover has the model&#39;s name in metal letters on the wall under the sign. The image model may relight the car or turn it slightly; a photo that shows another car, model or colour is not used. <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> has the switch (Showroom photos, on), the image model that makes the photos look photographed, and its daily limit. Past the limit, or when the image model is not available, the site makes the showroom itself for free, and the photo says why under it.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li>A car whose photos were made on the black studio: press <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> above its photos, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, apply</b>.</li><li>Every car at once: <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Showroom photos</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Yes, every car</b>.</li><li>Under a photo in the showroom: <b class="gd-ui">Redo</b> makes it again, <b class="gd-ui">Back to the original</b> puts back the version before the showroom.</li></ul><p class="gd-p">A car that stays where it was keeps its plate check. When the image model made the photo, check the plate again: the photo is off the site until you do. Photos made in the first showroom are made again in the new one with <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to this car</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Apply showroom to every car</b>.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-failed-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Failed photos</h2><p class="gd-p">The site makes the photo sizes itself: the image service is asked only to cut the car out (<b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b>: the switch to let the image service make every photo step is off). When the image service is busy or over its allowance, the photo still goes on the site from the original and is made again later. A listing marked Failed has <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> in its note; <b class="gd-ui">Retry failed photos</b> at the top does every listing. They are made again a few at a time, and the listing leaves Failed when they are done.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-primary-photo-is-always-the-front-exterior-release-43" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The primary photo is always the front exterior (release 43)</h2><p class="gd-p">The first photo of every car on the site, in the cards, the feeds and the Marketplace kit is its exterior at the standard angle (front three-quarter, in the dark showroom). An inside photo is never ahead of an outside one, and the cover mark follows by itself whenever photos are added, made again or reordered.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Primary photo is not exterior</b> is a flag and a filter in <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>: it marks a car whose first photo is an inside one because its best outside photo is not on the site yet, or it has none. Add or approve an outside photo and the flag clears by itself.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Redo photos with Gemini</b> on the car page makes every outside photo of the car again in the showroom with the image model. Nothing changes if it cannot finish: the photos stay as they were. It needs the image model switched on in Program settings, Listings.</li><li>The same press checks the car&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Other detail</b> photos again: an outside view filed there is moved to the outside photos (the front three-quarter becomes the first photo) and made in the showroom. This is what clears the flag on a car that showed nothing to redo.</li><li>Every outside photo has the same room behind it. When the car cannot be cut out cleanly, Gemini replaces the background from the original photo instead of leaving the place it was taken in.</li><li>The plate stays on the car&#39;s plate: the CarmaCars plate is drawn only where a plate can be, never on the wall sign or the model name. Inside photos stay sharp from front to back, never blurred.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Redo every car with Gemini</b> (Listings, Showroom photos; Admin and Fleet) brings every car to the current photo standard: today&#39;s Gemini allowance now, the rest by themselves over the next days, 10 calls a day kept for new photos.</li></ul></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-the-first-photo-plain-with-a-model-or-a-flyer" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The first photo: plain, with a model, or a flyer</h2><p class="gd-p">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">First photo</b>, choose what shows first on the site and in the Marketplace kit. Switch any time; the other photos stay as they are.</p><ul class="gd-ul"><li><b class="gd-ui">Plain car</b>: the cover photo as it is (the default).</li><li><b class="gd-ui">With a model</b>: a car-show photo made by the image model, with a fully clothed adult model beside the car. It needs the image model; until it is made (or when the image model is not there) the plain cover shows, and the listing says why.</li><li><b class="gd-ui">Flyer</b>: the cover photo with a band like a printed flyer: the car, the price a day from its live rates, the call to action, a badge and the logo. When the price, the words or the cover photo change, it is made again by itself within 10 minutes; the plain cover shows meanwhile.</li></ul><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Make it again</b> makes the chosen one again. The words of the flyer and the description of the model are in <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Listings</b> (First photo &quot;flyer&quot; and First photo &quot;with a model&quot;); {car}, {price}, {weekly} and {monthly} are filled for each car.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-marketing-photos-in-other-scenes" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Marketing photos in other scenes</h2><p class="gd-p">For Marketplace and social posts, a car&#39;s outside photos can be made again in other scenes. The website keeps its own photos in the dark showroom: a marketing set never replaces them.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a listing, under <b class="gd-ui">Marketing photos</b>, choose a scene, or <b class="gd-ui">Mix: a different scene on each photo</b>, and press <b class="gd-ui">Make the marketing set</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The copies show as they are made. The dark showroom and the plain white studio are made by the site when the image model is not there; the photographic scenes (a bright showroom, a city street at night, the Toronto waterfront, a parking garage, Highway, a scenic road, Brick building) need the image model, and say so on the copy when it is not there.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download (ZIP)</b> takes the set; the Marketplace kit&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">With scenes (ZIP)</b> takes the same set.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> lists the scenes. A scene made in a real place has a photo of that place: Brick building picks its photo by itself: the widest outside photo, as taken, of the shareholders&#39; own cars. To use another, press <b class="gd-ui">Change the reference photo</b> and pick one (the shareholders&#39; cars&#39; photos come first), or upload one. The scenes&#39; names and words are in the <b class="gd-ui">Marketing scenes</b> setting.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-extra-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Extra photos</h2><p class="gd-p">A photo that fits no shot is an extra photo. Under the shots, <b class="gd-ui">Extra outside photos</b> (put on the studio background) and <b class="gd-ui">Extra inside and detail photos</b> (touched up) each take any number at once. They count toward the 10 photos, get the same plate check, and come after the standard shots on the car&#39;s page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">In the review, <b class="gd-ui">Extra photos, in their order on the car page</b> lists them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Drag a photo by its handle (⋮⋮), or press <b class="gd-ui">Earlier</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Later</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the order</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-fix-a-cut-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Fix a cut-out</h2><p class="gd-p">When the background removal cuts badly (a mirror or a wheel missing, background left beside the car), press <b class="gd-ui">Edit the cut-out</b> under the outside photo.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cut-out</b> shows the car over the photo as taken, shown faintly. Choose <b class="gd-ui">Erase</b> and brush over what should go, or <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> and brush over what the cut-out took off. Set <b class="gd-ui">Brush size</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Zoom</b>; when zoomed, <b class="gd-ui">Move the view</b> pans. <b class="gd-ui">Undo</b> takes back the last stroke.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">On the studio</b> shows the car on the studio background. Drag the car to move it and use <b class="gd-ui">Size</b> to make it larger or smaller. <b class="gd-ui">Centre and full size</b> puts it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Save as a new version</b>. The photo is made again in about a minute; the version before and the photo as taken are kept. <b class="gd-ui">Reset to the automatic cut-out</b> starts again from the automatic one.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>If the car did not move, the plate check carries over: a photo marked no plate visible stays so, and a covered plate is covered again on the new photo when the review is open. If the car moved, check the plate again. A photo made before cut-outs were kept shows <b class="gd-ui">Make the cut-out</b> first; the editor opens by itself when it is ready.</div></aside><p class="gd-p">Every photo also gets a light touch-up by itself (exposure, levels, a little contrast and colour, mild sharpening), never enough to change the paint colour or hide a scratch. Turn it off for one photo with <b class="gd-ui">Use original colours</b> under it (the photo is made again; approve it again), or for every photo in Admin &gt; Settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Program settings</b> (Listings) with <b class="gd-ui">Auto-enhance listing photos</b>. The photo as uploaded is always kept.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-import-photos-from-a-google-drive-link" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Import photos from a Google Drive link</h2><p class="gd-p">The owner often hands over a car&#39;s photos as a public Google Drive folder, or one big folder with a folder per make and then per car. You do not download them: paste the link.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">One car.</b> On the car&#39;s listing, under the capture, <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from a Google Drive link</b>. Paste the folder link (shared with Anyone with the link) and press <b class="gd-ui">Import the photos</b>. Every photo in the folder, and in the folders inside it, is added to this car as if you had pressed Add photos: each is sorted to its shot (else filed as an extra photo, in file-name order), put on the studio background and checked for its plate. The box under the link, <b class="gd-ui">Submit the listing for processing when its photos are in</b>, is on by default.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Many cars.</b> <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Import photos from Drive</b> (a button on Vehicles). Paste the top folder&#39;s link and press <b class="gd-ui">Read the folder</b>. The page walks every folder and proposes a car for each folder that holds photos, from the year, make, model, colour and plate in the folder names (the make folder above counts; 01 Motors partner cars come first). Check the table: tick or untick <b class="gd-ui">Import</b>, change the car in the list (the likely cars come first), leave out a folder with <b class="gd-ui">Do not import this folder</b>. A line marked <b class="gd-ui">Check this one</b> matched two alike cars. Then press <b class="gd-ui">Import N photos from M folders</b>.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The page follows the import by itself. You can leave it and come back: it runs in the background.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The end shows the summary: imported, skipped and failed, and why for each (a file over 15 MB, a file that is not a photo, the same photo already on the car, a folder not shared).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Try the failed photos again</b> takes only the ones that failed. Pressing Import on the same link again never adds a photo twice: a Drive file already on the car is skipped, and so is the same picture under another name. A photo you took off the car can be imported again.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>JPG, PNG, HEIC and WebP only (HEIC and WebP are made JPEG first). At most 15 MB a photo, 600 photos, 400 folders and 4 GB in one import. Drive is asked politely, one photo at a time; a big import takes a while.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Without a key, Drive shows only the first 50 files of a folder on its public page; a folder with more is read in full when Drive allows it. In <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Photo import from Google Drive</b> box takes a Google API key with the Drive API on (after it is saved only its last 4 characters are shown, and it is never written to the change log): with it, folders of any size are read and photos download without Drive&#39;s warning pages.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-test-bookings-and-deleting-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Test bookings and deleting a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a booking made only to try the site, press <b class="gd-ui">Mark as a test booking</b> (Admins only; the reason is optional). <b class="gd-ui">Make it a real booking again</b> undoes it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">A car whose bookings are all test bookings can be deleted: the test bookings and their test payments go with it, and a copy is kept in the archive of deleted requests.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car with a real booking cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-pickup-from-owner-and-return-to-owner-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pickup from owner and return to owner (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Pickup from owner and return to owner</b> records the car&#39;s condition when CarmaCars picks it up from its owner or gives it back: the date and time, km, fuel, many photos at once with the suggested angles, and notes. <b class="gd-ui">Add photos</b> adds more to a record later. The owner sees these records read only on the car&#39;s page in their portal. They are the baseline condition for any dispute.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-incident-cards-release-34" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Incident cards (release 34)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Incident cards</b> prints the card for each car: what to do in an accident or a breakdown, the support number from Settings, a roadside number when there is one, a QR code to report it in the app, and the fleet insurance slip. Open a car and press <b class="gd-ui">Incident card</b> to print only that car; on the list, <b class="gd-ui">Print all cars</b> prints them all, two cards to a Letter page with crop marks, ready to laminate. Under Fleet insurance policy press <b class="gd-ui">Add the policy</b> (the insurer, the policy number, the dates, the named insured, the roadside number on the slip) and choose the uploaded slip if you have one: it is printed as it is, otherwise the fields are. The card never shows a premium. Fleet staff print the same cards from their portal.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="fleet-and-listings-field-jobs-shifts-and-who-gets-a-job" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field jobs, shifts and who gets a job</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Field jobs</b>, is the board Fleet uses, with every action Fleet has. Shifts are published by themselves from the shift template in Program settings (one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day by default, 14 days ahead, only forward from the latest shift), with a shift of its own for any handover or return no shift covers; <b class="gd-ui">Publish shifts</b> adds more by hand, and a shift you cancel is not published again. Field staff take them. <b class="gd-ui">Missing check-in and check-out</b>, on the same page, lists every past rental without its photos and readings, with <b class="gd-ui">Give to field staff</b>. Jobs go on shifts, not on people: each job is put on the shift covering its time (or that day&#39;s), whoever holds the shift does it (several people share the jobs, least busy first), a shift nobody holds keeps its jobs for whoever claims it, and work lands only on days with shifts (work due on a day without shifts moves to the day before, or to the next day with shifts when it comes in on the day; the booking&#39;s own times never change). A booking whose handover or return falls on a day with no shifts shows a warning on the board and on the booking. <b class="gd-ui">To a shift</b> moves a job to another shift. You can give a job to a field person on a shift that day or to an Admin, take it off with <b class="gd-ui">Unassign</b> (tick <b class="gd-ui">Tell them</b> to let them know), and an Admin who holds a job opens it on the field portal. A person who has not passed the academy cannot be given a job or take a shift. A shift with jobs and nobody on it within 24 hours alerts Fleet and the Admins once.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand', 'chapter', 'fleet-and-listings', 'A car comes from one of three places: a program owner, CarmaCars itself, or a partner rental company. You add cars and rentals by hand, retire cars, and delete cars that were added by mistake.

## Add a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then **Add a car**. Start with the VIN: everything else about the car comes from it.

1. Type or paste the VIN. At the 17th character the car is looked up: one line shows the year, make, model, trim, body, seats, doors, fuel, drive, gearbox and engine. Press Edit only if something is wrong.
2. When the VIN fits several trims, the form asks which trim it is: press the one on the car''s papers or badge, or **Not sure** (Admin > Today asks again).
3. No VIN at hand? Press **No VIN at hand? Add the car by its plate** and choose the year, make and model from the lists. The VIN can be added later; the details fill in then.
4. Tap the colour (it is not in the VIN). Leave it empty and it is read from the cover photo once the car has one.
5. Check the class. It is set from the make, model, body and age (a 2016 Porsche Macan is Premium, an SUV is SUV) and the line under it says why. Change it if it is wrong.
6. Choose who supplies it: **A program owner''s car** (choose the owner; the car starts its onboarding), **CarmaCars-owned (company fleet)** (no owner; all of its revenue is CarmaCars'') or **A partner rental company''s car** (choose the partner; leave the commission empty to use the partner''s).
7. The daily rate is filled in from similar cars, else the class. Keep it, change it, or empty it and set the rates later on the car''s Rates tab. Press **Add the car**.

> Tip: The title, description and features are written by themselves right after the car is added, from the VIN details. Change any of them on the car''s listing; a field you change is kept.

> Good to know: Every car gets a fleet number and its standard settings the moment it is added: a complete rate card (the daily rate you typed or the suggested one, weekend, weekly and monthly from it, the kilometres a day, the extra kilometre rate, the deposit and the delivery and pickup fee of its class) and drivers 18 to 20 allowed. Each value set this way says (Set automatically) on the car''s Overview and Rates tab until you change it. The defaults come from Settings: Program and Fee defaults.

> Tip: A VIN that does not add up (one character misread) shows a warning; you can still save it. A VIN the decoder cannot read asks only the year, make and model and never stops you: the details fill in when it is read later. The duplicate check runs as for every car: a VIN only once, a plate on one active car, and a likely twin waits for you in Similar cars before it is published.

The gearbox comes from the government''s fuel economy data for the model when it has one gearbox for it, or from the VIN when the VIN states it. Seats come from the VIN, else from the seat table for 3-row SUVs and minivans (a Yukon XL or a Palisade is 8, 7 with captain''s chairs), else 4 for a coupe or convertible and 5 for a sedan or hatchback. An SUV or minivan with neither is left without seats and shows Seats missing in Vehicles: the 7+ seats filter cannot show it until you set them. When either is not certain, Admin > Today shows **Confirm gearbox and seats**: press the gearbox and the number of seats, then **Save**. A car whose VIN fits several trims shows **Pick the trim** there: press the right one. Either way the title, description and search text are written again.

On a car''s page, **Who supplies the car** shows the supplier and the commission, and changes them. Vehicles filters by supply type.

## Partners

**People** > **Partners**. Partner rental companies whose cars we rent out on commission.

1. Press **Add a partner**: business and legal name, contacts, HST number, commission and insurance with its expiry date.
2. Open a partner for its cars, bookings, statements, payouts and documents. A warning shows when its insurance expires soon, and Staff tasks gets a reminder (Program settings sets how many days before).
3. Banking (Admins only): **Save the payout account** for the account we pay the partner into. The account number is stored encrypted. Press **Verify** once checked.
4. Portal: **Invite to the owner portal** gives the partner the owner portal with its cars, bookings, statements and the partner agreement, filled in and signed on screen in three taps.
5. The partner signs only in the portal, with the e-signature: a signature on paper is not recorded. **Read the partner agreement** shows the text they sign.

## A partner fleet on its own rates

Some partners send a price sheet of their own rates instead of sharing what the renter pays. 01 Motors works this way: its whole fleet is on the site, and staff manage its cars (it has no portal sign-in yet; add its email on the partner page and invite it later).

1. **People** > **Partners** > the partner. **Pricing** shows how it works: our base rate is the partner''s listed rate less the partner discount (10% unless you set another), to the nearest dollar; then every rule of our own cars applies (the weekend rate, lead-time pricing, promo codes, the non-refundable discount), with every fee, the deposit and HST. CarmaCars receives a kickback of 20% of the listed rental (the partner''s rates times the days booked); the partner is owed the rest. Press **Edit pricing** to change the discount, the kickback or the basis for every car at once.
2. **Cars** lists each car with its listed rates a day (1 to 2 days, 3 or more, 7 or more) and our base rates. Press **Edit** on a car to change a negotiated rate, give that car its own discount or kickback, mark it **Insurance included** or **No credit card needed**, or confirm its model year. Our rates change at once.
3. **Kickback and payable** lists each rental: the listed rental, the kickback receivable, the amount payable to the partner and our rental charge, with the totals not on a statement yet.
4. The site shows these cars with their tiers (1 to 2 days, 3 to 6 days, 7 days or more) and "Guideline rates; final price confirmed after review". A car with insurance included needs no coverage choice from the renter (coverage option 4, confirmed by itself); a car with no credit card needed takes a debit card for the payment and the deposit. The deposit, the licence and identity checks and the ages stay the same.
5. The price sheet has no years, VINs or plates. Until you confirm the year, the site leaves it out and says "Year confirmed when you book"; an offer waits until the year is confirmed (Edit on the car, Model year). Add the plate and the VIN on the car''s page before its first handover.
6. Real photos: open the car (its name in Cars), **Photos**, and add them. Once approved they replace the eight studio stand-ins.

| 3 days on the C43 AMG Blue, booked 3 weeks ahead | Amount |
| --- | --- |
| Listed rental (3 x $225) | $675.00 |
| Our rental charge (3 x $203, the listed rate less 10%) | $609.00 |
| Booked ahead −5% | −$30.45 |
| Fees (delivery, young driver and the like) and HST | CarmaCars'' own, 100% |
| Kickback receivable (20% of $675) | $135.00 |
| Payable to the partner | $540.00 |

> Good to know: The partner''s monthly statement shows each rental at the listed rate, the kickback and the amount payable; never what the renter paid. A refund lowers the partner''s share in proportion; our discount, lead-time pricing and any discount CarmaCars gives do not. Offers sent and bookings confirmed before the change keep their prices and are paid as before.
## A partner''s CRM (01 Motors'' GoHighLevel)

**Settings**, the **Partners** tile, then the partner (or **CRM link** on the partner''s page). Their CRM gets our cars, kept up to date, and their cars come to us.

1. Ask the partner for a Private Integration token and their location ID (the box **What 01 Motors gives us** on the page says exactly what to create and which scopes to tick). Paste both and press **Connect**. The token goes to the vault; the page only ever shows its last four characters.
2. Connect tests the link (their location, objects, products and pipelines) and runs the first sync. After that it runs by itself every 15 minutes, and within five minutes of a change to a car, a rate, a photo, a booking or a block. **Test connection** and **Run sync now** do it at once.
3. **What 01 Motors sees**: CarmaCars'' own cars and program owners'' cars that are on the site, with rates, the next 60 days and photos, as records of a "CarmaCars Vehicles" object in their CRM (or as products when their plan has no custom objects). Partner cars are never sent: not theirs, not another partner''s. Press **Change what we share** to leave out program owners'' cars, rates, availability or photos.
4. **Partner price**: the site''s rates, or the site''s rates less (or plus) a percentage, to the nearest dollar.
5. **Their cars coming in**: name the object in their CRM that holds their cars (Test connection lists them), or their feed address. Each of their cars is matched to their car here, or added as their partner car (it waits off the site unless you choose otherwise), with their rates as its sheet rates, their booked dates as calendar blocks and their photos for a car with none. A car that waits shows **Add as their car**, **Link** or **Set aside**.
6. **Leads both ways** (off until you turn it on): requests for their cars, and requests that came through their booking links, become contacts and opportunities in the pipeline stage you choose; an opportunity they move to the stage you name becomes a lead in **Leads**.
7. **Feed, widget and booking links**: a JSON or CSV feed and a widget for their GoHighLevel funnels and sites (copy the iframe), and booking links carmacars.ca/p/01-motors/<car> that mark the request as theirs for 30 days. **New key** ends the old feed and widget addresses at once.

> Good to know: A link that has failed for an hour shows on Admin > Today. Disconnect deletes the token from the vault; what is already in their CRM stays there.

## Add a rental by hand

Press **Add a rental** at the top of Bookings (or on To do). For phone, walk-in, Turo, partner and insurer bookings, the owner using their own car, and placeholders: a rental already agreed. To send an offer instead, use Send an offer.

1. Standing with the renter at pickup? Press **Start at pickup**: type the renter''s name and phone, choose the car, type the kilometres and the fuel, and press **Hold the car and finish later**. The pickup is now; the car is held for 2 hours (renewed while you work on it) and you get a task to finish the rental.
2. Nothing is required to save: the form is saved as a draft as you type (**Save draft** saves at once). Unfinished rentals, on Bookings and on this page, lists every draft with who started it, when, and what is still missing; Finish it opens it where it was left, on any device. Tick Hold the car while I finish to keep the car off the calendar while you type (2 hours, renewed as you save). Discard drops it and frees the car.
3. Quick start sets the usual choices in one tap: **Phone**, **Walk-in**, **Turo or another platform**, **Insurance replacement**, **Owner using own car** or **Placeholder**.
4. Choose the car and the dates. The calendar and the price are checked by themselves: clashes with other bookings and the cleaning time after each trip. An Admin may book over a clash with a reason.
5. The dates decide the case, shown under them (nothing to tick): a pickup ahead is an upcoming rental, handed over at pickup as usual. A pickup already passed with the return ahead is a rental already underway: it is recorded as on trip from the pickup you enter, on any active car (even one closed to public bookings), and anything a handover checks that is still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit, condition report, insurance) becomes a task. A return already passed is a rental that has ended: kept as completed, paid another way or unpaid.
6. Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one: name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. Add any other drivers.
7. We deliver it, or we pick it up: pick the address from the suggestions and its distance from our location prices the delivery (shown under the address), as on Send an offer.
8. Check the price: every line of the price can be changed where it stands. Type a new amount in the line (the rental charge for the trip or a rate a day, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan, delivery, each add-on, the deposit, the kilometres a day); HST and the total follow. Add a line from the list or a charge of its own; Remove takes a fee off. The (i) beside each line says what it is and how it is worked out. One optional reason covers all the changes. At the top of the price, Amounts I type: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter paid for each line ("$270 after tax for the rental, $50 for the Protection Plan"): each is worked back to its amount before tax, and a line without HST stays as typed. The choice is remembered on this device. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that, to the cent, and the line under it shows each line before tax. The total shown is the total that is saved; if they ever differ, it says by how much before you save.
9. Any length: the dates may run past 30 days (up to the staff limit in Program settings, 730 days by default). From 30 days the rental charge is the monthly rate for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. On the booking, Monthly periods shows each period: its share, and its own version of the agreement (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Program settings: long_rental_agreement_lead_days, 3 by default), with what is due for it on the renter''s Balance due. With Program settings, Charge the saved card for each period, on, that share is charged to the saved card when the agreement goes out (the renter gets the receipt; a declined or missing card gives Finance a task).
10. A car whose listing is not finished (a draft listing, onboarding, no photos or no rates yet) can be rented at once: it shows Listing not finished in the car list and stays off the public site. With no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason.
11. An owner''s car that is not on the fleet insurance policy yet: only an Admin adds its rentals, and ticks I checked that this car is insured for this rental. An owner''s car needs its terms (Revenue Share) first. The handover still needs the car on the fleet policy: press **Insurer confirmed** once the insurer confirms it.
12. Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): choose the insurer (Not listed: type its name, and it is added to the list), the claim number, the adjuster, the days and the daily rate authorized, the provisional end, and whether the insurer pays everything or the rental only. The booking is billed to the insurer; the renter owes only what it does not cover. The daily rate authorized is filled from the insurer''s rate sheet for the car (Insurance replacements: rates and billing); a different rate needs the reason. Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver when the insurer authorized them (Insurance replacements: rates and billing).
13. The rent is paid by: e-Transfer or cash (received), card on file (charged when the renter signs), payment link, platform payout (Turo), insurer billed later, cheque, bank transfer, or unpaid. Paid in parts (some cash, some e-Transfer): press **Add another payment (paid in parts)** and type each amount. Then the deposit, its own way: card hold, cash, e-Transfer (with its reference and date) or no deposit.
14. Before you save checks it all in one box: the renter, the car, the days, the total, what was received and what is still to collect, the deposit (or No deposit) and the agreement.
15. The rental agreement is sent to sign online (a rental agreement signed on paper is not accepted). The calendar: untick Blocks the car''s calendar for an insurance replacement with dates not known yet, with the reason.
16. Tick **Do not email the renter** if they should not get the confirmation. Press **Add the rental**.

> Tip: The rental is on the calendars at once (a payment link waits for the payment). The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal (never on paper). With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign, and until then the rental is awaiting signature. On the booking, **Verified in person** records a licence checked at the counter. A rental already underway can be paid by payment link (the renter signs, then pays from their booking) or the saved card, like an upcoming one.

## Retire or delete a car

**Cars** > **Retire or delete**, or the car''s own page.

1. **Retire this car** takes the car off the site and the calendars and keeps every record. It needs no future confirmed booking. **Restore** brings it back.
2. **Delete this car** removes a car added by mistake, with its photos. Only a car with nothing tied to money (no confirmed or paid booking, payment, statement, toll or damage). Type the plate or the name to confirm.
3. Booking requests that never confirmed and never took money (requested, offered, declined, expired) do not stop a delete. The confirmation lists them; they are removed with the car and a copy is kept. The renters stay on file.
4. On the same page, **Delete all sample cars** deletes every sample car that meets the rule at once, with its requests. Type DELETE SAMPLE CARS to confirm; the ones kept show why, with the booking numbers.

## Sample cars on the site

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, or **Settings** > **Site**. The 20 example cars the site started with, so the fleet never looks empty while the real cars are listed.

1. **Hide sample cars** asks first ("Hide all 20 sample cars from the site?"); press **Hide them** to take every sample car off the site at once, or **Keep them**. Nothing else stops it: not an enquiry, not an old request.
2. **Show sample cars** puts the 20 back, with their photos and rates. Ones that were deleted are made again.
3. On the site each one is marked "Example car". They never appear in search engines or the sitemap.
4. A request on a sample car is never a booking. When the person picks dates, the car page and the request form show a real car free for them (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price) with one tap to switch to it. If they keep the sample car, it becomes an enquiry (number EQ-1001 and up) and customer service gets the task Suggest a similar real car, naming the free real car.

> Tip: Hide the sample cars once enough real cars are on the site. Delete all sample cars removes them for good.

## Why a car is not on the site yet

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the card Not on the site yet.

1. Every real car that is not on the site is listed with its next step first: the rates, Publish now, the listing review.
2. The same car is a line on To do with **Set rates and publish**. The car comes off both once it is on the site.
3. A car without photos is marked sample photos: once listed it shows a sample photo until its real photos are approved.

## Placeholder bookings

A placeholder is a booking held for an insurer, or as a hold, next to the real rental on the same car.

1. On **Add a rental**, press **Placeholder** (Admins). It never blocks the calendar, is never handed over, sends the renter nothing, earns no commission and is left off the Live map. The owner sees only that the car is unavailable. Type what it is for, or leave it empty.
2. Enter the real rental as usual, even for the same days: it blocks the car, and tolls, tickets and damage go to it.
3. A booking made another way can become one: on the booking, **More actions** > **Mark as a placeholder**. Not once money was taken or the car went out. **Make it a real booking** undoes it; then turn the calendar switch on if it should hold the car.
4. On the booking, **Competing for these dates** (and **Also on this car for these dates** once booked) lists everything else on the car for those days and says which one keeps it off the car. A placeholder never counts.

## Tolls when two rentals overlap

Bookings held for an insurer and other placeholders are never matched to a toll. When two real rentals overlap the toll time, nobody is charged automatically: the toll waits in the work queue under Two rentals, with both bookings, and you choose who pays.
', 'Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand', 'Add a car, partners, add a rental, retire or delete a car, sample cars and tolls with two rentals.',
  'A car comes from one of three places: a program owner, CarmaCars itself, or a partner rental company. You add cars and rentals by hand, retire cars, and delete cars that were added by mistake.

## Add a car

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then **Add a car**. Start with the VIN: everything else about the car comes from it.

1. Type or paste the VIN. At the 17th character the car is looked up: one line shows the year, make, model, trim, body, seats, doors, fuel, drive, gearbox and engine. Press Edit only if something is wrong.
2. When the VIN fits several trims, the form asks which trim it is: press the one on the car''s papers or badge, or **Not sure** (Admin > Today asks again).
3. No VIN at hand? Press **No VIN at hand? Add the car by its plate** and choose the year, make and model from the lists. The VIN can be added later; the details fill in then.
4. Tap the colour (it is not in the VIN). Leave it empty and it is read from the cover photo once the car has one.
5. Check the class. It is set from the make, model, body and age (a 2016 Porsche Macan is Premium, an SUV is SUV) and the line under it says why. Change it if it is wrong.
6. Choose who supplies it: **A program owner''s car** (choose the owner; the car starts its onboarding), **CarmaCars-owned (company fleet)** (no owner; all of its revenue is CarmaCars'') or **A partner rental company''s car** (choose the partner; leave the commission empty to use the partner''s).
7. The daily rate is filled in from similar cars, else the class. Keep it, change it, or empty it and set the rates later on the car''s Rates tab. Press **Add the car**.

> Tip: The title, description and features are written by themselves right after the car is added, from the VIN details. Change any of them on the car''s listing; a field you change is kept.

> Good to know: Every car gets a fleet number and its standard settings the moment it is added: a complete rate card (the daily rate you typed or the suggested one, weekend, weekly and monthly from it, the kilometres a day, the extra kilometre rate, the deposit and the delivery and pickup fee of its class) and drivers 18 to 20 allowed. Each value set this way says (Set automatically) on the car''s Overview and Rates tab until you change it. The defaults come from Settings: Program and Fee defaults.

> Tip: A VIN that does not add up (one character misread) shows a warning; you can still save it. A VIN the decoder cannot read asks only the year, make and model and never stops you: the details fill in when it is read later. The duplicate check runs as for every car: a VIN only once, a plate on one active car, and a likely twin waits for you in Similar cars before it is published.

The gearbox comes from the government''s fuel economy data for the model when it has one gearbox for it, or from the VIN when the VIN states it. Seats come from the VIN, else from the seat table for 3-row SUVs and minivans (a Yukon XL or a Palisade is 8, 7 with captain''s chairs), else 4 for a coupe or convertible and 5 for a sedan or hatchback. An SUV or minivan with neither is left without seats and shows Seats missing in Vehicles: the 7+ seats filter cannot show it until you set them. When either is not certain, Admin > Today shows **Confirm gearbox and seats**: press the gearbox and the number of seats, then **Save**. A car whose VIN fits several trims shows **Pick the trim** there: press the right one. Either way the title, description and search text are written again.

On a car''s page, **Who supplies the car** shows the supplier and the commission, and changes them. Vehicles filters by supply type.

## Partners

**People** > **Partners**. Partner rental companies whose cars we rent out on commission.

1. Press **Add a partner**: business and legal name, contacts, HST number, commission and insurance with its expiry date.
2. Open a partner for its cars, bookings, statements, payouts and documents. A warning shows when its insurance expires soon, and Staff tasks gets a reminder (Program settings sets how many days before).
3. Banking (Admins only): **Save the payout account** for the account we pay the partner into. The account number is stored encrypted. Press **Verify** once checked.
4. Portal: **Invite to the owner portal** gives the partner the owner portal with its cars, bookings, statements and the partner agreement, filled in and signed on screen in three taps.
5. The partner signs only in the portal, with the e-signature: a signature on paper is not recorded. **Read the partner agreement** shows the text they sign.

## A partner fleet on its own rates

Some partners send a price sheet of their own rates instead of sharing what the renter pays. 01 Motors works this way: its whole fleet is on the site, and staff manage its cars (it has no portal sign-in yet; add its email on the partner page and invite it later).

1. **People** > **Partners** > the partner. **Pricing** shows how it works: our base rate is the partner''s listed rate less the partner discount (10% unless you set another), to the nearest dollar; then every rule of our own cars applies (the weekend rate, lead-time pricing, promo codes, the non-refundable discount), with every fee, the deposit and HST. CarmaCars receives a kickback of 20% of the listed rental (the partner''s rates times the days booked); the partner is owed the rest. Press **Edit pricing** to change the discount, the kickback or the basis for every car at once.
2. **Cars** lists each car with its listed rates a day (1 to 2 days, 3 or more, 7 or more) and our base rates. Press **Edit** on a car to change a negotiated rate, give that car its own discount or kickback, mark it **Insurance included** or **No credit card needed**, or confirm its model year. Our rates change at once.
3. **Kickback and payable** lists each rental: the listed rental, the kickback receivable, the amount payable to the partner and our rental charge, with the totals not on a statement yet.
4. The site shows these cars with their tiers (1 to 2 days, 3 to 6 days, 7 days or more) and "Guideline rates; final price confirmed after review". A car with insurance included needs no coverage choice from the renter (coverage option 4, confirmed by itself); a car with no credit card needed takes a debit card for the payment and the deposit. The deposit, the licence and identity checks and the ages stay the same.
5. The price sheet has no years, VINs or plates. Until you confirm the year, the site leaves it out and says "Year confirmed when you book"; an offer waits until the year is confirmed (Edit on the car, Model year). Add the plate and the VIN on the car''s page before its first handover.
6. Real photos: open the car (its name in Cars), **Photos**, and add them. Once approved they replace the eight studio stand-ins.

| 3 days on the C43 AMG Blue, booked 3 weeks ahead | Amount |
| --- | --- |
| Listed rental (3 x $225) | $675.00 |
| Our rental charge (3 x $203, the listed rate less 10%) | $609.00 |
| Booked ahead −5% | −$30.45 |
| Fees (delivery, young driver and the like) and HST | CarmaCars'' own, 100% |
| Kickback receivable (20% of $675) | $135.00 |
| Payable to the partner | $540.00 |

> Good to know: The partner''s monthly statement shows each rental at the listed rate, the kickback and the amount payable; never what the renter paid. A refund lowers the partner''s share in proportion; our discount, lead-time pricing and any discount CarmaCars gives do not. Offers sent and bookings confirmed before the change keep their prices and are paid as before.
## A partner''s CRM (01 Motors'' GoHighLevel)

**Settings**, the **Partners** tile, then the partner (or **CRM link** on the partner''s page). Their CRM gets our cars, kept up to date, and their cars come to us.

1. Ask the partner for a Private Integration token and their location ID (the box **What 01 Motors gives us** on the page says exactly what to create and which scopes to tick). Paste both and press **Connect**. The token goes to the vault; the page only ever shows its last four characters.
2. Connect tests the link (their location, objects, products and pipelines) and runs the first sync. After that it runs by itself every 15 minutes, and within five minutes of a change to a car, a rate, a photo, a booking or a block. **Test connection** and **Run sync now** do it at once.
3. **What 01 Motors sees**: CarmaCars'' own cars and program owners'' cars that are on the site, with rates, the next 60 days and photos, as records of a "CarmaCars Vehicles" object in their CRM (or as products when their plan has no custom objects). Partner cars are never sent: not theirs, not another partner''s. Press **Change what we share** to leave out program owners'' cars, rates, availability or photos.
4. **Partner price**: the site''s rates, or the site''s rates less (or plus) a percentage, to the nearest dollar.
5. **Their cars coming in**: name the object in their CRM that holds their cars (Test connection lists them), or their feed address. Each of their cars is matched to their car here, or added as their partner car (it waits off the site unless you choose otherwise), with their rates as its sheet rates, their booked dates as calendar blocks and their photos for a car with none. A car that waits shows **Add as their car**, **Link** or **Set aside**.
6. **Leads both ways** (off until you turn it on): requests for their cars, and requests that came through their booking links, become contacts and opportunities in the pipeline stage you choose; an opportunity they move to the stage you name becomes a lead in **Leads**.
7. **Feed, widget and booking links**: a JSON or CSV feed and a widget for their GoHighLevel funnels and sites (copy the iframe), and booking links carmacars.ca/p/01-motors/<car> that mark the request as theirs for 30 days. **New key** ends the old feed and widget addresses at once.

> Good to know: A link that has failed for an hour shows on Admin > Today. Disconnect deletes the token from the vault; what is already in their CRM stays there.

## Add a rental by hand

Press **Add a rental** at the top of Bookings (or on To do). For phone, walk-in, Turo, partner and insurer bookings, the owner using their own car, and placeholders: a rental already agreed. To send an offer instead, use Send an offer.

1. Standing with the renter at pickup? Press **Start at pickup**: type the renter''s name and phone, choose the car, type the kilometres and the fuel, and press **Hold the car and finish later**. The pickup is now; the car is held for 2 hours (renewed while you work on it) and you get a task to finish the rental.
2. Nothing is required to save: the form is saved as a draft as you type (**Save draft** saves at once). Unfinished rentals, on Bookings and on this page, lists every draft with who started it, when, and what is still missing; Finish it opens it where it was left, on any device. Tick Hold the car while I finish to keep the car off the calendar while you type (2 hours, renewed as you save). Discard drops it and frees the car.
3. Quick start sets the usual choices in one tap: **Phone**, **Walk-in**, **Turo or another platform**, **Insurance replacement**, **Owner using own car** or **Placeholder**.
4. Choose the car and the dates. The calendar and the price are checked by themselves: clashes with other bookings and the cleaning time after each trip. An Admin may book over a clash with a reason.
5. The dates decide the case, shown under them (nothing to tick): a pickup ahead is an upcoming rental, handed over at pickup as usual. A pickup already passed with the return ahead is a rental already underway: it is recorded as on trip from the pickup you enter, on any active car (even one closed to public bookings), and anything a handover checks that is still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit, condition report, insurance) becomes a task. A return already passed is a rental that has ended: kept as completed, paid another way or unpaid.
6. Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one: name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. A renter on file shows their licence, home address and the drivers named before (**Add them** puts those drivers on the rental), with an expired licence or an old address flagged. Add any other drivers.
7. We deliver it, or we pick it up: pick the address from the suggestions and its distance from our location prices the delivery (shown under the address), as on Send an offer.
8. Check the price: every line of the price can be changed where it stands. Type a new amount in the line (the rental charge for the trip or a rate a day, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan, delivery, each add-on, the deposit, the kilometres a day); HST and the total follow. Add a line from the list or a charge of its own; Remove takes a fee off. The (i) beside each line says what it is and how it is worked out. One optional reason covers all the changes. At the top of the price, Amounts I type: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter paid for each line ("$270 after tax for the rental, $50 for the Protection Plan"): each is worked back to its amount before tax, and a line without HST stays as typed. The choice is remembered on this device. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that, to the cent, and the line under it shows each line before tax. The total shown is the total that is saved; if they ever differ, it says by how much before you save.
9. Any length: the dates may run past 30 days (up to the staff limit in Program settings, 730 days by default). From 30 days the rental charge is the monthly rate for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. On the booking, Monthly periods shows each period: its share, and its own version of the agreement (CarmaCars'' and Blind Spot''s), sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Program settings: long_rental_agreement_lead_days, 3 by default), with what is due for it on the renter''s Balance due. With Program settings, Charge the saved card for each period, on, that share is charged to the saved card when the agreement goes out (the renter gets the receipt; a declined or missing card gives Finance a task).
10. A car whose listing is not finished (a draft listing, onboarding, no photos or no rates yet) can be rented at once: it shows Listing not finished in the car list and stays off the public site. With no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason.
11. An owner''s car that is not on the fleet insurance policy yet: only an Admin adds its rentals, and ticks I checked that this car is insured for this rental. An owner''s car needs its terms (Revenue Share) first. The handover still needs the car on the fleet policy: press **Insurer confirmed** once the insurer confirms it.
12. Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): choose the insurer (Not listed: type its name, and it is added to the list), the claim number, the adjuster, the days and the daily rate authorized, the provisional end, and whether the insurer pays everything or the rental only. The booking is billed to the insurer; the renter owes only what it does not cover. The daily rate authorized is filled from the insurer''s rate sheet for the car (Insurance replacements: rates and billing); a different rate needs the reason. Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver when the insurer authorized them (Insurance replacements: rates and billing).
13. The rent is paid by: e-Transfer or cash (received), card on file (charged when the renter signs), payment link, platform payout (Turo), insurer billed later, cheque, bank transfer, or unpaid. Paid in parts (some cash, some e-Transfer): press **Add another payment (paid in parts)** and type each amount. Then the deposit, its own way: card hold, cash, e-Transfer (with its reference and date) or no deposit.
14. Before you save checks it all in one box: the renter, the car, the days, the total, what was received and what is still to collect, the deposit (or No deposit) and the agreement.
15. The rental agreement is sent to sign online (a rental agreement signed on paper is not accepted). The calendar: untick Blocks the car''s calendar for an insurance replacement with dates not known yet, with the reason.
16. Tick **Do not email the renter** if they should not get the confirmation. Press **Add the rental**.

> Tip: The rental is on the calendars at once (a payment link waits for the payment). The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal (never on paper). With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign, and until then the rental is awaiting signature. On the booking, **Verified in person** records a licence checked at the counter. A rental already underway can be paid by payment link (the renter signs, then pays from their booking) or the saved card, like an upcoming one.

## Retire or delete a car

**Cars** > **Retire or delete**, or the car''s own page.

1. **Retire this car** takes the car off the site and the calendars and keeps every record. It needs no future confirmed booking. **Restore** brings it back.
2. **Delete this car** removes a car added by mistake, with its photos. Only a car with nothing tied to money (no confirmed or paid booking, payment, statement, toll or damage). Type the plate or the name to confirm.
3. Booking requests that never confirmed and never took money (requested, offered, declined, expired) do not stop a delete. The confirmation lists them; they are removed with the car and a copy is kept. The renters stay on file.
4. On the same page, **Delete all sample cars** deletes every sample car that meets the rule at once, with its requests. Type DELETE SAMPLE CARS to confirm; the ones kept show why, with the booking numbers.

## Sample cars on the site

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, or **Settings** > **Site**. The 20 example cars the site started with, so the fleet never looks empty while the real cars are listed.

1. **Hide sample cars** asks first ("Hide all 20 sample cars from the site?"); press **Hide them** to take every sample car off the site at once, or **Keep them**. Nothing else stops it: not an enquiry, not an old request.
2. **Show sample cars** puts the 20 back, with their photos and rates. Ones that were deleted are made again.
3. On the site each one is marked "Example car". They never appear in search engines or the sitemap.
4. A request on a sample car is never a booking. When the person picks dates, the car page and the request form show a real car free for them (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price) with one tap to switch to it. If they keep the sample car, it becomes an enquiry (number EQ-1001 and up) and customer service gets the task Suggest a similar real car, naming the free real car.

> Tip: Hide the sample cars once enough real cars are on the site. Delete all sample cars removes them for good.

## Why a car is not on the site yet

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, the card Not on the site yet.

1. Every real car that is not on the site is listed with its next step first: the rates, Publish now, the listing review.
2. The same car is a line on To do with **Set rates and publish**. The car comes off both once it is on the site.
3. A car without photos is marked sample photos: once listed it shows a sample photo until its real photos are approved.

## Placeholder bookings

A placeholder is a booking held for an insurer, or as a hold, next to the real rental on the same car.

1. On **Add a rental**, press **Placeholder** (Admins). It never blocks the calendar, is never handed over, sends the renter nothing, earns no commission and is left off the Live map. The owner sees only that the car is unavailable. Type what it is for, or leave it empty.
2. Enter the real rental as usual, even for the same days: it blocks the car, and tolls, tickets and damage go to it.
3. A booking made another way can become one: on the booking, **More actions** > **Mark as a placeholder**. Not once money was taken or the car went out. **Make it a real booking** undoes it; then turn the calendar switch on if it should hold the car.
4. On the booking, **Competing for these dates** (and **Also on this car for these dates** once booked) lists everything else on the car for those days and says which one keeps it off the car. A placeholder never counts.

## Tolls when two rentals overlap

Bookings held for an insurer and other placeholders are never matched to a toll. When two real rentals overlap the toll time, nobody is charged automatically: the toll waits in the work queue under Two rentals, with both bookings, and you choose who pays.
