 from the seat table for 3-row SUVs and minivans (a Yukon XL or a Palisade is 8, 7 with captain&#39;s chairs), else 4 for a coupe or convertible and 5 for a sedan or hatchback. An SUV or minivan with neither is left without seats and shows Seats missing in Vehicles: the 7+ seats filter cannot show it until you set them. When either is not certain, Admin &gt; Today shows <b class="gd-ui">Confirm gearbox and seats</b>: press the gearbox and the number of seats, then <b class="gd-ui">Save</b>. A car whose VIN fits several trims shows <b class="gd-ui">Pick the trim</b> there: press the right one. Either way the title, description and search text are written again.</p><p class="gd-p">On a car&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Who supplies the car</b> shows the supplier and the commission, and changes them. Vehicles filters by supply type.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-partners" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Partners</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b>. Partner rental companies whose cars we rent out on commission.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a partner</b>: business and legal name, contacts, HST number, commission and insurance with its expiry date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a partner for its cars, bookings, statements, payouts and documents. A warning shows when its insurance expires soon, and Staff tasks gets a reminder (Program settings sets how many days before).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Banking (Admins only): <b class="gd-ui">Save the payout account</b> for the account we pay the partner into. The account number is stored encrypted. Press <b class="gd-ui">Verify</b> once checked.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Portal: <b class="gd-ui">Invite to the owner portal</b> gives the partner the owner portal with its cars, bookings, statements and the partner agreement, filled in and signed on screen in three taps.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The partner signs only in the portal, with the e-signature: a signature on paper is not recorded. <b class="gd-ui">Read the partner agreement</b> shows the text they sign.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-a-partner-fleet-on-its-own-rates" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A partner fleet on its own rates</h2><p class="gd-p">Some partners send a price sheet of their own rates instead of sharing what the renter pays. 01 Motors works this way: its whole fleet is on the site, and staff manage its cars (it has no portal sign-in yet; add its email on the partner page and invite it later).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b> &gt; the partner. <b class="gd-ui">Pricing</b> shows how it works: our base rate is the partner&#39;s listed rate less the partner discount (10% unless you set another), to the nearest dollar; then every rule of our own cars applies (the weekend rate, lead-time pricing, promo codes, the non-refundable discount), with every fee, the deposit and HST. CarmaCars receives a kickback of 20% of the listed rental (the partner&#39;s rates times the days booked); the partner is owed the rest. Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit pricing</b> to change the discount, the kickback or the basis for every car at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> lists each car with its listed rates a day (1 to 2 days, 3 or more, 7 or more) and our base rates. Press <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> on a car to change a negotiated rate, give that car its own discount or kickback, mark it <b class="gd-ui">Insurance included</b> or <b class="gd-ui">No credit card needed</b>, or confirm its model year. Our rates change at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Kickback and payable</b> lists each rental: the listed rental, the kickback receivable, the amount payable to the partner and our rental charge, with the totals not on a statement yet.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The site shows these cars with their tiers (1 to 2 days, 3 to 6 days, 7 days or more) and &quot;Guideline rates; final price confirmed after review&quot;. A car with insurance included needs no coverage choice from the renter (coverage option 4, confirmed by itself); a car with no credit card needed takes a debit card for the payment and the deposit. The deposit, the licence and identity checks and the ages stay the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The price sheet has no years, VINs or plates. Until you confirm the year, the site leaves it out and says &quot;Year confirmed when you book&quot;; an offer waits until the year is confirmed (Edit on the car, Model year). Add the plate and the VIN on the car&#39;s page before its first handover.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Real photos: open the car (its name in Cars), <b class="gd-ui">Photos</b>, and add them. Once approved they replace the eight studio stand-ins.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">3 days on the C43 AMG Blue, booked 3 weeks ahead</th><th scope="col">Amount</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Listed rental (3 x $225)</td><td>$675.00</td></tr><tr><td>Our rental charge (3 x $203, the listed rate less 10%)</td><td>$609.00</td></tr><tr><td>Booked ahead −5%</td><td>−$30.45</td></tr><tr><td>Fees (delivery, young driver and the like) and HST</td><td>CarmaCars&#39; own, 100%</td></tr><tr><td>Kickback receivable (20% of $675)</td><td>$135.00</td></tr><tr><td>Payable to the partner</td><td>$540.00</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The partner&#39;s monthly statement shows each rental at the listed rate, the kickback and the amount payable; never what the renter paid. A refund lowers the partner&#39;s share in proportion; our discount, lead-time pricing and any discount CarmaCars gives do not. Offers sent and bookings confirmed before the change keep their prices and are paid as before.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-a-partner-s-crm-01-motors-gohighlevel" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A partner&#39;s CRM (01 Motors&#39; GoHighLevel)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Settings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Partners</b> tile, then the partner (or <b class="gd-ui">CRM link</b> on the partner&#39;s page). Their CRM gets our cars, kept up to date, and their cars come to us.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Ask the partner for a Private Integration token and their location ID (the box <b class="gd-ui">What 01 Motors gives us</b> on the page says exactly what to create and which scopes to tick). Paste both and press <b class="gd-ui">Connect</b>. The token goes to the vault; the page only ever shows its last four characters.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Connect tests the link (their location, objects, products and pipelines) and runs the first sync. After that it runs by itself every 15 minutes, and within five minutes of a change to a car, a rate, a photo, a booking or a block. <b class="gd-ui">Test connection</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Run sync now</b> do it at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">What 01 Motors sees</b>: CarmaCars&#39; own cars and program owners&#39; cars that are on the site, with rates, the next 60 days and photos, as records of a &quot;CarmaCars Vehicles&quot; object in their CRM (or as products when their plan has no custom objects). Partner cars are never sent: not theirs, not another partner&#39;s. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change what we share</b> to leave out program owners&#39; cars, rates, availability or photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Partner price</b>: the site&#39;s rates, or the site&#39;s rates less (or plus) a percentage, to the nearest dollar.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Their cars coming in</b>: name the object in their CRM that holds their cars (Test connection lists them), or their feed address. Each of their cars is matched to their car here, or added as their partner car (it waits off the site unless you choose otherwise), with their rates as its sheet rates, their booked dates as calendar blocks and their photos for a car with none. A car that waits shows <b class="gd-ui">Add as their car</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Link</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Set aside</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Leads both ways</b> (off until you turn it on): requests for their cars, and requests that came through their booking links, become contacts and opportunities in the pipeline stage you choose; an opportunity they move to the stage you name becomes a lead in <b class="gd-ui">Leads</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Feed, widget and booking links</b>: a JSON or CSV feed and a widget for their GoHighLevel funnels and sites (copy the iframe), and booking links carmacars.ca/p/01-motors/&lt;car&gt; that mark the request as theirs for 30 days. <b class="gd-ui">New key</b> ends the old feed and widget addresses at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A link that has failed for an hour shows on Admin &gt; Today. Disconnect deletes the token from the vault; what is already in their CRM stays there.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-add-a-rental-by-hand" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a rental by hand</h2><p class="gd-p">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b> at the top of Bookings (or on To do). For phone, walk-in, Turo, partner and insurer bookings, the owner using their own car, and placeholders: a rental already agreed. To send an offer instead, use Send an offer.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Standing with the renter at pickup? Press <b class="gd-ui">Start at pickup</b>: type the renter&#39;s name and phone, choose the car, type the kilometres and the fuel, and press <b class="gd-ui">Hold the car and finish later</b>. The pickup is now; the car is held for 2 hours (renewed while you work on it) and you get a task to finish the rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing is required to save: the form is saved as a draft as you type (<b class="gd-ui">Save draft</b> saves at once). Unfinished rentals, on Bookings and on this page, lists every draft with who started it, when, and what is still missing; Finish it opens it where it was left, on any device. Tick Hold the car while I finish to keep the car off the calendar while you type (2 hours, renewed as you save). Discard drops it and frees the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Quick start sets the usual choices in one tap: <b class="gd-ui">Phone</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Walk-in</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Turo or another platform</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Insurance replacement</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Owner using own car</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Placeholder</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car and the dates. The calendar and the price are checked by themselves: clashes with other bookings and the cleaning time after each trip. An Admin may book over a clash with a reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The dates decide the case, shown under them (nothing to tick): a pickup ahead is an upcoming rental, handed over at pickup as usual. A pickup already passed with the return ahead is a rental already underway: it is recorded as on trip from the pickup you enter, on any active car (even one closed to public bookings), and anything a handover checks that is still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit, condition report, insurance) becomes a task. A return already passed is a rental that has ended: kept as completed, paid another way or unpaid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one: name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. A renter on file shows their licence, home address and the drivers named before (<b class="gd-ui">Add them</b> puts those drivers on the rental), with an expired licence or an old address flagged. Add any other drivers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">We deliver it, or we pick it up: pick the address from the suggestions and its distance from our location prices the delivery (shown under the address), as on Send an offer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">Check the price: every line of the price can be changed where it stands. Type a new amount in the line (the rental charge for the trip or a rate a day, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan, delivery, each add-on, the deposit, the kilometres a day); HST and the total follow. Add a line from the list or a charge of its own; Remove takes a fee off. The (i) beside each line says what it is and how it is worked out. One optional reason covers all the changes. At the top of the price, Amounts I type: Before tax, or After tax (HST included) to type what the renter paid for each line (&quot;$270 after tax for the rental, $50 for the Protection Plan&quot;): each is worked back to its amount before tax, and a line without HST stays as typed. The choice is remembered on this device. Or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that, to the cent, and the line under it shows each line before tax. The total shown is the total that is saved; if they ever differ, it says by how much before you save.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Any length: the dates may run past 30 days (up to the staff limit in Program settings, 730 days by default). From 30 days the rental charge is the monthly rate for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. On the booking, Monthly periods shows each period: its share, and its own version of the agreement (CarmaCars&#39; and Blind Spot&#39;s), sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Program settings: long_rental_agreement_lead_days, 3 by default), with what is due for it on the renter&#39;s Balance due. With Program settings, Charge the saved card for each period, on, that share is charged to the saved card when the agreement goes out (the renter gets the receipt; a declined or missing card gives Finance a task).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">A car whose listing is not finished (a draft listing, onboarding, no photos or no rates yet) can be rented at once: it shows Listing not finished in the car list and stays off the public site. With no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">An owner&#39;s car that is not on the fleet insurance policy yet: only an Admin adds its rentals, and ticks I checked that this car is insured for this rental. An owner&#39;s car needs its terms (Revenue Share) first. The handover still needs the car on the fleet policy: press <b class="gd-ui">Insurer confirmed</b> once the insurer confirms it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Insurer billed later (or the Insurance replacement quick start): choose the insurer (Not listed: type its name, and it is added to the list), the claim number, the adjuster, the days and the daily rate authorized, the provisional end, and whether the insurer pays everything or the rental only. The booking is billed to the insurer; the renter owes only what it does not cover. The daily rate authorized is filled from the insurer&#39;s rate sheet for the car (Insurance replacements: rates and billing); a different rate needs the reason. Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&amp;LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver when the insurer authorized them (Insurance replacements: rates and billing).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">The rent is paid by: e-Transfer or cash (received), card on file (charged when the renter signs), payment link, platform payout (Turo), insurer billed later, cheque, bank transfer, or unpaid. Paid in parts (some cash, some e-Transfer): press <b class="gd-ui">Add another payment (paid in parts)</b> and type each amount. Then the deposit, its own way: card hold, cash, e-Transfer (with its reference and date) or no deposit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">Before you save checks it all in one box: the renter, the car, the days, the total, what was received and what is still to collect, the deposit (or No deposit) and the agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">15</span><div class="gd-t">The rental agreement is sent to sign online (a rental agreement signed on paper is not accepted). The calendar: untick Blocks the car&#39;s calendar for an insurance replacement with dates not known yet, with the reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">16</span><div class="gd-t">Tick <b class="gd-ui">Do not email the renter</b> if they should not get the confirmation. Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The rental is on the calendars at once (a payment link waits for the payment). The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal (never on paper). With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign, and until then the rental is awaiting signature. On the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Verified in person</b> records a licence checked at the counter. A rental already underway can be paid by payment link (the renter signs, then pays from their booking) or the saved card, like an upcoming one.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-retire-or-delete-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Retire or delete a car</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Retire or delete</b>, or the car&#39;s own page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Retire this car</b> takes the car off the site and the calendars and keeps every record. It needs no future confirmed booking. <b class="gd-ui">Restore</b> brings it back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Delete this car</b> removes a car added by mistake, with its photos. Only a car with nothing tied to money (no confirmed or paid booking, payment, statement, toll or damage). Type the plate or the name to confirm.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Booking requests that never confirmed and never took money (requested, offered, declined, expired) do not stop a delete. The confirmation lists them; they are removed with the car and a copy is kept. The renters stay on file.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the same page, <b class="gd-ui">Delete all sample cars</b> deletes every sample car that meets the rule at once, with its requests. Type DELETE SAMPLE CARS to confirm; the ones kept show why, with the booking numbers.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-sample-cars-on-the-site" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sample cars on the site</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Settings</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Site</b>. The 20 example cars the site started with, so the fleet never looks empty while the real cars are listed.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hide sample cars</b> asks first (&quot;Hide all 20 sample cars from the site?&quot;); press <b class="gd-ui">Hide them</b> to take every sample car off the site at once, or <b class="gd-ui">Keep them</b>. Nothing else stops it: not an enquiry, not an old request.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Show sample cars</b> puts the 20 back, with their photos and rates. Ones that were deleted are made again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">On the site each one is marked &quot;Example car&quot;. They never appear in search engines or the sitemap.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A request on a sample car is never a booking. When the person picks dates, the car page and the request form show a real car free for them (the same make and model first, else the same class and body at a similar price) with one tap to switch to it. If they keep the sample car, it becomes an enquiry (number EQ-1001 and up) and customer service gets the task Suggest a similar real car, naming the free real car.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Hide the sample cars once enough real cars are on the site. Delete all sample cars removes them for good.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-why-a-car-is-not-on-the-site-yet" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Why a car is not on the site yet</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, the card Not on the site yet.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Every real car that is not on the site is listed with its next step first: the rates, Publish now, the listing review.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The same car is a line on To do with <b class="gd-ui">Set rates and publish</b>. The car comes off both once it is on the site.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A car without photos is marked sample photos: once listed it shows a sample photo until its real photos are approved.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-placeholder-bookings" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Placeholder bookings</h2><p class="gd-p">A placeholder is a booking held for an insurer, or as a hold, next to the real rental on the same car.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">Placeholder</b> (Admins). It never blocks the calendar, is never handed over, sends the renter nothing, earns no commission and is left off the Live map. The owner sees only that the car is unavailable. Type what it is for, or leave it empty.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Enter the real rental as usual, even for the same days: it blocks the car, and tolls, tickets and damage go to it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A booking made another way can become one: on the booking, <b class="gd-ui">More actions</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Mark as a placeholder</b>. Not once money was taken or the car went out. <b class="gd-ui">Make it a real booking</b> undoes it; then turn the calendar switch on if it should hold the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the booking, <b class="gd-ui">Competing for these dates</b> (and <b class="gd-ui">Also on this car for these dates</b> once booked) lists everything else on the car for those days and says which one keeps it off the car. A placeholder never counts.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="partners-company-cars-and-rentals-added-by-hand-tolls-when-two-rentals-overlap" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tolls when two rentals overlap</h2><p class="gd-p">Bookings held for an insurer and other placeholders are never matched to a toll. When two real rentals overlap the toll time, nobody is charged automatically: the toll waits in the work queue under Two rentals, with both bookings, and you choose who pays.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'owner-money', 'chapter', 'owners-and-onboarding', 'Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.

## Owner invoices

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Invoices** tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner''s and each application''s Invoices tab.

1. Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.
2. **New invoice** makes an invoice of any amount for an owner''s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.
3. The monthly run and tracker invoices: **Run the monthly invoices** issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); **Issue all tracker invoices** bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.

![](/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1060; address: carmacars.ca/admin/invoices; pins: 1 83.3 22.4, 2 41.7 35.7, 3 29.0 43.4")

## Make, edit and issue an invoice

A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.

1. Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. **Add a line** for more.
2. **Save as draft** to come back to it, or **Save and issue** to send it now. On a draft''s page, **Issue and email** sends it.
3. Paid another way? Press **Already paid outside the platform** on the invoice: choose how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or card outside the platform), the date and the reference. A draft is issued without the invoice email first, the payment is recorded, and the owner gets no email unless you tick **Email the owner a receipt**. To record a smaller or extra payment, press **Record payment**. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.
4. **Resend email** sends the invoice again. **PDF** opens it as a PDF.

## Correct an issued invoice

An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.

1. Press **Void**, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press **Void the invoice**. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.
2. The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press **Save and issue**.
3. Already paid? Void the payment first, or press **Credit note** for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.

Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.

## The automatic debit

The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for payments the bank sends back and owners with no bank debit set up.

:::flow
Notice day | Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before
Debit day | The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice
Cleared | The invoice is paid
Returned, insufficient funds | The $50.00 Late Fee is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days
Returned for another reason | No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task
:::

1. The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.
2. How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.
3. Scheduled and processing lists each debit. **Pause** holds one (a reason is needed).
4. Owners lists each owner''s bank debit. Use **Pause**, **Resume**, **Send a notice now** or, with no bank debit set up, **Send the sign-up link**.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 920; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 1 21.8 21.7, 2 21.5 35.5, 3 91.5 75.4, 4 84.7 94.7")

5. Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank''s reason.
6. Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.
7. Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.

![](/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/debits; pins: 5 11.0 14.4, 6 10.2 52.3, 7 15.4 89.8")

Insufficient funds: the $50.00 Late Fee is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner''s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task. Any debit missed (returned for another reason, too late to retry, or a retry still waiting) comes off the owner''s next revenue statement by itself: when the statement is built, the invoice goes in arrears (a waiting retry is cancelled) and the statement deducts it. Nothing to do.

> Watch out: Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner''s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no bank debit set up gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.

## Before the debit day: the Debit preview

The top of the Debits tab shows the coming debit day.

1. **Debit preview** lists each owner with something to debit: the total, whether a bank debit is set up, whether the notice went, and each invoice in one line: the amount, the car, the fee (monthly fee, first and last month, tracker install, adjustment, late fee), the period and how it was worked out, such as "prorated: 20 of 30 days". The line opens the invoice.
2. Something looks wrong? Press **Hold** beside the owner and give the reason. Nothing is debited for that owner until you press **Resume**.
3. **Fee check** compares the month''s invoices with each car''s signed terms: no monthly fee on a flat monthly payment, a Turo-Only car, a shareholder''s car or a company car, nothing before the Enrollment Date, and the amount the terms give. It changes nothing: void and reissue an invoice that does not match. Each production deploy prints the same check.

## When a debit can''t go ahead

You get one email: "Can''t collect $X from the owner: the reason". The reasons are the words of the owner guide: no bank debit set up, owner cancelled the debit at their bank, amount went up after the notice, the bank sent the payment back. The email lists each amount in one line and has one button that fixes it.

1. **Send the sign-up link** opens the Debits tab on that owner. Press **Send the sign-up link** again there: the owner gets the email to set up their bank debit.
2. **Send a new notice** opens the same place with **Send a new notice** for the new amount.
3. **Open the invoice** opens the invoice to record a payment made another way.

## Owner statements

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Statements** tab

1. Press **Build all for a month** (or **Build one**).
2. Open each draft. Check it, **Rebuild** after a correction, **Preview PDF**, then **Approve**.
3. Press **Issue to the owner**. **Reissue** sends a corrected copy; **CSV** exports it.

![](/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 400; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements; pins: 1 79.9 27.3")

![An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.](/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 520; address: carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000; pins: 3 86.0 22.7")

## Staff commissions

**Money** > **Company**, the **Commissions** tab. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Not earned yet | The rental is ahead, or not paid in full
Pending approval | Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended
Approved | You approved it; the staff member is told
Paid | You recorded the payment; the staff member is told
Reversed | Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment
:::

1. By person shows each staff member''s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.
2. Press **Approve** on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.
3. Press **Record a payment**: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.
4. **Prices to review** lists prices typed by hand; **Sourcing claims** lists staff who say they sourced a website request; **Payments made** lists each payment.
5. **Owner requests** lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company''s share or of the cars'' rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press **Approve**, **Change and approve** (your terms, with a note) or **Decline**. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner''s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner''s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.
6. Who sourced an owner: the owner''s page, **Sourced by**. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.

|  | Commission |
| --- | --- |
| Sales | By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month''s rentals |
| An owner a salesperson brought in | The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars'', a partner''s or a shareholder''s cars |
| Field staff | 10% (also the field referral fee). Customer service, Fleet and Finance staff get no sales credit or commission, ever: their help is credited as Helped by on the booking and on their scorecard |
| Base | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off |
| On the owner statement | An owner''s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner''s car: from CarmaCars'' commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense |

> Tip: A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month''s Sales tier) goes on the owner''s next statement as an adjustment line.

## Field pay

**Money** > **Company**, the **Field pay** tab. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.

:::flow
Clocked in and out | Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out
Pay run started | Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions
Approved | The figures are frozen, the period''s hours are locked, the statements are numbered
Paid | You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email
:::

1. The tab **Pay run** shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings > Program, Field pay). **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between periods.
2. After the period ends, press **Start the payroll**: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). **Refresh the figures** takes in a change made since.
3. Press **Approve**. The period''s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under **Hours** first. **Withdraw** takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.
4. Press **Record payment** on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (**Send again** repeats it). The statement''s number opens its PDF; **CSV** gives the run for your accountant.
5. **Hours** lists everyone''s shifts of the period. **Add hours** enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.
6. **Hourly rates** shows each person''s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with **Set the rate** (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.

|  | Field pay |
| --- | --- |
| Overtime | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate |
| Vacation pay | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement |
| Deductions | None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer''s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so |
| Commissions that net to nothing | A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next |

> Tip: A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.

## Company model

Money > **Company model** is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.

1. **Forecast**: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months'' EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.
2. **Actuals**: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental''s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. **Refresh actuals now** recomputes them at once.
3. **Pro forma 5 years**: each year''s income statement, cash flow and key figures.
4. **Assumptions**: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press **Save the assumptions**; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked "From the actuals" left blank uses the latest complete month.
5. **Download as Excel**: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.

> Tip: Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month''s costs in Money > Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.

## Payroll for everyone (release 35)

**Money** > **Payroll** is one run every two weeks for the field staff (hours) and for customer service, Fleet and Finance (salary).

1. A salaried person is paid their monthly salary x 12 / 26, for the days they were employed in the period. The salary is their own (**Set the salary**, with a reason), else the monthly pay they were hired at, else their role''s (Program settings, va_salary_defaults), in US dollars unless set otherwise.
2. Finance prepares it: **Start the payroll**, **Add a bonus or deduction** with the reason, then **Send for approval**. You get an alert.
3. You press **Approve**, then **Record all payments** (one method and reference; each stub number is added to it) or **Record payment** line by line. Each person gets their stub by email and in their portal.

> Tip: Admin > Team also has **Schedules** (each role''s days and hours, anyone''s own, who is late today) and **KPIs** (every staff member''s KPIs for a week against the targets in Program settings).

> Good to know: The townhall page: pick the craziest story, enter the week''s social media figures, add the recording link, and mark anyone present or absent. Staff who miss two townhalls in a row are locked until you press **Unlock** on the staff list.

> Good to know: Each renter and lead shows an Intent card (hot, warm or cold, with the budget, car, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage they mentioned). The live map shows it on each pin. An AI reading fills the gaps within the free daily allowance only (Program settings, intent_ai_enabled).

> Good to know: Investors see Search traction under the deck: Google clicks and impressions of the last 28 days, indexed pages and the weekly trend. Type the indexed pages from Search Console on the investor deck page under Investors (no API exists for it).

## Company statements

**Money** > **Company**, the **Monthly statements** tab: CarmaCars'' own monthly statement, in twelve sections.

1. Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.
2. Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.
3. Download **PDF**, **PDF by owner** or **PDF by vehicle**, or press **Email me the PDFs**.
4. **Finalize** freezes the month. **Rebuild** works until then.

![](/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/reports; pins: 1 20.8 28.0, 2 19.4 59.3, 3 77.1 15.5, 4 46.9 15.5")

### Fees taken from the revenue statement
On an owner''s page, the **Fees** button sets **How fees are paid**: **Bank debit** (the default) or **Take from revenue statement**. Taken from the statement, the owner''s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement". Approved, the invoice reads **Paid from statement**, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task **Invoice ... back to the bank debit**.

### The flat-rate agreements
An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement** instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner''s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings > **Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK** is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.

## How it''s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts

Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: **Bank debit on the 15th**, or **Deduct from payouts** (taken from the owner''s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).

1. On an invoice, **How it''s paid**, **Change**. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.
2. Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.
3. For the first and last month, choose **Deduct from payouts** on the Terms tab (or at approval).
4. On the Terms tab, **Charge the agreed one-off fees** makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner''s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.

## Referral links between owners (release 28)

When one owner referred another, open the referrer''s **Terms** tab, **Referral links**, **This owner referred another owner**: choose the owner referred and the share in basis points (1000 = 10 points of the revenue the management fee is taken from). Set the referred owner''s own fee on their Terms as usual (for example a 40% management fee and $350 a month per car). Every statement of the referrer then has a **Referral share** line per referred car; it is paid from CarmaCars'' share, never the referred owner''s payout. With **sees the cars** on, the referrer finds **Cars you referred** in their owner portal: bookings, use and revenue, read only, without the other owner''s details. **End** stops the link; shares already earned are still paid.

## Statement periods (release 35)

Statements run from the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th covers them. A rental that crosses the cutoff, or a long weekly or biweekly rental, is paid for the days inside each period, never twice. Each statement lists amounts still uncollected from the renter separately; they are paid on the statement after they are collected.', 'Owner money', 'Owner invoices (drafts, void and reissue, credit notes), the automatic debit, statements, payouts and the company statement.',
  'Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.

## Owner invoices

**Money** > **Owner money**, the **Invoices** tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner''s and each application''s Invoices tab.

1. Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.
2. **New invoice** makes an invoice of any amount for an owner''s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.
3. The monthly run and tracker invoices: **Run the monthly invoices** issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); **Issue all tracker invoices** bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.

![](/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1060; address: carmacars.ca/admin/invoices; pins: 1 83.3 22.4, 2 41.7 35.7, 3 29.0 43.4")

## Make, edit and issue an invoice

A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.

1. Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. **Add a line** for more.
2. **Save as draft** to come back to it, or **Save and issue** to send it now. On a draft''s page, **Issue and email** sends it.
3. Paid another way? Press **Already paid outside the platform** on the invoice: choose how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or card outside the platform), the date and the reference. A draft is issued without the invoice email first, the payment is recorded, and the owner gets no email unless you tick **Email the owner a receipt**. To record a smaller or extra payment, press **Record payment**. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.
4. **Resend email** sends the invoice again. **PDF** opens it as a PDF.

