1. The tab **Pay run** shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings > Program, Field pay). **Earlier period** and **Later period** move between periods.
2. After the period ends, press **Start the payroll**: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). **Refresh the figures** takes in a change made since.
3. Press **Approve**. The period''s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under **Hours** first. **Withdraw** takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.
4. Press **Record payment** on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (**Send again** repeats it). The statement''s number opens its PDF; **CSV** gives the run for your accountant.
5. **Hours** lists everyone''s shifts of the period. **Add hours** enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, **Change** fixes one and **Remove** takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.
6. **Hourly rates** shows each person''s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with **Set the rate** (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.

|  | Field pay |
| --- | --- |
| Overtime | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate |
| Vacation pay | Off. Settings > Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement |
| Deductions | None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer''s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so |
| Commissions that net to nothing | A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next |

> Tip: A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.

## Company model

Money > **Company model** is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.

1. **Forecast**: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months'' EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.
2. **Actuals**: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental''s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. **Refresh actuals now** recomputes them at once.
3. **Pro forma 5 years**: each year''s income statement, cash flow and key figures.
4. **Assumptions**: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press **Save the assumptions**; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked "From the actuals" left blank uses the latest complete month.
5. **Download as Excel**: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.

> Tip: Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month''s costs in Money > Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.

## Payroll for everyone (release 35)

**Money** > **Payroll** is one run every two weeks for the field staff (hours) and for customer service, Fleet and Finance (salary).

1. A salaried person is paid their monthly salary x 12 / 26, for the days they were employed in the period. The salary is their own (**Set the salary**, with a reason), else the monthly pay they were hired at, else their role''s (Program settings, va_salary_defaults), in US dollars unless set otherwise.
2. Finance prepares it: **Start the payroll**, **Add a bonus or deduction** with the reason, then **Send for approval**. You get an alert.
3. You press **Approve**, then **Record all payments** (one method and reference; each stub number is added to it) or **Record payment** line by line. Each person gets their stub by email and in their portal.

> Tip: Admin > Team also has **Schedules** (each role''s days and hours, anyone''s own, who is late today) and **KPIs** (every staff member''s KPIs for a week against the targets in Program settings).

> Good to know: The townhall page: pick the craziest story, enter the week''s social media figures, add the recording link, and mark anyone present or absent. Staff who miss two townhalls in a row are locked until you press **Unlock** on the staff list.

> Good to know: Meetings, on the townhall page, lists the last eight townhalls and the next four. A townhall nobody attended is recorded as not held and counts nobody absent. **This townhall did not happen** does the same for a past one (its absences and alerts are cleared, and a lockout it caused is lifted). **Cancel this townhall** on an upcoming one sends no reminders for it; **Put it back on** undoes that.

> Good to know: Each renter and lead shows an Intent card (hot, warm or cold, with the budget, car, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage they mentioned). The live map shows it on each pin. An AI reading fills the gaps within the free daily allowance only (Program settings, intent_ai_enabled).

> Good to know: Investors see Search traction under the deck: Google clicks and impressions of the last 28 days, indexed pages and the weekly trend. Type the indexed pages from Search Console on the investor deck page under Investors (no API exists for it).

## Company statements

**Money** > **Company**, the **Monthly statements** tab: CarmaCars'' own monthly statement, in twelve sections.

1. Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.
2. Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.
3. Download **PDF**, **PDF by owner** or **PDF by vehicle**, or press **Email me the PDFs**.
4. **Finalize** freezes the month. **Rebuild** works until then.

![](/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/reports; pins: 1 20.8 28.0, 2 19.4 59.3, 3 77.1 15.5, 4 46.9 15.5")

### Fees taken from the revenue statement
On an owner''s page, the **Fees** button sets **How fees are paid**: **Bank debit** (the default) or **Take from revenue statement**. Taken from the statement, the owner''s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line "Invoice INV-..., paid from statement". Approved, the invoice reads **Paid from statement**, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task **Invoice ... back to the bank debit**.

### The flat-rate agreements
An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the **Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement** instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner''s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings > **Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK** is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.

## How it''s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts

Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: **Bank debit on the 15th**, or **Deduct from payouts** (taken from the owner''s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).

1. On an invoice, **How it''s paid**, **Change**. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.
2. Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.
3. For the first and last month, choose **Deduct from payouts** on the Terms tab (or at approval).
4. On the Terms tab, **Charge the agreed one-off fees** makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner''s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.

## Referral links between owners (release 28)

When one owner referred another, open the referrer''s **Terms** tab, **Referral links**, **This owner referred another owner**: choose the owner referred and the share in basis points (1000 = 10 points of the revenue the management fee is taken from). Set the referred owner''s own fee on their Terms as usual (for example a 40% management fee and $350 a month per car). Every statement of the referrer then has a **Referral share** line per referred car; it is paid from CarmaCars'' share, never the referred owner''s payout. With **sees the cars** on, the referrer finds **Cars you referred** in their owner portal: bookings, use and revenue, read only, without the other owner''s details. **End** stops the link; shares already earned are still paid.

## Statement periods (release 35)

Statements run from the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th covers them. A rental that crosses the cutoff, or a long weekly or biweekly rental, is paid for the days inside each period, never twice. Each statement lists amounts still uncollected from the renter separately; they are paid on the statement after they are collected.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Owner fee invoices are issued on the notice day and debited on the 15th. Invoices of any amount are made by hand, as drafts first. Statements are built, approved and issued each month, and payouts follow.</p><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-invoices" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner invoices</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Invoices</b> tab. Every owner invoice, drafts and voids included. The same list is on each owner&#39;s and each application&#39;s Invoices tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by Drafts, Open, Partly paid, Paid, Failed, In arrears or Void, or search by invoice number or owner. Open an invoice to see everything about it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">New invoice</b> makes an invoice of any amount for an owner&#39;s car, for example a registration fee of $123.45.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The monthly run and tracker invoices: <b class="gd-ui">Run the monthly invoices</b> issues the invoices for the 15th by hand, for a missed month (never twice); <b class="gd-ui">Issue all tracker invoices</b> bills the Tracker Install for each car waiting for its tracker.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/invoices</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1060"><img src="/guides/img/admin-14-owner-invoices-desktop-dc4ed1f1.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1060"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:83.3%;top:22.4%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:41.7%;top:35.7%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:29%;top:43.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-make-edit-and-issue-an-invoice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Make, edit and issue an invoice</h2><p class="gd-p">A new invoice is a draft: the owner sees nothing and it is never debited until you issue it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car, a title (for example Registration fee) and, if you like, the due date (empty: 7 days after it is issued). Each line: the description, the quantity, the unit amount to the cent, HST on or off, and a note. <b class="gd-ui">Add a line</b> for more.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Save as draft</b> to come back to it, or <b class="gd-ui">Save and issue</b> to send it now. On a draft&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Issue and email</b> sends it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Paid another way? Press <b class="gd-ui">Already paid outside the platform</b> on the invoice: choose how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or card outside the platform), the date and the reference. A draft is issued without the invoice email first, the payment is recorded, and the owner gets no email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Email the owner a receipt</b>. To record a smaller or extra payment, press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b>. The page lists the payments with their receipts, the automatic debits, the emails sent and the history.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Resend email</b> sends the invoice again. <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b> opens it as a PDF.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-correct-an-issued-invoice" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Correct an issued invoice</h2><p class="gd-p">An issued invoice is never edited. You void it and issue a corrected one.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Void</b>, write the reason (the owner reads it), keep Make a corrected invoice from it ticked, and press <b class="gd-ui">Void the invoice</b>. Its scheduled debit is cancelled and the owner is told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The corrected invoice opens as a draft with the same lines. Fix the amounts and press <b class="gd-ui">Save and issue</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Already paid? Void the payment first, or press <b class="gd-ui">Credit note</b> for the amount to give back: it gets its own number and the owner sees it.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">Invoices issued before October 20, 2026 at the old default (for example $904.00, or $1,017.00 when the Insurance Fee was $450.00) are not changed by themselves. Where an owner agreed another amount, void them and reissue at the agreed amount.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-the-automatic-debit" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The automatic debit</h2><p class="gd-p">The debit runs by itself. Your job is to watch for payments the bank sends back and owners with no bank debit set up.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Notice day</span><em>Invoices issued, one notice per owner, 10 days before</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Debit day</span><em>The 15th from 6:00: one debit per invoice</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Cleared</span><em>The invoice is paid</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Returned, insufficient funds</span><em>The $50.00 Late Fee is added once; the same amount is tried again within 30 days</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Returned for another reason</span><em>No retry and no Late Fee: the debit pauses and you get a task</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tiles show the next debit day and notice day, scheduled, processing, cleared and returned debits.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">How it runs explains the policy in words, read from Program settings.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Scheduled and processing lists each debit. <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b> holds one (a reason is needed).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Owners lists each owner&#39;s bank debit. Use <b class="gd-ui">Pause</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Resume</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Send a notice now</b> or, with no bank debit set up, <b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/debits</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/920"><img src="/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-f65f061a.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="920"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.8%;top:21.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:21.5%;top:35.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:91.5%;top:75.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.7%;top:94.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol" start="5"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Results: each debit, cleared or returned, with the bank&#39;s reason.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Run log: each notice and debit run, with its counts.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Notices sent: who was told what, for which debit day.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/debits</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1230/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-15-owner-debits-desktop-8d4682bc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1230" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:11%;top:14.4%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.2%;top:52.3%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:15.4%;top:89.8%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div><p class="gd-p">Insufficient funds: the $50.00 Late Fee is added to that invoice once and collected with the owner&#39;s next debit, and the original amount is tried again within 30 days, as section 4.4 of the Enrollment Agreement sets out. The retry is never more than the original amount. Returned again: the invoice is in arrears and you get a task. Any debit missed (returned for another reason, too late to retry, or a retry still waiting) comes off the owner&#39;s next revenue statement by itself: when the statement is built, the invoice goes in arrears (a waiting retry is cancelled) and the statement deducts it. Nothing to do.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Returned for any other reason (account closed, payment stopped, no authorization): there is no retry and no Late Fee. The owner&#39;s debit pauses, the owner gets an email asking them to fix the account or pay another way, and you get a task. A debit is never more than its notice said. An owner with no bank debit set up gets an email on the notice day and you get a task; nothing is debited for them.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-before-the-debit-day-the-debit-preview" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Before the debit day: the Debit preview</h2><p class="gd-p">The top of the Debits tab shows the coming debit day.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Debit preview</b> lists each owner with something to debit: the total, whether a bank debit is set up, whether the notice went, and each invoice in one line: the amount, the car, the fee (monthly fee, first and last month, tracker install, adjustment, late fee), the period and how it was worked out, such as &quot;prorated: 20 of 30 days&quot;. The line opens the invoice.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Something looks wrong? Press <b class="gd-ui">Hold</b> beside the owner and give the reason. Nothing is debited for that owner until you press <b class="gd-ui">Resume</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Fee check</b> compares the month&#39;s invoices with each car&#39;s signed terms: no monthly fee on a flat monthly payment, a Turo-Only car, a shareholder&#39;s car or a company car, nothing before the Enrollment Date, and the amount the terms give. It changes nothing: void and reissue an invoice that does not match. Each production deploy prints the same check.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-when-a-debit-can-t-go-ahead" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">When a debit can&#39;t go ahead</h2><p class="gd-p">You get one email: &quot;Can&#39;t collect $X from the owner: the reason&quot;. The reasons are the words of the owner guide: no bank debit set up, owner cancelled the debit at their bank, amount went up after the notice, the bank sent the payment back. The email lists each amount in one line and has one button that fixes it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b> opens the Debits tab on that owner. Press <b class="gd-ui">Send the sign-up link</b> again there: the owner gets the email to set up their bank debit.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Send a new notice</b> opens the same place with <b class="gd-ui">Send a new notice</b> for the new amount.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Open the invoice</b> opens the invoice to record a payment made another way.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-owner-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Owner statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Statements</b> tab</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Build all for a month</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Build one</b>).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open each draft. Check it, <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> after a correction, <b class="gd-ui">Preview PDF</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Issue to the owner</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Reissue</b> sends a corrected copy; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> exports it.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/400"><img src="/guides/img/admin-16-statements-desktop-43a313ea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="400"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:79.9%;top:27.3%" aria-hidden="true">1</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/statements/2eedf660-50ce-4bd9-86d6-01bbe149c000</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/520"><img src="/guides/img/admin-17-statement-desktop-106ee57f.jpg" alt="An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="520"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:86%;top:22.7%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div><figcaption>An approved statement: the owner gets it by email with the PDF on the 10th, and payouts follow under Payouts.</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-staff-commissions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Staff commissions</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Commissions</b> tab. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Not earned yet</span><em>The rental is ahead, or not paid in full</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pending approval</span><em>Completed and paid in full; a Sales month once it has ended</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>You approved it; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded the payment; the staff member is told</em></li><li><b>5</b><span>Reversed</span><em>Cancelled, refunded or charged back; after payment it comes off the next payment</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">By person shows each staff member&#39;s month (Sales: rental days of 100 and the tier), what is not earned yet, pending approval, approved and paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b> on a person (everything that may be approved now) or on one commission.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record a payment</b>: choose how it was paid (e-Transfer, bank transfer, Wise, cash, the monthly pay statement or another way), the reference and the date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Prices to review</b> lists prices typed by hand; <b class="gd-ui">Sourcing claims</b> lists staff who say they sourced a website request; <b class="gd-ui">Payments made</b> lists each payment.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Owner requests</b> lists the commission each salesperson asks for an owner they brought in: a flat amount, or a percent of the company&#39;s share or of the cars&#39; rental revenue, for a number of months or for as long as the car is with us. Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change and approve</b> (your terms, with a note) or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Nothing accrues before you approve. A flat amount is earned at the owner&#39;s first paid rental, once; a percent on each paid rental of the owner&#39;s cars in the time approved. Each then comes to the list above for approval.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Who sourced an owner: the owner&#39;s page, <b class="gd-ui">Sourced by</b>. Only an Admin changes it, with a reason. A waiting request of the person before is withdrawn; an approved one, with what it has not paid yet, goes to the new person.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Commission</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sales</td><td>By rental days of the month: under 50 days 10%, from 50 days 15%, from 100 days 20%, on all that month&#39;s rentals</td></tr><tr><td>An owner a salesperson brought in</td><td>The request you approved. A CarmaCars expense, never deducted before Owner Revenue; none on CarmaCars&#39;, a partner&#39;s or a shareholder&#39;s cars</td></tr><tr><td>Field staff</td><td>10% (also the field referral fee). Customer service, Fleet and Finance staff get no sales credit or commission, ever: their help is credited as Helped by on the booking and on their scorecard</td></tr><tr><td>Base</td><td>The rental charge before tax, after discounts, with late extra days; never delivery, kilometres, add-ons or anything else bought. Only a refund of the rental charge comes off</td></tr><tr><td>On the owner statement</td><td>An owner&#39;s car: deducted with the kickbacks before Owner Revenue, its own line on the statement. A partner&#39;s car: from CarmaCars&#39; commission. A CarmaCars-owned car: a CarmaCars expense</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A commission that changes after an owner statement was built (a refund, or the month&#39;s Sales tier) goes on the owner&#39;s next statement as an adjustment line.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-field-pay" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Field pay</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Field pay</b> tab. Field staff clock in and out on their phones (My hours); you run the pay every two weeks. Nothing is paid automatically.</p><ol class="gd-flow"><li><b>1</b><span>Clocked in and out</span><em>Field staff press Clock in and Clock out; Fleet or you fix a forgotten clock-out</em></li><li><b>2</b><span>Pay run started</span><em>Hours times the hourly rate, plus the approved commissions</em></li><li><b>3</b><span>Approved</span><em>The figures are frozen, the period&#39;s hours are locked, the statements are numbered</em></li><li><b>4</b><span>Paid</span><em>You recorded how each person was paid; they get their statement by email</em></li></ol><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The tab <b class="gd-ui">Pay run</b> shows the current two-week period (Sunday to Saturday: the first day is Settings &gt; Program, Field pay). <b class="gd-ui">Earlier period</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Later period</b> move between periods.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">After the period ends, press <b class="gd-ui">Start the payroll</b>: one line for each person with hours times their hourly rate, plus the staff commissions and referral fees approved by the end of the period (see Staff commissions). <b class="gd-ui">Refresh the figures</b> takes in a change made since.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>. The period&#39;s hours are locked, each line gets a statement number and the figures are frozen. Someone still clocked in blocks it: fix their shift under <b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> first. <b class="gd-ui">Withdraw</b> takes an approved run back while no payment is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> on a line: choose e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash, the reference (not needed for cash) and the date. The commissions in the line are marked paid and the person gets their pay statement by email (<b class="gd-ui">Send again</b> repeats it). The statement&#39;s number opens its PDF; <b class="gd-ui">CSV</b> gives the run for your accountant.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hours</b> lists everyone&#39;s shifts of the period. <b class="gd-ui">Add hours</b> enters a shift for someone who forgot to clock in, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> fixes one and <b class="gd-ui">Remove</b> takes one out. Each needs a reason and is kept in a log. Fleet does the same under Field hours but sees no pay.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Hourly rates</b> shows each person&#39;s rate: CA$18.00 an hour unless you give them their own with <b class="gd-ui">Set the rate</b> (a reason is needed). A pay run keeps the rate it was started with.</div></li></ol></div><div class="gd-tablewrap"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col"></th><th scope="col">Field pay</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Overtime</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: pay overtime, after 44 hours in a week, at 150% of the rate</td></tr><tr><td>Vacation pay</td><td>Off. Settings &gt; Program, Field pay: vacation pay (Ontario: 4%) adds that share of wages, overtime and commissions to each statement</td></tr><tr><td>Deductions</td><td>None are worked out: income tax, CPP, EI and the employer&#39;s contributions are for your accountant. Each statement says so</td></tr><tr><td>Commissions that net to nothing</td><td>A person whose approved commissions add up to nothing or less (a clawback) is not paid them this period: they carry to the next</td></tr></tbody></table></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A shift of more than 16 hours (a setting) is refused, and so are hours that overlap another shift of the same person. The field staff member sees their hours and statements under My hours on their phone.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-model" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company model</h2><p class="gd-p">Money &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company model</b> is the CarmaCars model workbook, live: the actuals, the forecast and the pro forma on one page. Admins only (not Finance). Never share it: investors have their own sheets in the investor portal.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Forecast</b>: the latest actual month, the EBITDA break-even month, the next 12 months&#39; EBITDA and the lowest cash, a chart of EBITDA and cash, and 36 months marked A (actual) or F (forecast): cars, utilization, revenue per rented day, revenue, costs, EBITDA, investor returns, tax and cash.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Actuals</b>: filled in by themselves every hour from the bookings, payments, payouts, expenses and investments. Rental earned is spread over each rental&#39;s days (before HST, insurer-billed and renter-billed apart, placeholders left out), with fees by kind, cash received by method, rentals and rented days, owner and partner shares, commissions, kickbacks, expenses by category and investor payouts. <b class="gd-ui">Refresh actuals now</b> recomputes them at once.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pro forma 5 years</b>: each year&#39;s income statement, cash flow and key figures.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Assumptions</b>: growth, the utilization ramp, rates, monthly costs, hires, planned capital raises, the fleet insurance premium and tax. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save the assumptions</b>; the forecast, the pro forma and the download use them at once. A field marked &quot;From the actuals&quot; left blank uses the latest complete month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Download as Excel</b>: the full internal workbook with live formulas and the current actuals.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Enter the fleet insurance premium under Assumptions; until then it counts as $0 and profit is overstated. Enter each month&#39;s costs in Money &gt; Expenses: a cost line with nothing entered for an actual month uses the assumption, marked est.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-payroll-for-everyone-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Payroll for everyone (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Payroll</b> is one run every two weeks for the field staff (hours) and for customer service, Fleet and Finance (salary).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">A salaried person is paid their monthly salary x 12 / 26, for the days they were employed in the period. The salary is their own (<b class="gd-ui">Set the salary</b>, with a reason), else the monthly pay they were hired at, else their role&#39;s (Program settings, va_salary_defaults), in US dollars unless set otherwise.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Finance prepares it: <b class="gd-ui">Start the payroll</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Add a bonus or deduction</b> with the reason, then <b class="gd-ui">Send for approval</b>. You get an alert.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">You press <b class="gd-ui">Approve</b>, then <b class="gd-ui">Record all payments</b> (one method and reference; each stub number is added to it) or <b class="gd-ui">Record payment</b> line by line. Each person gets their stub by email and in their portal.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>Admin &gt; Team also has <b class="gd-ui">Schedules</b> (each role&#39;s days and hours, anyone&#39;s own, who is late today) and <b class="gd-ui">KPIs</b> (every staff member&#39;s KPIs for a week against the targets in Program settings).</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The townhall page: pick the craziest story, enter the week&#39;s social media figures, add the recording link, and mark anyone present or absent. Staff who miss two townhalls in a row are locked until you press <b class="gd-ui">Unlock</b> on the staff list.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Meetings, on the townhall page, lists the last eight townhalls and the next four. A townhall nobody attended is recorded as not held and counts nobody absent. <b class="gd-ui">This townhall did not happen</b> does the same for a past one (its absences and alerts are cleared, and a lockout it caused is lifted). <b class="gd-ui">Cancel this townhall</b> on an upcoming one sends no reminders for it; <b class="gd-ui">Put it back on</b> undoes that.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Each renter and lead shows an Intent card (hot, warm or cold, with the budget, car, length, dates, urgency, delivery and coverage they mentioned). The live map shows it on each pin. An AI reading fills the gaps within the free daily allowance only (Program settings, intent_ai_enabled).</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Investors see Search traction under the deck: Google clicks and impressions of the last 28 days, indexed pages and the weekly trend. Type the indexed pages from Search Console on the investor deck page under Investors (no API exists for it).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-company-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Company statements</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Money</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Company</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Monthly statements</b> tab: CarmaCars&#39; own monthly statement, in twelve sections.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the month. The tiles show revenue, fees, refunds, expenses and the company net.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Switch between Total, Per owner and Per vehicle.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Download <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b>, <b class="gd-ui">PDF by owner</b> or <b class="gd-ui">PDF by vehicle</b>, or press <b class="gd-ui">Email me the PDFs</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Finalize</b> freezes the month. <b class="gd-ui">Rebuild</b> works until then.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/reports</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/760"><img src="/guides/img/admin-18-company-statements-desktop-8e2738ed.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="760"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:20.8%;top:28%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:19.4%;top:59.3%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:77.1%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:46.9%;top:15.5%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Fees taken from the revenue statement</h3><p class="gd-p">On an owner&#39;s page, the <b class="gd-ui">Fees</b> button sets <b class="gd-ui">How fees are paid</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit</b> (the default) or <b class="gd-ui">Take from revenue statement</b>. Taken from the statement, the owner&#39;s invoices (not the upfront one) are not debited: the next owner statement pays each one from the payout, as far as it goes, with the line &quot;Invoice INV-..., paid from statement&quot;. Approved, the invoice reads <b class="gd-ui">Paid from statement</b>, or part paid with the rest on the next statement. An invoice still owing 2 months after its billing date goes back to the bank debit after the usual notice, and you get the task <b class="gd-ui">Invoice ... back to the bank debit</b>.</p><h3 class="gd-h3">The flat-rate agreements</h3><p class="gd-p">An owner whose every car is on a flat monthly payment signs the <b class="gd-ui">Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement</b> instead of the standard one (the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement and Forms A to D are the same). The owner&#39;s page says which set applies. When the pay model changes, the signed Enrollment Agreement ends and the owner signs the new one in the owner portal; changed back before signing, the signed one is in force again. The lawyer approved the flat-rate set: Program settings &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Flat-rate agreements awaiting lawyer OK</b> is off, and is turned on only to mark a new text still under review. Owners can sign either way.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-how-it-s-paid-bank-debit-or-deducted-from-payouts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">How it&#39;s paid: bank debit or deducted from payouts</h2><p class="gd-p">Every owner invoice is paid one of two ways: <b class="gd-ui">Bank debit on the 15th</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> (taken from the owner&#39;s monthly payouts until paid, never debited).</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On an invoice, <b class="gd-ui">How it&#39;s paid</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Change</b>. A draft changed to Deduct from payouts is issued without the debit email.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each monthly statement deducts as much as the payout allows and shows it to the owner as a deduction; the rest waits for the next statement. The invoice screen shows what was deducted and what is left.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">For the first and last month, choose <b class="gd-ui">Deduct from payouts</b> on the Terms tab (or at approval).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">On the Terms tab, <b class="gd-ui">Charge the agreed one-off fees</b> makes one invoice for a car from the one-off fees agreed on the owner&#39;s terms (all, or the ones you name), deducted from payouts or debited.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-referral-links-between-owners-release-28" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Referral links between owners (release 28)</h2><p class="gd-p">When one owner referred another, open the referrer&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Terms</b> tab, <b class="gd-ui">Referral links</b>, <b class="gd-ui">This owner referred another owner</b>: choose the owner referred and the share in basis points (1000 = 10 points of the revenue the management fee is taken from). Set the referred owner&#39;s own fee on their Terms as usual (for example a 40% management fee and $350 a month per car). Every statement of the referrer then has a <b class="gd-ui">Referral share</b> line per referred car; it is paid from CarmaCars&#39; share, never the referred owner&#39;s payout. With <b class="gd-ui">sees the cars</b> on, the referrer finds <b class="gd-ui">Cars you referred</b> in their owner portal: bookings, use and revenue, read only, without the other owner&#39;s details. <b class="gd-ui">End</b> stops the link; shares already earned are still paid.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="owner-money-statement-periods-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Statement periods (release 35)</h2><p class="gd-p">Statements run from the 8th of one month to the 7th of the next, and the payout on the 10th covers them. A rental that crosses the cutoff, or a long weekly or biweekly rental, is paid for the days inside each period, never twice. Each statement lists amounts still uncollected from the renter separately; they are paid on the statement after they are collected.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'settings', 'chapter', 'search-car-pages-landing-pages-and-guides', 'Settings change the public site and the rules of the program at once. Program settings are kept as dated rows, so earlier values stay on record.

## The Settings page

1. Site setup lists what is still missing on the public site, with **Open site settings**.
2. Site settings: contact details, hours, tagline, logo, socials, Google place id and featured cars.
3. Program settings: every timing and policy value.
4. Forms: Blind Spot''s rental agreement for every booking, and the official ServiceOntario PDFs and what goes in each field.
5. Insurers: insurance companies billed for bookings.

![](/guides/img/admin-24-settings-desktop-89b31691.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 900; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings; pins: 1 32.6 33.0, 2 25.8 40.2, 3 77.4 40.2, 4 25.8 73.2, 5 25.8 84.9")

The other tiles: Site content (headings, FAQs, legal text), Fee defaults, Deposit tiers, Kilometre choices, Vehicle classes, Vehicle class rules, Airports and delivery, Protection Plan prices, Card coverage, Reviews, Quo contacts (everyone with a phone number as a contact in Quo: see Texts and calls), Text alerts, Partners (each partner company''s CRM link: see Partners, company cars and rentals added by hand), Email aliases and reply-to, My profile, Staff and roles, Promo codes, Quick replies and Call helper.

**My profile**: the greeting name of this login. To do greets it whole ("Good morning, Abbas and Mahad" on a login the owners share) and the assistant uses it; empty, the first name of the account. Press **Change the greeting name**, type it and save.

## Program settings

1. Buffer between trips (90 minutes): the time held before and after every trip, in every availability and conflict check (requests, offers, date changes, extensions, the calendar). The cleaning block after a trip is this time; Turnaround between trips is the same number. A booking already closer than this is not changed: the calendar rings it.
1. Late fee and extensions (Booking requests and offers): the late fee per started hour (17.5% of the daily rate, at least $25; new bookings and offers only), the extension discounts (no longer applied since release 35: an extension costs the booking''s all-in price a day) and **Approve a renter''s extension at once when nothing needs a person** (on). A car''s own switch is in Fleet, the car, **Edit details**: **Renters extend themselves**.
1. RentalCover (the Protection Plan): whether quotes price the plan once the key is set (on), the markup (on, 20%, no fixed amount), how long a quote is reused, the car value limit ($50,000) and whether a car with no value may have the plan (off).
2. Settings come in groups such as Company, Booking requests and offers, Owner debits and statement emails, Deposits, Delivery, Owners and fleet, and Tolls and damage. Open one to see its fields.
3. First reply target for customer service and sales (minutes), under Booking requests and offers: 5 by default. New booking requests, enquiries, changes renters ask for and renter messages are due that many minutes after they come in; the scorecard and the staff screens use it. What renters are told (Reply wording, in Site settings) is separate.
4. Staff commissions and prices typed by hand: the commission outside Sales (10%, field staff only: customer service, Fleet and Finance earn none), the three Sales tiers and their days (10%, 15% from 50 days, 20% from 100 days, the month''s target), the price floor a day (empty: none) and the discount from the rate sheet that flags a price (20%). The owner confirmed these values in October 2026. The remote Sales values follow: the three remote tiers (5%, 10%, 15%), the touches a month (400), the drop under it (one tier) and its floor (2.5%), the peak hours a week (20), the reply target (15 minutes) and the peak hours (noon to 6 pm, Thursday to Sunday).
5. Staff agreement defaults by function, at the bottom: pay (a month, an hour or commission only), the rate, the schedule (full time, part time or flexible), days a week and hours a day for Customer service, Fleet, Finance and Sales, the values every assistant shares, and the field staff wage. Sales is commission only: no rate and a flexible schedule. Press **Save the defaults**.
6. Live visitors and live chat: recording visits, the signal thresholds, follow-up tasks, the chat and its assistant, and how long visits and chats are kept.
7. Discount games: the same values as Settings, Discount games (the prize table and the games are easier to change there).
8. Deposits: the toll and ticket window after the return (7 days: settling sooner suggests a hold-back), the longest hold-back (30 days after the return), how long before a card hold lapses it is collected (36 hours), and collecting what is owed after the deposit by itself (the card on file, then a pay link, then a Finance task). A deposit is never released by itself.
9. Field jobs and handovers: field jobs made from each confirmed booking (on) and who gets them (the least busy field staff member, or nobody so Fleet assigns), how field staff may take a deposit at the check-in besides a card (e-Transfer and cash), and whether they may release a car whose tracker is not reporting, with a reason (on; you get an urgent task). Field pay: the first day of a pay period (every period is two weeks), the default hourly rate (CA$18.00), whether overtime is paid (off), after how many hours in a week (44) and at what share of the rate (150%), vacation pay added to each statement (off; Ontario 4%) and the longest shift (16 hours).
10. Sign-in by phone: codes by text from the CarmaCars number (on), US numbers (off until the Quo number is registered for US texting, A2P 10DLC), codes per number and per connection an hour, and whether a verified phone confirms an account like a confirmed email. Accepting an offer, signing and paying need a confirmed account; an account made by phone gives its email on the pay page before its first payment.
11. Calendar sync, Turo by email, Booking recovery emails and Site check: how often calendar links are read, the Turo inbound address and who may forward to it, the reminder delays and sending hours, and the site check with the address its alerts go to (rent@carmacars.ca), the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours.
12. Change a value and press **Save**. It is saved as a new row from today; the rows before stay as they were.

