  '<p class="gd-p">Every function adds rentals that come in by phone, at the counter, from Turo, a partner, an insurer or someone you know. The rental is confirmed and on the calendar at once.</p><section class="gd-task" id="add-a-rental-by-hand-add-a-rental" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Add a rental</h2><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>, the <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b> button. Your home address must be in your profile first: until it is, the page asks for it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">At pickup with the renter? Press <b class="gd-ui">Start at pickup</b>: the renter&#39;s name and phone, the car, the kilometres and the fuel, then <b class="gd-ui">Hold the car and finish later</b>. The car is held for 2 hours and you get a task to finish it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing is required to save: the form is saved as a draft as you type (<b class="gd-ui">Save draft</b> saves at once). Unfinished rentals, on Today and on this page, opens a draft where it was left, on any device. Tick Hold the car while I finish to keep the car off the calendar while you type.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the car, the dates and the places. The check shows any clash with another booking or with the cleaning time after a trip. You cannot book over a clash: ask an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The dates decide the case, shown under them. Car already out with the renter? Enter the pickup as when it left: the rental is recorded as on trip, and anything still missing (signature, licence check, coverage proof, deposit) becomes a task. A rental that has already ended is recorded by an Admin.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Find the renter by name, email or phone, or add a new one with their name, email, phone, date of birth and licence. A renter on file shows their licence, home address and the drivers named before (<b class="gd-ui">Add them</b> puts those drivers on the rental), with an expired licence or an old address flagged. Add any other drivers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">The calendar and the price are checked by themselves once the car and the dates are in. The price comes from the rate sheet. You may add the extras, how damage is covered and an allowed promo code.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Quick start: <b class="gd-ui">Phone</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Walk-in</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Turo or another platform</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Insurance replacement</b> sets the usual choices.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">8</span><div class="gd-t">A car tagged Listing not finished can be rented too: it stays off the public site. If it has no rates yet, type the rental charge for the whole rental and the reason. An owner&#39;s car not yet on the fleet insurance policy is added by an Admin only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">9</span><div class="gd-t">Every line of the price can be changed where it stands (customer service and sales, while Program settings allow it): the rental charge for the trip or a rate a day, the young driver fee, the Protection Plan, delivery, each add-on, the kilometres a day; add a fee from the list or a charge of its own. The (i) beside each line says what it is. The rate-sheet price stays on the booking; a price far under it is flagged for an Admin, never refused. Know what the renter paid with tax? Choose After tax (HST included) under Amounts I type and type those amounts (&quot;$270 after tax for the rental, $50 for the Protection Plan&quot;), or type the Total the renter pays (after tax): the rental charge is worked out so the total is exactly that. The total shown is the total saved.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">10</span><div class="gd-t">Any length: past 30 days the monthly rate applies for each 30 days, and the monthly periods are listed. Each later period gets its own agreement, sent to the renter to sign a few days before it starts (Monthly periods on the booking; Send the agreement for the next period now if needed).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">11</span><div class="gd-t">Choose how the rent is paid (e-Transfer or cash received, card on file, payment link, platform payout, insurer billed later; the ways open to you are set by an Admin; paid in parts: Add another payment) and then how the deposit is paid (card hold, cash or e-Transfer with its reference). Before you save sums it all up. The rental agreement is sent to the renter to sign online (never on paper). An insurance replacement with dates not known yet: untick Blocks the car&#39;s calendar and say why. Insurer billed later shows Charges to the insurer: type the rate a day of VLF, LDW, T&amp;LDW, PAP/PEC or Waiver Saver that the insurer authorized (empty: none); each is the rate times the days, plus HST, billed to the insurer.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">12</span><div class="gd-t">Under Who found this client, choose <b class="gd-ui">I sourced this client</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Entered for CarmaCars</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">13</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the rental</b>. The renter gets the confirmation email unless you tick <b class="gd-ui">Do not email the renter</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">14</span><div class="gd-t">A rental you add is credited to you and shows in My sales as a rental you added. If you sourced it, its commission shows there too.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The renter signs the rental agreement in their portal before pickup. With the saved card, nothing is charged when you add the rental: the card is charged when the renter presses Accept and sign. At the counter, they sign on the phone with <b class="gd-ui">Sign now on this device</b>. A payment link keeps the booking waiting for payment.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'my-jobs', 'chapter', 'start-here', 'The portal has four tabs at the bottom of the screen: **Today**, **My shifts**, **My pay** and **Training** (and **Sales** if you asked to do sales too). Today is where the work is.

## Your shift and the clock

1. At the top of **Today**: your shift, and **Clock in**. Press it when you start. The phone shares where you are at that moment only.
2. The bar shows how many of the day''s must-dos are done.
3. When you finish, press **Clock out**. Anything still open is listed: give a reason for each, then press **Clock out with these reasons**. Fleet is told, so someone can cover them.

## One list, in order

The list is built for you from the bookings and the cars:

1. **Your work**: every pickup and return of the day (deliveries and collections too) at its time, and onboarding prep Fleet gave you. Each car and time is one card.
2. **When you have time**: cars to clean (not checked clean for a week), cars needing service or not roadworthy, and cars that need listing photos.
3. Switch to **Tomorrow** to see what is planned so far.

## A card

1. The time, what it is (Pickup, Return, Delivery to the renter), the car and its plate, the renter and the booking.
2. The steps of the card, ticked as they are done: the clean check, the add-ons in the car, the pickup photos and handover.
3. One big button: the next thing to do. **Start the pickup** or **Start the return** opens the job screen, where the clean check and the add-ons come first.
4. **More** has the place with **Open in maps**, the call to the renter, and helping the renter.

The card''s **Prepare: put each in the car, then tick** checklist lists every add-on to put in the car with its quantity. The office sees your ticks as you go.

> Watch out: The pickup cannot be finished until every add-on (a child seat, for example) is ticked as in the car. If the trip must go without it, ask an Admin to override on the job.

## Clean checks

Every car is checked clean before each pickup and after each return: choose **Clean** or **Needs cleaning**, take the photo and press **Save the clean check**. On a cleaning card in spare time, press **Check it clean** the same way.

## Cars needing service, and listing photos

1. On a service card, press **Give an update** (taken in, at the shop, waiting for parts, sorted) and **Send the update to Fleet**.
2. On a photo card, press **Take the listing photos**: the photo shoot opens with the angles the listing is missing.

## Onboarding prep

Fleet gives you the prep of a car joining the fleet on a day you hold a shift. Press **Open the prep**, then each item: upload what it needs (the safety certificate with its date) and press **Mark it done**. When every item is done, the owner''s onboarding checklist updates and Fleet is told.

## The Add button

The red **Add** button at the bottom right of Today:

1. **Money spent**: gas, a wash, parts, parking. The amount, the car, the booking and a photo of the receipt, then **Send to Finance**. Finance approves it and pays you back if you used your own money. No receipt yet: you get a To do until you add it.
2. **Service record**: what was done, where, the odometer, the cost and the invoice photo, then **Record the service**. The car''s maintenance resets, the expense is made on the car, and Fleet and Finance are told.
3. **Photos of a car**: a photo and a note, saved on the car.
4. **A problem with a car**: damage, a warning light, a ticket or lost property (see Report, rentals, referrals and profile).

## Help a renter on the spot

From a card''s **More**, or with **Find the booking** on Help a renter (by booking number, name or phone):

1. **Take a payment** or **Take the deposit hold**: **Show a QR for their phone** (they pay on their own phone), **Text the link**, **Email the link**, or **Use the card reader** when you have it. Never type a card number.
2. The licence: check it in person on the pickup.
3. The agreement: **They sign on my phone**, with their own finger.

> Good to know: Refunds stay with Finance and Admin.

## Check the renter''s licence

The renter''s licence photos and selfie are checked before the handover. You can check them yourself, for a booking on one of your own jobs today or in the next 7 days. Everything you do is recorded with your name and "field staff".

1. My jobs shows **Licences to check** when the licence front, back or selfie of a renter on one of your jobs waits for a decision. The same check is on the job itself, under **Check the licence**.
2. Press **Review the licence**. The images open with the name, date of birth and licence details on the booking.
3. Look at each image and the licence reader''s lines under each driver (Pass or Flag: valid to the return, class, age, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back): no sign of alteration, and the selfie matches the licence photo. A photo you take that is blurry or cut off says so at once: take it again.
4. One is wrong? Open **Reject this one** under it, type the reason the renter reads and press **Reject**. The renter is told why and sends a new one.
5. Then press **Approve all**: everything still waiting is approved at once.

> Tip: The renter''s proof of coverage stays with the office. Meeting the renter at the handover? You can still check the original licence in person from the ready check (see A handover).

## Documents to sign

Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.

1. My jobs shows "You have a document to sign". Press **Read and sign**.
2. Check the key values at the top (your role, wage and start date), then press **Read the PDF** and read it.
3. Sign in a few steps: press **Send the code** and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.
4. Press **Sign**. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.

## Move a car

1. Under Moving a car, press **Start a move**. Choose the Car and Why (for example Reposition).
2. Fill in From and the Odometer (km), then press **Start the move now**.
3. When you arrive, press **End the move**, fill in Now at and the odometer, then press **End the move now**.

## Call and text the renter

**Call** on a card opens the Quo app with the renter''s number, so the call comes from the CarmaCars number; **Text** opens a small window that sends from the CarmaCars number and keeps the text with the booking.

**Cars now** and **Map of your cars** are links at the bottom of Today.

## Start a handover in one tap (release 42)

On a pickup or a return that is not started yet, the job shows **Start the check-in now** (or **Start the check-out now**): one tap acknowledges the job, starts it and opens the one-screen handover. Not with the car yet? Press **Acknowledge** so the office knows you have the job, and start it later.', 'Today', 'Your shift, then one list of the day: each car and time is one card. The Add button, and helping a renter on the spot.',
