  '<p class="gd-p">The portal has four tabs at the bottom of the screen: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, <b class="gd-ui">My shifts</b>, <b class="gd-ui">My pay</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Training</b> (and <b class="gd-ui">Sales</b> if you asked to do sales too). Today is where the work is.</p><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-your-shift-and-the-clock" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your shift and the clock</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">At the top of <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>: your shift, and <b class="gd-ui">Clock in</b>. Press it when you start. The phone shares where you are at that moment only.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The bar shows how many of the day&#39;s must-dos are done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When you finish, press <b class="gd-ui">Clock out</b>. Anything still open is listed: give a reason for each, then press <b class="gd-ui">Clock out with these reasons</b>. Fleet is told, so someone can cover them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-one-list-in-order" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One list, in order</h2><p class="gd-p">The list is built for you from the bookings and the cars:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Your work</b>: every pickup and return of the day (deliveries and collections too) at its time, and onboarding prep Fleet gave you. Each car and time is one card.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">When you have time</b>: cars to clean (not checked clean for a week), cars needing service or not roadworthy, and cars that need listing photos.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Switch to <b class="gd-ui">Tomorrow</b> to see what is planned so far.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-missing-check-in-and-check-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Missing check-in and check-out</h2><p class="gd-p">On <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>: past rentals you handled or were given that are missing their photos and readings, closed bookings and pickups recorded with the details later included.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add the photos and readings</b> on one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Add the odometer, the fuel and the damage photos, then save. Fleet can give you more of them.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-a-card" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A card</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The time, what it is (Pickup, Return, Delivery to the renter), the car and its plate, the renter and the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The steps of the card, ticked as they are done: the clean check, the add-ons in the car, the pickup photos and handover.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">One big button: the next thing to do. <b class="gd-ui">Start the pickup</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Start the return</b> opens the job screen, where the clean check and the add-ons come first.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">More</b> has the place with <b class="gd-ui">Open in maps</b>, the call to the renter, and helping the renter.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">The card&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">Prepare: put each in the car, then tick</b> checklist lists every add-on to put in the car with its quantity. The office sees your ticks as you go.</p><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>The pickup cannot be finished until every add-on (a child seat, for example) is ticked as in the car. If the trip must go without it, ask an Admin to override on the job.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-clean-checks" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Clean checks</h2><p class="gd-p">Every car is checked clean before each pickup and after each return: choose <b class="gd-ui">Clean</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Needs cleaning</b>, take the photo and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the clean check</b>. On a cleaning card in spare time, press <b class="gd-ui">Check it clean</b> the same way.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-cars-needing-service-and-listing-photos" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Cars needing service, and listing photos</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">On a service card, press <b class="gd-ui">Give an update</b> (taken in, at the shop, waiting for parts, sorted) and <b class="gd-ui">Send the update to Fleet</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">On a photo card, press <b class="gd-ui">Take the listing photos</b>: the photo shoot opens with the angles the listing is missing.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-onboarding-prep" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Onboarding prep</h2><p class="gd-p">Fleet gives you the prep of a car joining the fleet on a day you hold a shift. Press <b class="gd-ui">Open the prep</b>, then each item: upload what it needs (the safety certificate with its date) and press <b class="gd-ui">Mark it done</b>. When every item is done, the owner&#39;s onboarding checklist updates and Fleet is told.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-the-add-button" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Add button</h2><p class="gd-p">The red <b class="gd-ui">Add</b> button at the bottom right of Today:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money spent</b>: gas, a wash, parts, parking. The amount, the car, the booking and a photo of the receipt, then <b class="gd-ui">Send to Finance</b>. Finance approves it and pays you back if you used your own money. No receipt yet: you get a To do until you add it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Service record</b>: what was done, where, the odometer, the cost and the invoice photo, then <b class="gd-ui">Record the service</b>. The car&#39;s maintenance resets, the expense is made on the car, and Fleet and Finance are told.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Photos of a car</b>: a photo and a note, saved on the car.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">A problem with a car</b>: damage, a warning light, a ticket or lost property (see Report, rentals, referrals and profile).</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-help-a-renter-on-the-spot" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Help a renter on the spot</h2><p class="gd-p">From a card&#39;s <b class="gd-ui">More</b>, or with <b class="gd-ui">Find the booking</b> on Help a renter (by booking number, name or phone):</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Take a payment</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Take the deposit hold</b>: <b class="gd-ui">Show a QR for their phone</b> (they pay on their own phone), <b class="gd-ui">Text the link</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Email the link</b>, or <b class="gd-ui">Use the card reader</b> when you have it. Never type a card number.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The licence: check it in person on the pickup.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The agreement: <b class="gd-ui">They sign on my phone</b>, with their own finger.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Refunds stay with Finance and Admin.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-check-the-renter-s-licence" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Check the renter&#39;s licence</h2><p class="gd-p">The renter&#39;s licence photos and selfie are checked before the handover. You can check them yourself, for a booking on one of your own jobs today or in the next 7 days. Everything you do is recorded with your name and &quot;field staff&quot;.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">My jobs shows <b class="gd-ui">Licences to check</b> when the licence front, back or selfie of a renter on one of your jobs waits for a decision. The same check is on the job itself, under <b class="gd-ui">Check the licence</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Review the licence</b>. The images open with the name, date of birth and licence details on the booking.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Look at each image and the licence reader&#39;s lines under each driver (Pass or Flag: valid to the return, class, age, name and date of birth, the Ontario number, front and back): no sign of alteration, and the selfie matches the licence photo. A photo you take that is blurry or cut off says so at once: take it again.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">One is wrong? Open <b class="gd-ui">Reject this one</b> under it, type the reason the renter reads and press <b class="gd-ui">Reject</b>. The renter is told why and sends a new one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Approve all</b>: everything still waiting is approved at once.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>The renter&#39;s proof of coverage stays with the office. Meeting the renter at the handover? You can still check the original licence in person from the ready check (see A handover).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-documents-to-sign" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Documents to sign</h2><p class="gd-p">Your staff agreement, when CarmaCars sends it.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">My jobs shows &quot;You have a document to sign&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Read and sign</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the key values at the top (your role, wage and start date), then press <b class="gd-ui">Read the PDF</b> and read it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Sign in a few steps: press <b class="gd-ui">Send the code</b> and type the 6-digit code from your phone or email, tick that you read it, draw your initials beside the key terms (confidentiality, the rules on money, keys and cars, ending the agreement), tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b>. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, stays on the same page.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-move-a-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Move a car</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Moving a car, press <b class="gd-ui">Start a move</b>. Choose the Car and Why (for example Reposition).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Fill in From and the Odometer (km), then press <b class="gd-ui">Start the move now</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">When you arrive, press <b class="gd-ui">End the move</b>, fill in Now at and the odometer, then press <b class="gd-ui">End the move now</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-call-and-text-the-renter" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Call and text the renter</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Call</b> on a card opens the Quo app with the renter&#39;s number, so the call comes from the CarmaCars number; <b class="gd-ui">Text</b> opens a small window that sends from the CarmaCars number and keeps the text with the booking.</p><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars now</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Map of your cars</b> are links at the bottom of Today.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-jobs-start-a-handover-in-one-tap-release-42" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Start a handover in one tap (release 42)</h2><p class="gd-p">On a pickup or a return that is not started yet, the job shows <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-in now</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Start the check-out now</b>): one tap acknowledges the job, starts it and opens the one-screen handover. Not with the car yet? Press <b class="gd-ui">Acknowledge</b> so the office knows you have the job, and start it later.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('field', 'my-hours-and-pay', 'chapter', 'photo-shoots', 'Jobs are put on shifts: claim a shift and its jobs are yours. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved.

## My shifts

1. **Free to claim**: shifts someone gave up (first to claim takes it) and open shifts. Each shows the jobs already on it, for example "On it: 3 pickups, 1 return, 2 cleans". Press **Claim this shift**: its jobs are yours on **Today** and here. You can claim once you passed the academy.
2. **Coming up**: your shifts, each with the shift''s jobs and the work planned for you. It updates as bookings come in. Sharing a shift? Its jobs are split between you, least busy first; the others'' show on **Today** under **Also on your shift**, and **Take it** takes one.
3. Cannot work one? Press **Give this shift up** and say why. It is offered at once to everyone free then, and its jobs go with it to whoever claims it. Under 24 hours before the start it is marked late on your record.
4. **Swap with someone**: choose their shift and press **Ask for the swap**. They press **Accept the swap** or **Decline**. Each of you takes the other shift''s jobs.
5. **Past shifts**: each day with your hours, the jobs, the photos and the money you spent.
6. **Money you spent**: each one with where it stands. No receipt yet? Take the photo and press **Add the receipt**.

## Clock in and out

Clock in and out on **Today**, with your shift. Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.

## Pay details

Before your first pay, **My pay** asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press **Save my pay details**. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.

## Your pay and your pay statements

A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.

1. The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.
2. An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.
3. Under Pay statements on **My pay**, press **PDF** for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.

> Tip: A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.

## Where you clock in and out

The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.

## Availability, standing shifts and the minimum (release 35)

1. Set when you can work (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday, plus a note) on Welcome; change it later on My shifts or Profile.
2. My shifts opens as a week calendar: tap a shift to claim it. The cards are on the List tab.
3. A standing weekly shift, such as every Saturday 10 to 6, claims each matching published shift by itself up to two weeks ahead. Drop one date (the give-up rules apply) or end it.
4. Hold at least the minimum (2 shifts in 7 days by default). Under it, you get a daily reminder and a To do.
5. Pay stubs come every two weeks under My pay, with a PDF and an email once paid.', 'My shifts and My pay', 'Claim, give up and swap shifts, what you did on each, your hours, pay statements and pay details.',
  'Jobs are put on shifts: claim a shift and its jobs are yours. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved.

## My shifts

Shifts are published by themselves, up to 14 days ahead: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day, and a shift of its own for a handover or return no shift covers. Fleet may add or cancel shifts too.

1. **Free to claim**: shifts someone gave up (first to claim takes it) and open shifts. Each shows the jobs already on it, for example "On it: 3 pickups, 1 return, 2 cleans". Press **Claim this shift**: its jobs are yours on **Today** and here. You can claim once you passed the academy.
2. **Coming up**: your shifts, each with the shift''s jobs and the work planned for you. It updates as bookings come in. Sharing a shift? Its jobs are split between you, least busy first; the others'' show on **Today** under **Also on your shift**, and **Take it** takes one.
3. Cannot work one? Press **Give this shift up** and say why. It is offered at once to everyone free then, and its jobs go with it to whoever claims it. Under 24 hours before the start it is marked late on your record.
4. **Swap with someone**: choose their shift and press **Ask for the swap**. They press **Accept the swap** or **Decline**. Each of you takes the other shift''s jobs.
5. **Past shifts**: each day with your hours, the jobs, the photos and the money you spent.
6. **Money you spent**: each one with where it stands. No receipt yet? Take the photo and press **Add the receipt**.

## Clock in and out

Clock in and out on **Today**, with your shift. Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.

## Pay details

Before your first pay, **My pay** asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press **Save my pay details**. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.

## Your pay and your pay statements

A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.

1. The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.
2. An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.
3. Under Pay statements on **My pay**, press **PDF** for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.

> Tip: A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.

## Where you clock in and out

The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.

## Availability, standing shifts and the minimum (release 35)

1. Set when you can work (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday, plus a note) on Welcome; change it later on My shifts or Profile.
2. My shifts opens as a week calendar: tap a shift to claim it. The cards are on the List tab.
3. A standing weekly shift, such as every Saturday 10 to 6, claims each matching published shift by itself up to two weeks ahead. Drop one date (the give-up rules apply) or end it.
4. Hold at least the minimum (2 shifts in 7 days by default). Under it, you get a daily reminder and a To do.
5. Pay stubs come every two weeks under My pay, with a PDF and an email once paid.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Jobs are put on shifts: claim a shift and its jobs are yours. Your hours are paid every two weeks at your hourly rate (CA$18.00 an hour unless your agreement says another rate), with the commissions an Admin has approved.</p><section class="gd-task" id="my-hours-and-pay-my-shifts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">My shifts</h2><p class="gd-p">Shifts are published by themselves, up to 14 days ahead: one shift of 10:00 to 17:00 every second day, and a shift of its own for a handover or return no shift covers. Fleet may add or cancel shifts too.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Free to claim</b>: shifts someone gave up (first to claim takes it) and open shifts. Each shows the jobs already on it, for example &quot;On it: 3 pickups, 1 return, 2 cleans&quot;. Press <b class="gd-ui">Claim this shift</b>: its jobs are yours on <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> and here. You can claim once you passed the academy.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Coming up</b>: your shifts, each with the shift&#39;s jobs and the work planned for you. It updates as bookings come in. Sharing a shift? Its jobs are split between you, least busy first; the others&#39; show on <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> under <b class="gd-ui">Also on your shift</b>, and <b class="gd-ui">Take it</b> takes one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Cannot work one? Press <b class="gd-ui">Give this shift up</b> and say why. It is offered at once to everyone free then, and its jobs go with it to whoever claims it. Under 24 hours before the start it is marked late on your record.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Swap with someone</b>: choose their shift and press <b class="gd-ui">Ask for the swap</b>. They press <b class="gd-ui">Accept the swap</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Decline</b>. Each of you takes the other shift&#39;s jobs.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Past shifts</b>: each day with your hours, the jobs, the photos and the money you spent.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Money you spent</b>: each one with where it stands. No receipt yet? Take the photo and press <b class="gd-ui">Add the receipt</b>.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-hours-and-pay-clock-in-and-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Clock in and out</h2><p class="gd-p">Clock in and out on <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, with your shift. Forgot to clock out, or a time is wrong? Tell Fleet: they fix it, say why, and the change is written in a log.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-hours-and-pay-pay-details" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Pay details</h2><p class="gd-p">Before your first pay, <b class="gd-ui">My pay</b> asks for your pay details: your full legal name, email, phone, SIN and a photo of a void cheque. Press <b class="gd-ui">Save my pay details</b>. Your SIN is kept encrypted: only Finance and Admin can see it, every look is recorded, and you see only its last 3 digits. How you are paid (bank, e-Transfer) is just below.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-hours-and-pay-your-pay-and-your-pay-statements" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Your pay and your pay statements</h2><p class="gd-p">A pay period is two weeks, Sunday to Saturday. An Admin runs the pay after it ends.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The pay is your hours times your hourly rate, plus the commissions and referral fees an Admin approved by the end of the period (see Commissions). Overtime and vacation pay are added only if CarmaCars has switched them on.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An Admin approves the pay run, pays you (by e-Transfer, bank transfer or cash) and records it. You get an email with the amount and how you were paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under Pay statements on <b class="gd-ui">My pay</b>, press <b class="gd-ui">PDF</b> for the statement of a period: your hours day by day, the amounts, the commissions in it and how it was paid.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>A pay statement shows no income tax, CPP or EI. They are not worked out in the portal: for your tax slips, ask CarmaCars or your accountant.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-hours-and-pay-where-you-clock-in-and-out" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Where you clock in and out</h2><p class="gd-p">The phone asks for your location once when you clock in and once when you clock out, and never in between. Allow it. If it is off, or you are more than 500 m from the lot, you can still clock in or out: write why in the box that appears, and Fleet sees it.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="my-hours-and-pay-availability-standing-shifts-and-the-minimum-release-35" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Availability, standing shifts and the minimum (release 35)</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Set when you can work (mornings, afternoons and evenings for each weekday, plus a note) on Welcome; change it later on My shifts or Profile.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">My shifts opens as a week calendar: tap a shift to claim it. The cards are on the List tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A standing weekly shift, such as every Saturday 10 to 6, claims each matching published shift by itself up to two weeks ahead. Drop one date (the give-up rules apply) or end it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Hold at least the minimum (2 shifts in 7 days by default). Under it, you get a daily reminder and a To do.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Pay stubs come every two weeks under My pay, with a PDF and an email once paid.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
-- GUIDES 2865 END
